00:13:07,260 --> 00:13:08,489
(The theme is the new generation.)

281
00:13:08,490 --> 00:13:09,830
(Separating the space on stage by using the objects)

282
00:13:10,790 --> 00:13:12,660
These 30 people must be different.

283
00:13:13,030 --> 00:13:14,369
It's like they're in a contest.

284
00:13:14,370 --> 00:13:15,470
I can't wait.

285
00:13:17,130 --> 00:13:18,700
Hash's so dogged right now.

286
00:13:20,070 --> 00:13:21,340
(Performance by Team Hash)

287
00:13:28,680 --> 00:13:29,849
(Awesome)

288
00:13:29,850 --> 00:13:30,919
(Cheering)

289
00:13:30,920 --> 00:13:32,180
(Focused)

290
00:13:36,150 --> 00:13:37,150
(Eyes focused)

291
00:13:37,151 --> 00:13:38,160
(Focused)

292
00:13:38,290 --> 00:13:39,390
(Shaking his head)

293
00:13:39,760 --> 00:13:41,030
I'm getting goosebumps.

294
00:13:41,260 --> 00:13:42,760
I didn't see that coming.

295
00:13:45,760 --> 00:13:46,799
(Shocked)

296
00:13:46,800 --> 00:13:48,100
(Surprised)

297
00:13:59,680 --> 00:14:00,710
(Cheering)

298
00:14:00,980 --> 00:14:02,280
Hash, let's go!

299
00:14:05,450 --> 00:14:06,620
Hash, let's go!

300
00:14:13,960 --> 00:14:15,290
That's her style.

301
00:14:15,960 --> 00:14:16,960
(Surprised)

302
00:14:20,330 --> 00:14:21,330
x

303
00:14:21,330 --> 00:14:22,330
(That's legendary.)

304
00:14:25,870 --> 00:14:26,870
(Surprised)

305
00:14:27,810 --> 00:14:28,810
Good job.

306
00:14:29,270 --> 00:14:30,980
The table's going up.

307
00:14:31,080 --> 00:14:32,080
(Immersed)

308
00:14:32,240 --> 00:14:34,410
How are they keeping the heavy table up?

309
00:14:37,980 --> 00:14:39,280
Hey.

310
00:14:39,420 --> 00:14:41,350
So that's how it goes.

311
00:14:43,250 --> 00:14:44,460
(Fascinated)

312
00:14:53,730 --> 00:14:54,730
(Loving it)

313
00:14:54,730 --> 00:14:55,730
(Thrilled)

314
00:14:58,200 --> 00:15:00,840
Good job. That's awesome!

315
00:15:02,710 --> 00:15:03,870
(Please.)

316
00:15:07,410 --> 00:15:08,509
(She nailed it.)

317
00:15:08,510 --> 00:15:09,980
I like that part.

318
00:15:14,180 --> 00:15:15,550
(Completely immersed)

319
00:15:23,060 --> 00:15:24,960
(Shocked)

320
00:15:25,160 --> 00:15:26,860
The judges might like Hash's performance.

321
00:15:39,680 --> 00:15:40,740
That's wonderful.

322
00:15:42,780 --> 00:15:44,579
(Team Hash's dancers: Lee Ha Yeon, Lee Hyun Seung, Oh Ye Rin)

323
00:15:44,580 --> 00:15:45,679
(Hong Yun Jee, Song Min Chae, Kim Dong Hee, Oh Se Eun, Lee Su Jin)

324
00:15:45,680 --> 00:15:46,820
(Lee Yun Ah, Choi Seo Bin, Lim Hyo Su, Yun Dong Hyun)

325
00:15:47,350 --> 00:15:49,190
(Applauding)

326
00:15:51,090 --> 00:15:53,360
(Oh, my gosh.)

327
00:15:53,890 --> 00:15:55,029
Don't cry.

328
00:15:55,030 --> 00:15:56,259
(Already addicted)

329
00:15:56,260 --> 00:15:58,060
(In shock)

330
00:15:58,230 --> 00:15:59,359
(In love)

331
00:15:59,360 --> 00:16:00,800
Gosh.

332
00:16:00,960 --> 00:16:03,199
It's a matter of taking a risk...

333
00:16:03,200 --> 00:16:05,669
or staying safe...

334
00:16:05,670 --> 00:16:07,869
in 24 hours.

335
00:16:07,870 --> 00:16:11,080
I think that determines it.

336
00:16:11,140 --> 00:16:14,109
Yes. Reason, story, emotion.

337
00:16:14,110 --> 00:16:16,109
Cleanliness. So...

338
00:16:16,110 --> 00:16:17,110
I feel like...

339
00:16:17,111 --> 00:16:18,649
- we're on the same page?
- Yes.

340
00:16:18,650 --> 00:16:21,720
I will announce the choreographer who got eliminated first.

341
00:16:22,090 --> 00:16:23,389
Oh, no.

342
00:16:23,390 --> 00:16:24,520
Oh, my gosh.

343
00:16:24,790 --> 00:16:26,859
Today, we fight judges...

344
00:16:26,860 --> 00:16:29,289
didn't evaluate on who's the better choreographer,

345
00:16:29,290 --> 00:16:32,999
but who was more persuasive...

346
00:16:33,000 --> 00:16:34,900
in terms of proving their directing skills.

347
00:16:35,000 --> 00:16:36,069
As a result,

348
00:16:36,070 --> 00:16:38,700
the first choreographer to be eliminated is...

349
00:16:39,800 --> 00:16:43,010
Renan.

350
00:16:43,810 --> 00:16:46,940
(The first eliminated choreographer is Renan.)

351
00:16:47,210 --> 00:16:48,579
Some cases, the story is stronger than the prop.

352
00:16:48,580 --> 00:16:50,409
Then the prop was stronger than the story.

353
00:16:50,410 --> 00:16:52,419
But I feel like in her case,

354
00:16:52,420 --> 00:16:54,849
the story and the prop were a little weak.

355
00:16:54,850 --> 00:16:57,859
And in terms of order, I'd probably put...

356
00:16:57,860 --> 00:16:59,259
Renan last.

357
00:16:59,260 --> 00:17:00,290
Yes.

358
00:17:04,290 --> 00:17:05,930
JEONG MIN JUN.

359
00:17:06,260 --> 00:17:07,900
Hash.

360
00:17:08,800 --> 00:17:12,700
I will announce the choreographer who survived.

361
00:17:12,970 --> 00:17:14,769
Honey J.

362
00:17:14,770 --> 00:17:15,970
Please announce it.

363
00:17:16,270 --> 00:17:17,939
We fight judges...

364
00:17:17,940 --> 00:17:20,179
evaluated based on...

365
00:17:20,180 --> 00:17:22,749
the quality of the work, the use of the object,

366
00:17:22,750 --> 00:17:25,720
and how persuasive the concept was.

367
00:17:26,020 --> 00:17:27,080
As a result,

368
00:17:27,180 --> 00:17:29,090
only one choreographer...

369
00:17:29,290 --> 00:17:30,889
demonstrated directing skills...

370
00:17:30,890 --> 00:17:33,360
convincingly.

371
00:17:33,660 --> 00:17:37,660
The survivor who will join in the next mission is...

372
00:17:38,860 --> 00:17:40,630
I think I'm going to win.

373
00:17:41,870 --> 00:17:43,430
I want to survive.

374
00:17:44,500 --> 00:17:47,300
The survivor who will join in the next mission is...

375
00:17:47,740 --> 00:17:49,340
(Last Stage: 24H)

376
00:17:50,540 --> 00:17:53,280
JEONG MIN JUN.

377
00:17:53,810 --> 00:17:55,079
Congratulations.

378
00:17:55,080 --> 00:17:56,350
(JEONG MIN JUN survives.)

379
00:17:56,880 --> 00:17:59,920
(Hash got eliminated.)

380
00:18:01,890 --> 00:18:04,220
(The eliminated choreographer, Hash)

381
00:18:04,620 --> 00:18:06,019
Hash was good,

382
00:18:06,020 --> 00:18:08,359
but it wasn't distinctive enough.

383
00:18:08,360 --> 00:18:11,029
I think what if Hash just used the wall...

384
00:18:11,030 --> 00:18:12,559
or the table for a reason,

385
00:18:12,560 --> 00:18:15,329
like what if that wall was stopping her from something...

386
00:18:15,330 --> 00:18:17,699
I think it just was a wall for no reason.

387
00:18:17,700 --> 00:18:19,439
- MIN JUN had everything.
- That's right.

388
00:18:19,440 --> 00:18:21,609
Reason, story, emotion.

389
00:18:21,610 --> 00:18:22,869
Quality.

390
00:18:22,870 --> 00:18:25,680
He hit all the marks, so...

391
00:18:27,640 --> 00:18:28,749
MIN JUN.

392
00:18:28,750 --> 00:18:29,910
Congratulations.

393
00:18:30,280 --> 00:18:31,620
Well done.

394
00:18:32,020 --> 00:18:33,250
Good job.

395
00:18:33,720 --> 00:18:36,490
I'm not sure whether I should clap or not.

396
00:18:36,620 --> 00:18:41,759
(You can watch their full video on "The CHOOM" and "Mnet Plus.")

397
00:18:41,760 --> 00:18:43,530
(The night after the Last Stage)

398
00:18:45,530 --> 00:18:47,870
(Feeling heavy-hearted about leave)

399
00:18:48,330 --> 00:18:50,970
(Renan gets ready to leave.)

400
00:18:51,700 --> 00:18:53,639
- Renan.
- Hey.

401
00:18:53,640 --> 00:18:55,170
(The choreographers are here to say goodbye.)

402
00:18:56,040 --> 00:18:57,509
Renan.

403
00:18:57,510 --> 00:18:58,740
Sit down.

404
00:18:59,610 --> 00:19:01,210
Let's talk. It's been a while.

405
00:19:02,080 --> 00:19:03,210
I'm scared.

406
00:19:04,210 --> 00:19:05,649
You did well.

407
00:19:05,650 --> 00:19:07,450
- No.
- Well done.

408
00:19:07,580 --> 00:19:09,090
You all did well.

409
00:19:10,250 --> 00:19:13,360
You can be less hard on yourself.

410
00:19:14,320 --> 00:19:16,629
You're already talented enough.

411
00:19:16,630 --> 00:19:18,230
Believe in yourself.

412
00:19:18,600 --> 00:19:20,059
I could've just had fun,

413
00:19:20,060 --> 00:19:22,930
but I couldn't do that just like her.

414
00:19:24,330 --> 00:19:26,070
(The light in Renan's room went off every time she had a hard time.)

415
00:19:26,570 --> 00:19:29,970
You were alone in the dark.

416
00:19:30,070 --> 00:19:31,539
Whenever I turned my head,

417
00:19:31,540 --> 00:19:33,180
I could see you pulled your hat down to your lips.

418
00:19:33,280 --> 00:19:35,450
That's what I saw all the time.

419
00:19:35,550 --> 00:19:36,849
When things don't go well,

420
00:19:36,850 --> 00:19:40,250
I can't forgive myself.

421
00:19:40,580 --> 00:19:41,850
If something doesn't work out,

422
00:19:41,950 --> 00:19:43,520
I blame myself.

423
00:19:43,620 --> 00:19:46,019
You don't have to be so hard on yourself.

424
00:19:46,020 --> 00:19:47,489
- Just enjoy it.
- Relax.

425
00:19:47,490 --> 00:19:50,030
Just have fun. That's all you need to do.

426
00:19:51,800 --> 00:19:52,830
How did you...

427
00:19:53,600 --> 00:19:55,130
beat me all three times?

428
00:19:56,670 --> 00:19:57,670
Seriously.

429
00:20:00,500 --> 00:20:02,439
- I almost cried.
- Why?

430
00:20:02,440 --> 00:20:05,280
They asked me, "How would you feel to see Hash leave?"

431
00:20:05,510 --> 00:20:07,079
I said I'd do nothing but cry.

432
00:20:07,080 --> 00:20:09,009
Stop making me cry.

433
00:20:09,010 --> 00:20:10,750
I don't want to cry anymore.

434
00:20:11,820 --> 00:20:14,150
I'm crying again.

435
00:20:14,550 --> 00:20:15,619
Why am I crying?

436
00:20:15,620 --> 00:20:18,389
I'm the one who's leaving.

437
00:20:18,390 --> 00:20:19,790
Why am I crying?

438
00:20:21,020 --> 00:20:22,760
You're on your own now.

439
00:20:22,860 --> 00:20:23,889
You have to show them.

440
00:20:23,890 --> 00:20:25,129
I couldn't do it.

441
00:20:25,130 --> 00:20:27,300
I'll prove myself in the competition scene.

442
00:20:27,660 --> 00:20:29,399
You have to prove yourself here.

443
00:20:29,400 --> 00:20:30,500
(A request from the one who's leaving)

444
00:20:31,130 --> 00:20:33,040
(A heaviness of the one who has to say goodbye)

445
00:20:33,340 --> 00:20:35,740
You're good. I know you are.

446
00:20:36,070 --> 00:20:38,710
I know it from being your rival.

447
00:20:39,010 --> 00:20:41,680
You're darn strong.

448
00:20:42,480 --> 00:20:43,650
How are you so strong?

449
00:20:45,720 --> 00:20:48,950
I learned so much through Street World Fighter.

450
00:20:49,050 --> 00:20:51,919
I got to try work, missions, and experience...

451
00:20:51,920 --> 00:20:53,620
that I haven't had before.

452
00:20:54,120 --> 00:20:56,359
Most importantly, I got to learn a lot...

453
00:20:56,360 --> 00:20:58,130
from other directors.

454
00:20:59,260 --> 00:21:01,399
"That can be a way to create a choreography."

455
00:21:01,400 --> 00:21:03,369
"Gosh, that's another perspective to see it."

456
00:21:03,370 --> 00:21:06,939
This show gave me a chance...

457
00:21:06,940 --> 00:21:09,540
to broaden my perspective.

458
00:21:10,540 --> 00:21:13,310
I'm leaving the show now.

459
00:21:13,410 --> 00:21:15,979
Everything I gained and learned here...

460
00:21:15,980 --> 00:21:17,580
will reflect in my growth forward.

461
00:21:17,680 --> 00:21:19,319
I'll continue to work hard...

462
00:21:19,320 --> 00:21:21,050
and prove myself.

463
00:21:22,050 --> 00:21:24,660
Please look forward to my improvement.

464
00:21:25,660 --> 00:21:27,690
(Hash leaves the Director's Room after leaving her last message.)

465
00:21:28,860 --> 00:21:30,489
Through this show,

466
00:21:30,490 --> 00:21:33,560
I've become a better choreographer and a better director.

467
00:21:33,800 --> 00:21:36,630
Please look forward to my highlights.

468
00:21:37,030 --> 00:21:39,700
I am Director Renan.

469
00:21:40,740 --> 00:21:42,740
(Renan leaves the Director's Room where she laughed and cried.)

470
00:21:44,540 --> 00:21:46,380
(New morning arrives after two directors leave.)

471
00:21:46,540 --> 00:21:48,880
I have sad news as soon as I'm here.

472
00:21:49,110 --> 00:21:51,950
This is sad.

473
00:21:52,580 --> 00:21:54,180
She wrote a message for everyone.

474
00:21:54,580 --> 00:21:55,820
It's touching.

475
00:21:55,950 --> 00:21:57,889
"Thank you for leading us..."

476
00:21:57,890 --> 00:22:00,089
"during the Director's Cut."

477
00:22:00,090 --> 00:22:01,959
"Since the first signature choreography match,"

478
00:22:01,960 --> 00:22:03,889
"you were the only one who took my side,"

479
00:22:03,890 --> 00:22:05,929
"and you've always been very supportive."

480
00:22:05,930 --> 00:22:08,199
I'm glad this experience left them...

481
00:22:08,200 --> 00:22:09,300
good memories.

482
00:22:09,730 --> 00:22:11,570
This is why I don't get close to people.

483
00:22:11,700 --> 00:22:13,140
We finally became close,

484
00:22:13,540 --> 00:22:15,210
but their rooms are closed.

485
00:22:15,310 --> 00:22:16,640
And the lights are off.

486
00:22:17,410 --> 00:22:19,010
This is heartbreaking.

487
00:22:19,480 --> 00:22:20,580
I mean it.

488
00:22:21,480 --> 00:22:24,110
I'll cherish this letter.

489
00:22:25,580 --> 00:22:28,520
Two people are gone out of ten.

490
00:22:29,090 --> 00:22:31,120
It feels really empty.

491
00:22:31,220 --> 00:22:32,960
(2 Director's Rooms are shut.)

492
00:22:33,060 --> 00:22:35,290
(And one Director's Room is still empty.)

493
00:22:36,030 --> 00:22:37,260
I'm back.

494
00:22:38,060 --> 00:22:41,130
How do I feel? I did everything I could to come back.

495
00:22:46,200 --> 00:22:47,699
It's a lot of pressure.

496
00:22:47,700 --> 00:22:50,070
Renan on one shoulder and Hash on the other.

497
00:22:51,170 --> 00:22:52,840
(Screaming)

498
00:22:55,780 --> 00:22:57,650
I bet other people were afraid...

499
00:22:58,080 --> 00:22:59,280
after seeing my performance.

500
00:22:59,880 --> 00:23:01,850
"He's dangerous."

501
00:23:02,320 --> 00:23:04,450
I bet that's how other people felt.

502
00:23:05,860 --> 00:23:07,920
Now that I'm back,

503
00:23:08,530 --> 00:23:11,360
I'll shock the other choreographers...

504
00:23:11,560 --> 00:23:14,030
into thinking that I'm a strong candidate to win.

505
00:23:15,270 --> 00:23:21,370
("Royalty" by Yoon Mi Rae and Tiger JK)

506
00:24:40,450 --> 00:24:42,520
(K-pop Solo Artist Direct Mission)

507
00:24:42,820 --> 00:24:43,950
(Nice!)

508
00:24:44,050 --> 00:24:45,890
(It's time to do my job.)

509
00:24:46,260 --> 00:24:47,360
(2:2 Duet Match)

510
00:24:47,820 --> 00:24:48,860
(BAILEY match)

511
00:24:50,290 --> 00:24:51,390
(TAEYONG match)

512
00:24:52,800 --> 00:24:54,730
(All 4 choreographers from the losing team...)

513
00:24:54,830 --> 00:24:56,670
(will head straight to the Last Stage: 24H.)

514
00:24:56,770 --> 00:24:57,869
(Screaming)

515
00:24:57,870 --> 00:24:59,800
(If I lose, it's the Last Stage.)

516
00:24:59,900 --> 00:25:02,170
(I'm going to send everyone to the Last Stage.)

517
00:25:02,270 --> 00:25:03,270
(I must win no matter what.)

518
00:25:03,270 --> 00:25:04,270
I need to get everyone involved.

519
00:25:04,271 --> 00:25:05,339
(BAILEY match)

520
00:25:05,340 --> 00:25:07,080
(No one's willing to yield.)

521
00:25:07,180 --> 00:25:08,180
(JEONG MIN JUN and Kasper's choreography shoot)

522
00:25:08,181 --> 00:25:09,650
(JEONG MIN JUN has trouble directing.)

523
00:25:09,750 --> 00:25:11,149
(It's frustrating, to be honest.)

524
00:25:11,150 --> 00:25:12,949
(There is not a single thing that I like so far.)

525
00:25:12,950 --> 00:25:13,950
(What do you want then?)

526
00:25:13,951 --> 00:25:15,519
(Who will TAEYONG...)

527
00:25:15,520 --> 00:25:16,520
(Who will BAILEY...)

528
00:25:16,521 --> 00:25:20,990
(Which team will the solo artist choose?)

529
00:25:24,900 --> 00:25:26,199
- Hello.
- Hello.

530
00:25:26,200 --> 00:25:27,500
Hello.

531
00:25:28,600 --> 00:25:32,340
(8 choreographers gather in the Directors' Lab.)

532
00:25:33,270 --> 00:25:34,600
Why is everyone calm?

533
00:25:35,370 --> 00:25:36,710
Perhaps because two people are gone?

534
00:25:37,010 --> 00:25:40,410
All I'm thinking about is avoiding the Last Stage.

535
00:25:41,010 --> 00:25:42,550
Absolutely.

536
00:25:42,780 --> 00:25:46,050
There will be a new mission today, right?

537
00:25:46,220 --> 00:25:47,419
What are we doing today?

538
00:25:47,420 --> 00:25:48,820
Tell us already.

539
00:25:49,020 --> 00:25:52,160
Film, stage... K-pop?

540
00:25:52,790 --> 00:25:53,790
Is it a mega mission?

541
00:25:53,890 --> 00:25:55,089
That's absurd.

542
00:25:55,090 --> 00:25:56,359
Who said no?

543
00:25:56,360 --> 00:25:57,660
(Diverse speculations rise along with the memories.)

544
00:25:57,830 --> 00:25:59,999
I don't even know what we're doing next.

545
00:26:00,000 --> 00:26:01,059
(What's going to happen today?)

546
00:26:01,060 --> 00:26:04,269
What's happening? Tell me already.

547
00:26:04,270 --> 00:26:06,600
Oh, I don't know. I'm just going to lie down.

548
00:26:07,600 --> 00:26:09,069
The competition that started with ten people...

549
00:26:09,070 --> 00:26:10,310
(Startled)

550
00:26:11,110 --> 00:26:12,540
- The competition...
- My goodness.

551
00:26:12,640 --> 00:26:14,440
The competition that started with ten people...

552
00:26:14,640 --> 00:26:17,109
has now narrowed down to eight choreographers...

553
00:26:17,110 --> 00:26:19,179
who will continue the directing battle.

554
00:26:19,180 --> 00:26:20,379
Here we go.

555
00:26:20,380 --> 00:26:21,419
It's the next mission.

556
00:26:21,420 --> 00:26:22,850
The next mission is...

557
00:26:23,390 --> 00:26:24,519
(K-pop Solo Artist Direct Mission)

558
00:26:24,520 --> 00:26:26,959
the K-pop Solo Artist Direct Mission.

559
00:26:26,960 --> 00:26:28,360
- What?
- What?

560
00:26:28,790 --> 00:26:29,990
Gosh.

561
00:26:30,460 --> 00:26:32,900
The choreographers will direct a male solo artist...

562
00:26:33,000 --> 00:26:35,730
and a female solo artist.

563
00:26:35,900 --> 00:26:37,800
The completed work will...

564
00:26:38,100 --> 00:26:42,439
become their official performance...

565
00:26:42,440 --> 00:26:43,509
in September.

566
00:26:43,510 --> 00:26:45,079
Nice.

567
00:26:45,080 --> 00:26:46,839
It's a chance for me to do my job. Oh, my gosh.

568
00:26:46,840 --> 00:26:47,880
This is going to be fun.

569
00:26:48,010 --> 00:26:49,809
Awesome. That's going to be so much fun.

570
00:26:49,810 --> 00:26:51,980
It's time to do my job.

571
00:26:52,180 --> 00:26:56,589
We get to give the situation and story to the artist.

572
00:26:56,590 --> 00:26:58,919
We choose their characters on stage,

573
00:26:58,920 --> 00:27:01,559
set the theme, and shape their identity.

574
00:27:01,560 --> 00:27:03,289
And we lead them.

575
00:27:03,290 --> 00:27:07,359
Simply put, we decide everything from head to toe.

576
00:27:07,360 --> 00:27:09,370
That's exactly what I'm doing.

577
00:27:09,500 --> 00:27:10,670
It's meant for me.

578
00:27:11,470 --> 00:27:12,499
It's made for me.

579
00:27:12,500 --> 00:27:13,599
I couldn't be more confident.

580
00:27:13,600 --> 00:27:16,539
The production crew got me what I'm good at.

581
00:27:16,540 --> 00:27:17,809
I might as well accept it.

582
00:27:17,810 --> 00:27:20,209
It's one's ability to seize the opportunity, right?

583
00:27:20,210 --> 00:27:22,409
I'm confident.

584
00:27:22,410 --> 00:27:23,880
Because it's a K-pop mission.

585
00:27:24,250 --> 00:27:25,650
(While everyone is confident,)

586
00:27:25,750 --> 00:27:29,490
(only one Director's Room is quiet.)

587
00:27:29,590 --> 00:27:30,749
What am I going to do?

588
00:27:30,750 --> 00:27:32,389
I've never done K-pop before.

589
00:27:32,390 --> 00:27:35,059
If I were to do it, I could.

590
00:27:35,060 --> 00:27:37,659
It'll be a nice experience.

591
00:27:37,660 --> 00:27:40,600
Still, I have no idea what to do.

592
00:27:42,130 --> 00:27:45,169
The two solo artists who will be performing.

593
00:27:45,170 --> 00:27:47,240
Here they are.

594
00:27:47,400 --> 00:27:48,710
Who are they?

595
00:27:49,110 --> 00:27:50,139
(Male solo artist)

596
00:27:50,140 --> 00:27:51,609
(SM Entertainment, Fight Judge, global male group)

597
00:27:51,610 --> 00:27:52,780
A fight judge?

598
00:27:53,180 --> 00:27:54,910
Who was here as a fight judge?

599
00:27:55,110 --> 00:27:56,510
Is it Eunhyuk?

600
00:27:56,850 --> 00:27:57,879
That's Eunhyuk.

601
00:27:57,880 --> 00:28:00,979
SM Entertainment's global group who was here as a fight judge...

602
00:28:00,980 --> 00:28:02,020
Eunhyuk?

603
00:28:02,050 --> 00:28:03,220
A fight judge.

604
00:28:03,320 --> 00:28:04,919
A global male group. TAEYONG.

605
00:28:04,920 --> 00:28:05,990
It's got to be TAEYONG.

606
00:28:06,660 --> 00:28:09,060
He was the fight judge in Season One.

607
00:28:09,160 --> 00:28:11,760
(Is TAEYONG the male solo artist?)

608
00:28:11,930 --> 00:28:13,660
I hope it's TAEYONG.

609
00:28:13,760 --> 00:28:15,399
I recently worked with him.

610
00:28:15,400 --> 00:28:17,999
I know exactly...

611
00:28:18,000 --> 00:28:20,269
what he likes...

612
00:28:20,270 --> 00:28:21,810
and what he pursues.

613
00:28:22,010 --> 00:28:23,110
Please.

614
00:28:23,170 --> 00:28:24,339
Is it TAEYONG?

615
00:28:24,340 --> 00:28:26,480
(The artist's guide track is finally revealed.)

616
00:28:26,910 --> 00:28:28,040
(Smiling)

617
00:28:28,410 --> 00:28:30,609
It's him! Right?

618
00:28:30,610 --> 00:28:32,750
It's TAEYONG!

619
00:28:32,780 --> 00:28:34,319
(Excited)

620
00:28:34,320 --> 00:28:35,790
It must be TAEYONG.

621
00:28:35,890 --> 00:28:37,190
I bet it's TAEYONG.

622
00:28:39,590 --> 00:28:42,189
(He can't help but dance.)

623
00:28:42,190 --> 00:28:43,290
The song...

624
00:28:43,430 --> 00:28:46,999
I thought this was a song you could physically collide with.

625
00:28:47,000 --> 00:28:49,069
I figured I could capture...

626
00:28:49,070 --> 00:28:50,469
my own style in this.

627
00:28:50,470 --> 00:28:51,600
It sounds cool.

628
00:28:51,800 --> 00:28:55,740
It's an aggressive track that feels like...

629
00:28:55,970 --> 00:28:57,209
the performance would stick to it perfectly.

630
00:28:57,210 --> 00:28:58,439
I like it. It's good,

631
00:28:58,440 --> 00:29:00,039
but the concept will need to be executed really well.

632
00:29:00,040 --> 00:29:02,849
If you just the concept entirely around the song's vibe,

633
00:29:02,850 --> 00:29:04,510
we all will end up looking similar,

634
00:29:04,650 --> 00:29:07,580
so it will need a unique angle.

635
00:29:08,320 --> 00:29:11,289
The track is great, but I've never taken charge...

636
00:29:11,290 --> 00:29:12,490
of a male solo artist before,

637
00:29:12,660 --> 00:29:14,390
so I'm curious about the female solo artist.

638
00:29:15,230 --> 00:29:16,829
(Female solo artist)

639
00:29:16,830 --> 00:29:18,459
(Kinjaz, W-D, THE -LACKLABEL)

640
00:29:18,460 --> 00:29:19,999
(Shouting)

641
00:29:20,000 --> 00:29:21,970
(Explosive reaction)

642
00:29:22,070 --> 00:29:23,929
The second I saw Kinjaz, I knew immediately.

643
00:29:23,930 --> 00:29:26,040
Even without the other keywords, I know for sure.

644
00:29:26,400 --> 00:29:27,699
BAILEY is...

645
00:29:27,700 --> 00:29:29,009
literally the only intersection...

646
00:29:29,010 --> 00:29:30,470
among these three.

647
00:29:30,670 --> 00:29:33,339
(Then is the female solo artist BAILEY?)

648
00:29:33,340 --> 00:29:34,679
BAILEY. Bailey Sok

649
00:29:34,680 --> 00:29:35,910
I know her so well.

650
00:29:36,080 --> 00:29:37,849
We've even collaborated on choreography before.

651
00:29:37,850 --> 00:29:39,880
I probably have the deepest understanding of her.

652
00:29:39,920 --> 00:29:41,149
I'm curious about the track.

653
00:29:41,150 --> 00:29:42,689
The song has to be good, though.

654
00:29:42,690 --> 00:29:44,150
Please.

655
00:29:44,620 --> 00:29:46,589
(The female solo artist's guide track is revealed.)

656
00:29:46,590 --> 00:29:48,220
I'm going with this one.

657
00:29:50,430 --> 00:29:51,729
This is it!

658
00:29:51,730 --> 00:29:52,900
(This is it!)

659
00:29:52,930 --> 00:29:55,130
She's going crazy over there. She bubbles over with joy.

660
00:29:55,470 --> 00:29:56,999
I'm so excited!

661
00:29:57,000 --> 00:29:59,500
Regardless of how it goes, I just love it so much.

662
00:29:59,540 --> 00:30:02,169
It has a kind of heavy, deep vibe.

663
00:30:02,170 --> 00:30:05,179
This kind of deep, slightly minor vibe...

664
00:30:05,180 --> 00:30:06,209
is something...

665
00:30:06,210 --> 00:30:07,480
I can pull off really well.

666
00:30:07,510 --> 00:30:09,109
Musically, this one is...

667
00:30:09,110 --> 00:30:11,810
definitely much closer to what I prefer.

668
00:30:11,880 --> 00:30:12,880
It's totally my style.

669
00:30:12,881 --> 00:30:14,519
It has many intricate sounds...

670
00:30:14,520 --> 00:30:17,589
that I really want to experiment with,

671
00:30:17,590 --> 00:30:18,759
so I want it so badly.

672
00:30:18,760 --> 00:30:20,160
The song is tricky, though.

673
00:30:20,260 --> 00:30:21,660
Rather than having an easy hook,

674
00:30:21,760 --> 00:30:23,229
it feels like you have to keep dancing non-stop.

675
00:30:23,230 --> 00:30:24,689
The choreography will be crucial.

676
00:30:24,690 --> 00:30:25,800
(The choreography looks to be the deciding factor for this track.)

677
00:30:25,960 --> 00:30:27,859
Although this mission involves...

678
00:30:27,860 --> 00:30:29,029
directing a solo artist,

679
00:30:29,030 --> 00:30:31,670
the choreographers will not be competing alone.

680
00:30:31,900 --> 00:30:33,900
Street World Fighter: Directors' War's...

681
00:30:34,000 --> 00:30:35,670
first team battle.

682
00:30:36,040 --> 00:30:37,269
(2:2 Duet Match)

683
00:30:37,270 --> 00:30:39,210
The 2-on-2 Duet Match.

684
00:30:41,010 --> 00:30:42,150
Nice!

685
00:30:43,310 --> 00:30:44,750
(Celebrating it in joy)

686
00:30:44,810 --> 00:30:45,849
I love it.

687
00:30:45,850 --> 00:30:47,650
I figured there would be a team mission at least once.

688
00:30:47,920 --> 00:30:49,089
I like it.

689
00:30:49,090 --> 00:30:51,890
This was a pairing format...

690
00:30:51,960 --> 00:30:53,389
I really wanted to try.

691
00:30:53,390 --> 00:30:54,590
The 2-on-2 duet match.

692
00:30:55,430 --> 00:30:56,929
The eight choreographers...

693
00:30:56,930 --> 00:30:58,259
will pair up into teams of two...

694
00:30:58,260 --> 00:31:00,430
to direct each solo artist.

695
00:31:01,400 --> 00:31:02,669
Starting now,

696
00:31:02,670 --> 00:31:04,699
choreographers will personally choose the partner...

697
00:31:04,700 --> 00:31:06,569
they will execute the mission with.

698
00:31:06,570 --> 00:31:08,540
- Okay.
- Those who finalize their teams...

699
00:31:08,740 --> 00:31:10,309
must register their names...

700
00:31:10,310 --> 00:31:12,180
on the registration board in the center of the stage,

701
00:31:12,240 --> 00:31:13,709
and only registered pairs...

702
00:31:13,710 --> 00:31:15,750
will be recognized as official teams.

703
00:31:16,110 --> 00:31:18,750
Furthermore, once the quota is filled,

704
00:31:18,880 --> 00:31:22,220
that specific artist can no longer be chosen.

705
00:31:24,450 --> 00:31:25,690
We have to move fast.

706
00:31:25,760 --> 00:31:27,120
The result of this mission...

707
00:31:27,190 --> 00:31:29,490
directly links to survival.

708
00:31:29,590 --> 00:31:31,760
All four choreographers who win their matches...

709
00:31:31,890 --> 00:31:32,959
(The winners survive.)

710
00:31:32,960 --> 00:31:34,530
will survive.

711
00:31:34,630 --> 00:31:36,569
All four choreographers on the losing teams...

712
00:31:36,570 --> 00:31:40,640
will go straight to the Last Stage: 24H.

713
00:31:41,600 --> 00:31:43,339
I didn't know I'd be hearing that again.

714
00:31:43,340 --> 00:31:45,380
Why are you sending four whole people?

715
00:31:45,580 --> 00:31:47,709
That means a 50-50 chance.

716
00:31:47,710 --> 00:31:49,109
So we have no choice but to win.

717
00:31:49,110 --> 00:31:51,250
If I lose, I go straight to the Last Stage.

718
00:31:51,350 --> 00:31:53,520
I really need to choose my team wisely.

719
00:31:54,720 --> 00:31:56,490
I need to find...

720
00:31:56,720 --> 00:31:58,620
an absolute winning member.

721
00:31:58,660 --> 00:32:00,719
I have to pick someone who won't end up in the Last Stage.

722
00:32:00,720 --> 00:32:02,690
I need to settle this immediately...

723
00:32:02,930 --> 00:32:04,359
and get our names up on that registration board quickly.

724
00:32:04,360 --> 00:32:06,460
Avoiding the Last Stage is the smartest move.

725
00:32:06,600 --> 00:32:08,700
Who would want to team up with me for a K-pop mission?

726
00:32:09,330 --> 00:32:10,730
Probably no one.

727
00:32:11,030 --> 00:32:13,400
If you want to win, you have to take me.

728
00:32:13,600 --> 00:32:15,610
If you're looking for a winning teammate, it's me.

729
00:32:15,770 --> 00:32:17,170
I'm winning this time, no matter what.

730
00:32:17,540 --> 00:32:18,569
Got it?

731
00:32:18,570 --> 00:32:19,609
I'm the best...

732
00:32:19,610 --> 00:32:21,180
at the NEO vibe out of everyone here.

733
00:32:21,280 --> 00:32:23,110
You know I do this kind of stuff better than anyone.

734
00:32:23,280 --> 00:32:25,580
The time has finally come for me to show my true worth.

735
00:32:26,780 --> 00:32:27,980
I've made up my mind.

736
00:32:28,750 --> 00:32:29,919
I'm going with TAEYONG's track.

737
00:32:29,920 --> 00:32:31,719
I need to choose something I can execute better...

738
00:32:31,720 --> 00:32:35,390
and something I can whip up quickly and make look tasty.

739
00:32:35,460 --> 00:32:36,860
Someone TAEYONG would vibe with.

740
00:32:36,890 --> 00:32:37,890
It's NaiN.

741
00:32:37,891 --> 00:32:40,730
NaiN worked with TAEYONG most recently, after all.

742
00:32:40,900 --> 00:32:41,900
Gosh.

743
00:32:41,901 --> 00:32:44,270
(BADA's desired teammate: NaiN)

744
00:32:44,370 --> 00:32:46,669
BADA picks me.

745
00:32:46,670 --> 00:32:48,369
(NaiN, please accept my heart.)

746
00:32:48,370 --> 00:32:50,010
(Is NaiN's choice BADA as well?)

747
00:32:50,140 --> 00:32:54,479
I think I'm going with the male artist now.

748
00:32:54,480 --> 00:32:58,380
Then shouldn't I team up with NaiN,

749
00:32:58,920 --> 00:33:00,550
who's been my rival all this time?

750
00:33:00,620 --> 00:33:02,120
I have to win no matter what.

751
00:33:02,220 --> 00:33:05,089
That's why I thought NaiN and I had to join forces.

752
00:33:05,090 --> 00:33:07,089
But what if NaiN doesn't take me?

753
00:33:07,090 --> 00:33:09,190
I feel like she might go to Kasper or INGYOO.

754
00:33:09,560 --> 00:33:11,630
Please.

755
00:33:11,960 --> 00:33:13,300
NaiN!

756
00:33:13,400 --> 00:33:14,699
NaiN!

757
00:33:14,700 --> 00:33:15,769
(Desperate BABYZOO)

758
00:33:15,770 --> 00:33:16,969
Seriously.

759
00:33:16,970 --> 00:33:18,939
NaiN, you know why...

760
00:33:18,940 --> 00:33:21,300
our projects overlap so much, don't you?

761
00:33:21,340 --> 00:33:23,369
NaiN, I'm right here!

762
00:33:23,370 --> 00:33:24,770
NaiN!

763
00:33:24,910 --> 00:33:26,609
I really want to do BAILEY's track.

764
00:33:26,610 --> 00:33:27,939
First off...

765
00:33:27,940 --> 00:33:29,109
Simeez?

766
00:33:29,110 --> 00:33:31,479
I thought Simeez was the only one...

767
00:33:31,480 --> 00:33:34,020
who could bring out the feminine vibe.

768
00:33:34,320 --> 00:33:37,719
She's someone who can compensate...

769
00:33:37,720 --> 00:33:39,990
for what you might call my slight weaknesses.

770
00:33:40,790 --> 00:33:42,130
(Flapping)

771
00:33:42,530 --> 00:33:46,830
(A performance to win her over)

772
00:33:47,860 --> 00:33:49,399
(Gestures trying to win over Simeez)

773
00:33:49,400 --> 00:33:50,999
(She has no idea.)

774
00:33:51,000 --> 00:33:53,540
(While Kasper sends out his love signals)

775
00:33:54,340 --> 00:33:57,240
I think teaming up with Simeez makes the most sense.

776
00:33:57,870 --> 00:33:59,909
Since I never want to end up in the Last Stage,

777
00:33:59,910 --> 00:34:01,509
wouldn't it be best to pair up with Simeez,

778
00:34:01,510 --> 00:34:04,509
where our synergy would clearly pop?

779
00:34:04,510 --> 00:34:06,419
She's been handling IVE...

780
00:34:06,420 --> 00:34:08,790
right from the pre-production stage, and tapping into that experience

781
00:34:08,850 --> 00:34:10,589
while setting a solid concept and tone...

782
00:34:10,590 --> 00:34:11,920
would make our work convincing.

783
00:34:11,990 --> 00:34:14,360
I'm just praying Simeez feels the same way.

784
00:34:15,630 --> 00:34:16,659
(Another heart signal)

785
00:34:16,660 --> 00:34:17,930
(INGYOO's desired teammate: Simeez)

786
00:34:18,690 --> 00:34:21,159
(Who wants to team up with me?)

787
00:34:21,160 --> 00:34:23,030
I think I'll team up with INGYOO.

788
00:34:23,100 --> 00:34:24,830
INGYOO just sent me a signal.

789
00:34:24,930 --> 00:34:26,339
Hang on.

790
00:34:26,340 --> 00:34:28,599
It looks like Kasper is also sending a signal.

791
00:34:28,600 --> 00:34:29,639
Or am I imagining things?

792
00:34:29,640 --> 00:34:30,969
I locked eyes with both INGYOO and Kasper.

793
00:34:30,970 --> 00:34:31,970
Now...

794
00:34:31,971 --> 00:34:33,180
(Two men are sending desperate signals toward Simeez.)

795
00:34:34,180 --> 00:34:36,079
They both are... Maybe I'm wrong.

796
00:34:36,080 --> 00:34:38,250
If I have to choose, that's kind of tough for me.

797
00:34:38,410 --> 00:34:39,779
(Who will be the teammate to join Simeez?)

798
00:34:39,780 --> 00:34:41,350
Are you sending signals now?

799
00:34:42,190 --> 00:34:43,690
(Thinking)

800
00:34:44,790 --> 00:34:46,219
Would anyone even want to team up with me?

801
00:34:46,220 --> 00:34:47,820
I'm such an old-timer.

802
00:34:47,920 --> 00:34:49,829
I'm kind of an old head, you know?

803
00:34:49,830 --> 00:34:50,830
So...

804
00:34:50,831 --> 00:34:51,890
(An old head)

805
00:34:51,960 --> 00:34:53,900
Would any of them actually want to work with me?

806
00:34:54,600 --> 00:34:56,199
Should I just pair up with whoever's left?

807
00:34:56,200 --> 00:34:58,800
Let's say MIN JUN and I are left. Even if I team up with him,

808
00:34:58,970 --> 00:35:00,100
I'm still confident.

809
00:35:00,700 --> 00:35:01,999
I need to team up with INGYOO.

810
00:35:02,000 --> 00:35:04,869
They are only going to try pairing up with frontrunners,

811
00:35:04,870 --> 00:35:06,109
so I think I need to claim him first...

812
00:35:06,110 --> 00:35:07,540
and block his way.

813
00:35:07,680 --> 00:35:09,649
I have to win this mission.

814
00:35:09,650 --> 00:35:11,910
I don't want to go to the Last Stage ever again.

815
00:35:12,080 --> 00:35:13,149
I should sprint straight to INGYOO...

816
00:35:13,150 --> 00:35:14,950
and tell him to do BAILEY's track with me.

817
00:35:15,050 --> 00:35:16,350
I'll drag him along like this.

818
00:35:16,420 --> 00:35:18,589
Then let me get ready to dash out,

819
00:35:18,590 --> 00:35:19,990
since I have to be the first one sprinting.

820
00:35:20,160 --> 00:35:22,289
(Warming up)

821
00:35:22,290 --> 00:35:25,360
Everyone is ready to sprint right now.

822
00:35:26,130 --> 00:35:27,759
When is the siren going off?

823
00:35:27,760 --> 00:35:30,930
It usually goes off so fast. Why is it taking forever today?

824
00:35:30,970 --> 00:35:32,899
Isn't NaiN at an advantage?

825
00:35:32,900 --> 00:35:34,600
Isn't she too close to the registration board?

826
00:35:34,700 --> 00:35:36,640
I'm going to sprint really fast.

827
00:35:36,840 --> 00:35:38,310
(Team selection starts!)

828
00:35:38,710 --> 00:35:40,410
(Simeez rushes out.)

829
00:35:40,910 --> 00:35:42,450
Is it now?

830
00:35:43,450 --> 00:35:45,309
(I have to hurry.)

831
00:35:45,310 --> 00:35:47,850
(All 8 choreographers sprint out at full speed.)

832
00:35:48,550 --> 00:35:49,589
(Got you!)

833
00:35:49,590 --> 00:35:51,790
Even if it means kidnapping INGYOO, I have to drag him over.

834
00:35:51,850 --> 00:35:54,220
There was only one path. BAILEY was the only option for me.

835
00:35:54,290 --> 00:35:55,759
(Full sprint)

836
00:35:55,760 --> 00:35:56,790
What?

837
00:35:57,130 --> 00:35:59,129
- Should we do this one?
- Right?

838
00:35:59,130 --> 00:36:00,159
NaiN, do you want to team up with me?

839
00:36:00,160 --> 00:36:01,959
NaiN, put your name on it!

840
00:36:01,960 --> 00:36:02,969
(This is not finalized yet.)

841
00:36:02,970 --> 00:36:03,999
Let's do this together.

842
00:36:04,000 --> 00:36:05,000
(Hesitant)

843
00:36:05,001 --> 00:36:06,040
- Let's do it.
- No.

844
00:36:06,200 --> 00:36:08,199
No. That's not it.

845
00:36:08,200 --> 00:36:09,470
Hurry!

846
00:36:09,610 --> 00:36:11,770
(Stopping him urgently)

847
00:36:11,840 --> 00:36:13,910
You have to form the team before sticking the names on.

848
00:36:14,310 --> 00:36:15,650
Did you guys already form a team?

849
00:36:15,980 --> 00:36:18,709
Wait, aren't you supposed to form the team first?

850
00:36:18,710 --> 00:36:19,950
Right. We need to talk it out.

851
00:36:19,980 --> 00:36:22,390
Exactly, talk first.

852
00:36:22,490 --> 00:36:24,050
Let's go back in.

853
00:36:24,220 --> 00:36:25,690
- What?
- We need to talk first.

854
00:36:26,090 --> 00:36:27,290
We need to talk.

855
00:36:27,460 --> 00:36:28,589
I'm the first one to enter.

856
00:36:28,590 --> 00:36:30,490
Honestly, it makes the most sense that we team up.

857
00:36:31,160 --> 00:36:32,759
(Thinking)

858
00:36:32,760 --> 00:36:34,699
I think this is the right moment for us to join forces.

859
00:36:34,700 --> 00:36:36,399
It's time to show them what we've got.

860
00:36:36,400 --> 00:36:37,529
(My goodness.)

861
00:36:37,530 --> 00:36:38,629
What do we do?

862
00:36:38,630 --> 00:36:41,670
People with great aesthetic sense need to stick together.

863
00:36:42,140 --> 00:36:43,309
For now,

864
00:36:43,310 --> 00:36:44,410
my first choice is Simeez.

865
00:36:44,840 --> 00:36:45,880
(Come here.)

866
00:36:46,080 --> 00:36:47,540
He's calling for me.

867
00:36:47,940 --> 00:36:49,780
I should go crash this conversation.

868
00:36:51,150 --> 00:36:53,349
- Could we talk for just a second?
- Okay.

869
00:36:53,350 --> 00:36:54,950
Let's talk in a bit, too.

870
00:36:55,150 --> 00:36:56,190
Well...

871
00:36:56,520 --> 00:36:59,589
Even though Simeez was already with INGYOO,

872
00:36:59,590 --> 00:37:01,259
with the mindset of "it never hurts to give it a shot,"

873
00:37:01,260 --> 00:37:02,990
I asked to talk to Simeez.

874
00:37:03,230 --> 00:37:04,789
Kasper is someone...

875
00:37:04,790 --> 00:37:06,960
who studied BAILEY inside out, too.

876
00:37:08,130 --> 00:37:09,600
(I'm confident, too.)

877
00:37:09,630 --> 00:37:11,930
- You don't even need to explain?
- Why?

878
00:37:13,300 --> 00:37:14,470
What do I do?

879
00:37:15,200 --> 00:37:18,039
INGYOO was talking with Simeez for quite a while.

880
00:37:18,040 --> 00:37:19,209
I thought, "His mind is already made up."

881
00:37:19,210 --> 00:37:20,439
"There's no way I can turn him around."

882
00:37:20,440 --> 00:37:22,780
Stalling for time here would be fatal.

883
00:37:22,880 --> 00:37:25,079
NaiN, you know why our projects...

884
00:37:25,080 --> 00:37:26,849
- overlap so much, don't you?
- I also think...

885
00:37:26,850 --> 00:37:29,020
there's a good reason people keep calling us together.

886
00:37:29,090 --> 00:37:31,190
If you want to unlock that synergy, you have to team up with me.

887
00:37:31,890 --> 00:37:33,920
I'll make sure that synergy pays off.

888
00:37:34,120 --> 00:37:35,219
(Approaching)

889
00:37:35,220 --> 00:37:36,660
How about taking on BAILEY with me?

890
00:37:37,030 --> 00:37:38,460
She's my favorite.

891
00:37:38,490 --> 00:37:39,799
Would you like to team up with me?

892
00:37:39,800 --> 00:37:40,959
(Torn)

893
00:37:40,960 --> 00:37:42,370
My goodness. But...

894
00:37:42,900 --> 00:37:44,070
BAILEY?

895
00:37:44,170 --> 00:37:45,270
NaiN.

896
00:37:45,400 --> 00:37:46,500
What will you do?

897
00:37:47,540 --> 00:37:48,640
What do you want to do?

898
00:37:49,410 --> 00:37:51,210
BABYZOO, what are you leaning toward?

899
00:37:51,310 --> 00:37:52,739
- NaiN. Let's talk for a second.
- Okay.

900
00:37:52,740 --> 00:37:53,880
Let's head over this way, then.

901
00:37:54,010 --> 00:37:55,849
- MIN JUN? Okay.
- But, MIN JUN,

902
00:37:55,850 --> 00:37:57,609
I feel like I have to do TAEYONG's track.

903
00:37:57,610 --> 00:37:58,780
- Do you not mind?
- It doesn't matter.

904
00:37:59,320 --> 00:38:00,379
MIN JUN.

905
00:38:00,380 --> 00:38:01,949
I wanted to work with NaiN,

906
00:38:01,950 --> 00:38:03,389
but the moment she went straight to BABYZOO,

907
00:38:03,390 --> 00:38:04,649
it seemed like her mind was already set,

908
00:38:04,650 --> 00:38:06,090
so my focus shifted immediately.

909
00:38:06,790 --> 00:38:08,019
I was worried...

910
00:38:08,020 --> 00:38:10,759
because they are the ones doing a lot of projects lately,

911
00:38:10,760 --> 00:38:14,260
whereas I'm from the generation whose work has dwindled down.

912
00:38:14,360 --> 00:38:15,629
I thought it might feel burdensome...

913
00:38:15,630 --> 00:38:17,269
if I ask them to team up with me first.

914
00:38:17,270 --> 00:38:19,470
So I figured I should just wait a bit.

915
00:38:19,540 --> 00:38:21,700
Do you feel like you'd need me?

916
00:38:21,870 --> 00:38:23,840
BABYZOO is actually my first choice.

917
00:38:24,540 --> 00:38:26,110
I will head straight to BABYZOO the second I step out.

918
00:38:27,110 --> 00:38:30,410
The thing is, our strengths are distinctly different.

919
00:38:30,680 --> 00:38:32,820
He's really good at the things I fall short in.

920
00:38:33,020 --> 00:38:35,050
I think he excels at building unique formations...

921
00:38:35,350 --> 00:38:38,289
and crafting flashy visual pictures...

922
00:38:38,290 --> 00:38:40,919
using dancers.

923
00:38:40,920 --> 00:38:43,260
So I had BABYZOO in mind from the very start.

924
00:38:43,960 --> 00:38:44,989
All right.

925
00:38:44,990 --> 00:38:47,559
(Feeling bitter)

926
00:38:47,560 --> 00:38:49,330
Since I have zero K-pop experience,

927
00:38:49,370 --> 00:38:50,930
I'm pretty much the odd one out.

928
00:38:51,070 --> 00:38:54,040
Feeling like nobody wanted me was so heartbreaking.

929
00:38:54,500 --> 00:38:55,640
Do you want to team up with me?

930
00:38:56,070 --> 00:38:57,439
(Well...)

931
00:38:57,440 --> 00:38:58,940
Can you wait? I need to think.

932
00:38:59,610 --> 00:39:00,610
I'm sorry.

933
00:39:00,840 --> 00:39:01,979
He doesn't have much K-pop experience.

934
00:39:01,980 --> 00:39:03,979
This isn't just about tossing out ideas.

935
00:39:03,980 --> 00:39:05,079
It's a battle to get your choreo picked.

936
00:39:05,080 --> 00:39:06,379
With my own neck on the line,

937
00:39:06,380 --> 00:39:09,590
it's tough to hold someone's hand and spoon-feed them through this.

938
00:39:10,220 --> 00:39:11,989
I wanted to pour my heart into doing well,

939
00:39:11,990 --> 00:39:14,460
but this massive wall called K-pop blocked my way.

940
00:39:14,990 --> 00:39:17,730
What can I actually bring to the table?

941
00:39:18,060 --> 00:39:19,859
(Heavy-hearted)

942
00:39:19,860 --> 00:39:23,100
Koo Young was standing right there, all by himself.

943
00:39:23,900 --> 00:39:26,470
So I thought I had to do this with him.

944
00:39:27,300 --> 00:39:28,470
Do you want to head to a room and chat?

945
00:39:28,570 --> 00:39:31,910
He's a director with an insane career history.

946
00:39:32,640 --> 00:39:33,879
For 24 years?

947
00:39:33,880 --> 00:39:35,809
His career spans longer than my actual age.

948
00:39:35,810 --> 00:39:38,380
When it comes to sheer experience, no one can beat him.

949
00:39:38,750 --> 00:39:40,579
I have to team up with him, no matter what.

950
00:39:40,580 --> 00:39:42,890
I need to talk this through with Koo Young.

951
00:39:43,350 --> 00:39:47,119
Personally, working on the Title Sequence Film Mission...

952
00:39:47,120 --> 00:39:49,559
made me realize our dance styles spark...

953
00:39:49,560 --> 00:39:51,060
- incredible synergy, - Right.

954
00:39:51,230 --> 00:39:53,099
which is why I want to work with you.

955
00:39:53,100 --> 00:39:54,159
To be honest,

956
00:39:54,160 --> 00:39:55,559
(Chuckling)

957
00:39:55,560 --> 00:39:57,130
you're my favorite.

958
00:39:57,670 --> 00:39:58,769
- Then...
- I don't care about anything...

959
00:39:58,770 --> 00:40:00,199
as long as I'm with you.

960
00:40:00,200 --> 00:40:01,540
Even if I get eliminated, it won't matter.

961
00:40:02,370 --> 00:40:03,639
Ever since I joined this survival show,

962
00:40:03,640 --> 00:40:05,909
I have always wanted to collaborate with Koo Young at least once,

963
00:40:05,910 --> 00:40:08,109
and I felt it would be so much fun.

964
00:40:08,110 --> 00:40:10,580
I'd be thrilled if you joined me.

965
00:40:11,110 --> 00:40:12,180
I'm serious.

966
00:40:13,080 --> 00:40:14,849
I mean it. I'm being serious.

967
00:40:14,850 --> 00:40:17,890
Thankfully, BADA extended her hand,

968
00:40:18,150 --> 00:40:20,259
and there is immense trust, credibility,

969
00:40:20,260 --> 00:40:21,559
and effortless chemistry between us.

970
00:40:21,560 --> 00:40:23,860
Teaming up with her is amazing for me too.

971
00:40:25,290 --> 00:40:26,600
Their conversation is dragging on.

972
00:40:27,830 --> 00:40:29,270
It looks like Kasper is desperate.

973
00:40:29,700 --> 00:40:31,670
- This is driving me crazy.
- Just do it with me.

974
00:40:32,000 --> 00:40:33,300
I assumed you were going for TAEYONG's track.

975
00:40:33,440 --> 00:40:36,009
I know what BAILEY needs,

976
00:40:36,010 --> 00:40:39,010
and I know the exact extent of her skill set.

977
00:40:39,240 --> 00:40:41,280
Besides, I've directed the most solo artists out of anyone here.

978
00:40:41,640 --> 00:40:42,709
Right?

979
00:40:42,710 --> 00:40:45,480
I'm not scrambling to find someone just to win...

980
00:40:45,580 --> 00:40:47,049
and dodge the Last Stage.

981
00:40:47,050 --> 00:40:48,520
I simply want to do this with you.

982
00:40:49,350 --> 00:40:51,290
Honestly, I love them both.

983
00:40:51,350 --> 00:40:52,350
I was torn.

984
00:40:52,590 --> 00:40:53,919
If not me, who else are you going to team up with?

985
00:40:53,920 --> 00:40:55,120
If you're not in, I'll do it by myself.

986
00:40:55,830 --> 00:40:57,330
I think I was conflicted.

987
00:40:58,260 --> 00:41:01,230
I mean, there's no one here...

988
00:41:03,000 --> 00:41:04,269
I want to work with besides you.

989
00:41:04,270 --> 00:41:06,640
(You're the only one.)

990
00:41:07,370 --> 00:41:08,469
This is driving me crazy.

991
00:41:08,470 --> 00:41:11,010
I thought Simeez was the only one.

992
00:41:11,240 --> 00:41:14,610
Kasper has a lot of experience directing solo artists...

993
00:41:14,840 --> 00:41:16,450
and knows BAILEY so well...

994
00:41:16,680 --> 00:41:19,180
that he could elevate her performance.

995
00:41:19,280 --> 00:41:22,180
Meanwhile, INGYOO can pinpoint an artist's peak potential so well.

996
00:41:22,650 --> 00:41:24,550
So I was agonizing over it.

997
00:41:25,320 --> 00:41:26,420
What did she say?

998
00:41:26,860 --> 00:41:28,690
- I should head in.
- She's hesitating.

999
00:41:29,160 --> 00:41:32,060
Simeez was the only person on my mind.

1000
00:41:32,230 --> 00:41:33,560
Because I was desperate too.

1001
00:41:33,660 --> 00:41:35,500
I figured she might want me.

1002
00:41:35,760 --> 00:41:37,900
(What is Simeez's choice?)

1003
00:41:38,370 --> 00:41:39,599
Well, as for us...

1004
00:41:39,600 --> 00:41:41,870
You guys look pretty rock-solid.

1005
00:41:42,440 --> 00:41:43,610
We've made up our minds.

1006
00:41:44,170 --> 00:41:45,469
(NaiN and BABYZOO)

1007
00:41:45,470 --> 00:41:46,540
(They selected the male solo artist.)

1008
00:41:46,680 --> 00:41:49,180
- BABYZOO!
- NaiN! Let's show them.

1009
00:41:49,350 --> 00:41:50,680
I'm finally teaming up with you.

1010
00:41:51,010 --> 00:41:52,549
I know. We're finally on the same team.

1011
00:41:52,550 --> 00:41:54,720
I have a good feeling right now.

1012
00:41:55,450 --> 00:41:57,320
- We'll never go to the Last Stage.
- Of course not.

1013
00:41:58,090 --> 00:41:59,460
Where are you sticking your name? TAEYONG?

1014
00:41:59,920 --> 00:42:02,360
I don't want to go against Koo Young and BADA.

1015
00:42:02,420 --> 00:42:04,889
Wouldn't Koo Young head over to TAEYONG?

1016
00:42:04,890 --> 00:42:06,029
I wanted to avoid them.

1017
00:42:06,030 --> 00:42:07,299
(Those who choose the male solo artist slot...)

1018
00:42:07,300 --> 00:42:09,570
(will go against NaiN and BABYZOO.)

1019
00:42:11,100 --> 00:42:12,699
Let's go!

1020
00:42:12,700 --> 00:42:14,499
(BADA and Back Koo Young)

1021
00:42:14,500 --> 00:42:17,310
(They selected the male solo artist.)

1022
00:42:17,540 --> 00:42:21,780
Just as expected, BADA and Koo Young stuck their names.

1023
00:42:21,910 --> 00:42:23,479
It's going to be tough,

1024
00:42:23,480 --> 00:42:26,550
but now is our only chance to take down Koo Young and BADA.

1025
00:42:26,620 --> 00:42:28,820
(Solo Artist Direct Mission, Male Artist)

1026
00:42:29,050 --> 00:42:30,119
What are we going to do?

1027
00:42:30,120 --> 00:42:31,720
Hey. Just team up with me.

1028
00:42:31,920 --> 00:42:33,390
This is torture.

1029
00:42:33,590 --> 00:42:36,890
I still haven't decided between the two. It's hard.

1030
00:42:37,160 --> 00:42:38,360
I really hope she chooses me.

1031
00:42:38,560 --> 00:42:39,629
She seemed torn,

1032
00:42:39,630 --> 00:42:41,660
but I predicted the answer would be obvious.

1033
00:42:43,770 --> 00:42:44,770
(Team up with me.)

1034
00:42:44,770 --> 00:42:45,770
(Studying his face)

1035
00:42:46,870 --> 00:42:49,340
I'm going with INGYOO. I'm so sorry.

1036
00:42:49,710 --> 00:42:50,839
I'm really sorry.

1037
00:42:50,840 --> 00:42:54,379
Rather than bouncing ideas back and forth,

1038
00:42:54,380 --> 00:42:55,909
Kasper tends to work entirely under his own direct lead.

1039
00:42:55,910 --> 00:42:57,549
So I had no choice but to go with someone...

1040
00:42:57,550 --> 00:42:59,180
whose working style aligns better with mine.

1041
00:42:59,420 --> 00:43:00,920
Okay.

1042
00:43:01,220 --> 00:43:04,289
- I'm really sorry.
- My goodness.

1043
00:43:04,290 --> 00:43:06,519
(JEONG MIN JUN and Kasper: Female solo artist)

1044
00:43:06,520 --> 00:43:09,590
(Solo Artist Direct Mission Female Artist)

1045
00:43:09,830 --> 00:43:12,359
With Kasper's experience,

1046
00:43:12,360 --> 00:43:14,260
he and MIN JUN will click really well.

1047
00:43:14,600 --> 00:43:16,999
- Do you trust me?
- Sure. Do you trust me?

1048
00:43:17,000 --> 00:43:18,000
(Of course.)

1049
00:43:18,200 --> 00:43:19,869
It wasn't the result I wanted.

1050
00:43:19,870 --> 00:43:22,839
I think I felt a bit pathetic about myself.

1051
00:43:22,840 --> 00:43:24,009
The two remaining people.

1052
00:43:24,010 --> 00:43:26,210
I don't think they recognize what I bring to the table.

1053
00:43:26,640 --> 00:43:28,509
But it's hard to take them lightly.

1054
00:43:28,510 --> 00:43:30,279
Kasper has plenty of experience.

1055
00:43:30,280 --> 00:43:33,720
The ones who looked the most like seasoned directors chose BAILEY.

1056
00:43:34,320 --> 00:43:36,719
I will send Kasper and MIN JUN to the Last Stage.

1057
00:43:36,720 --> 00:43:37,790
It is what it is.

1058
00:43:39,250 --> 00:43:41,460
It's about time for Kasper to experience it.

1059
00:43:42,020 --> 00:43:43,430
The unchosen ones.

1060
00:43:43,860 --> 00:43:45,230
A team forged by Nature.

1061
00:43:45,860 --> 00:43:47,359
This isn't a team made by our own will.

1062
00:43:47,360 --> 00:43:49,470
Nature brought us together. It's Season Two.

1063
00:43:50,100 --> 00:43:52,700
I think it was a moment I was humiliated by my abilities.

1064
00:43:52,940 --> 00:43:54,200
I feel like crying.

1065
00:43:55,500 --> 00:43:57,570
(Without fail, the siren blares across the Directors' Square.)

1066
00:43:58,210 --> 00:44:01,340
I was pleased to get to collaborate with NaiN.

1067
00:44:01,710 --> 00:44:04,110
I was so thrilled to team up with INGYOO.

1068
00:44:04,550 --> 00:44:06,420
(A warm atmosphere fills the Square after the duet pairings are set.)

1069
00:44:06,720 --> 00:44:08,680
(But MIN JUN's chair sits empty.)

1070
00:44:09,820 --> 00:44:12,050
(Glancing over)

1071
00:44:14,690 --> 00:44:15,959
I felt so small.

1072
00:44:15,960 --> 00:44:18,290
I think I felt a bit pathetic about myself.

1073
00:44:18,490 --> 00:44:20,129
Everyone else has so much experience...

1074
00:44:20,130 --> 00:44:22,129
- Yes!
- and radiates confidence.

1075
00:44:22,130 --> 00:44:24,330
but since I lack K-pop experience,

1076
00:44:24,500 --> 00:44:27,769
I wondered what I could bring to the table in this mission.

1077
00:44:27,770 --> 00:44:30,010
I didn't want to become dead weight to Kasper.

1078
00:44:30,740 --> 00:44:32,509
I was worried I'd just be a burden.

1079
00:44:32,510 --> 00:44:34,310
No. Seriously, don't worry about it.

1080
00:44:34,680 --> 00:44:35,879
Just trust me and follow my lead.

1081
00:44:35,880 --> 00:44:37,909
I can tell you what you're capable of...

1082
00:44:37,910 --> 00:44:40,320
and exactly what you need to do.

1083
00:44:40,420 --> 00:44:41,420
And...

1084
00:44:41,421 --> 00:44:44,020
MIN JUN might lack K-pop experience right now,

1085
00:44:44,120 --> 00:44:45,789
but I believed he had his own strengths.

1086
00:44:45,790 --> 00:44:47,219
You can't always be great from the start.

1087
00:44:47,220 --> 00:44:49,460
If I were in a dance competition, I wouldn't do as well as MIN JUN.

1088
00:44:49,860 --> 00:44:51,290
Thankfully, I felt relieved.

1089
00:44:51,490 --> 00:44:52,930
I had so many worries weighing on me.

1090
00:44:53,100 --> 00:44:55,800
Kasper has a long career and tons of experience.

1091
00:44:56,070 --> 00:44:57,600
It was a huge help back then.

1092
00:44:57,930 --> 00:45:00,070
For now, we just have to put in the work no matter what.

1093
00:45:00,100 --> 00:45:01,800
This is terrifying.

1094
00:45:02,600 --> 00:45:03,940
This is scary.

1095
00:45:04,440 --> 00:45:06,440
- The silence is even scarier.
- That's what makes them scarier.

1096
00:45:06,710 --> 00:45:07,940
I'm terrified of these two.

1097
00:45:08,640 --> 00:45:10,449
I looked into their eyes, and they were ashen.

1098
00:45:10,450 --> 00:45:11,679
They were filled with resentment.

1099
00:45:11,680 --> 00:45:12,980
It looked like he was about to summon a spirit.

1100
00:45:13,280 --> 00:45:14,450
The spirit has entered him.

1101
00:45:14,820 --> 00:45:15,879
MIN JUN literally...

1102
00:45:15,880 --> 00:45:17,619
walked back from the brink of death.

1103
00:45:17,620 --> 00:45:20,190
Would it even be fun watching him go back to the Last Stage?

1104
00:45:20,290 --> 00:45:22,989
Watching Simeez and INGYOO get sent to the Last Stage here...

1105
00:45:22,990 --> 00:45:24,460
will be the truly entertaining picture.

1106
00:45:24,960 --> 00:45:26,130
Please say something.

1107
00:45:26,360 --> 00:45:28,560
I'm just back from the Last Stage, so I've got venom in me now.

1108
00:45:28,760 --> 00:45:30,800
- My goodness.
- I'm scared.

1109
00:45:30,900 --> 00:45:33,269
I'm beating Simeez and INGYOO no matter what...

1110
00:45:33,270 --> 00:45:34,900
and dragging them all down to the Last Stage.

1111
00:45:35,100 --> 00:45:37,210
Please, go get a taste of that bitter pill yourselves.

1112
00:45:37,440 --> 00:45:39,439
Don't even ask me. I have no intention of going.

1113
00:45:39,440 --> 00:45:40,979
I desperately wanted to avoid the Last Stage,

1114
00:45:40,980 --> 00:45:43,109
and I'm going to claw my way to a win this time.

1115
00:45:43,110 --> 00:45:44,379
I want a complete victory.

1116
00:45:44,380 --> 00:45:46,010
We absolutely cannot go to the Last Stage.

1117
00:45:47,020 --> 00:45:48,220
It's brutal over there.

1118
00:45:48,320 --> 00:45:50,350
Hee Jung's heart is feeling heavy now.

1119
00:45:51,050 --> 00:45:54,020
She's kind of famous for being BAILEY's lookalike.

1120
00:45:54,120 --> 00:45:55,259
- Right.
- Hee Jung is?

1121
00:45:55,260 --> 00:45:57,359
A lot of people say she looks like BAILEY.

1122
00:45:57,360 --> 00:45:59,030
I feel like you'd be on BAILEY's visual mood board.

1123
00:45:59,530 --> 00:46:01,160
- What? Me?
- Yes.

1124
00:46:01,730 --> 00:46:02,970
I get that a lot.

1125
00:46:03,270 --> 00:46:04,300
Hey!

1126
00:46:04,370 --> 00:46:05,370
My gosh. What's that?

1127
00:46:05,371 --> 00:46:07,039
(Startled)

1128
00:46:07,040 --> 00:46:08,040
(Shocked)

1129
00:46:08,041 --> 00:46:09,269
What? It's amazing!

1130
00:46:09,270 --> 00:46:11,239
(Thrilled)

1131
00:46:11,240 --> 00:46:12,370
Unbelievable!

1132
00:46:13,310 --> 00:46:14,340
Hey!

1133
00:46:14,410 --> 00:46:15,410
My gosh. What's that?

1134
00:46:15,411 --> 00:46:17,079
(Startled)

1135
00:46:17,080 --> 00:46:18,080
(Shocked)

1136
00:46:18,250 --> 00:46:19,780
I was really surprised.

1137
00:46:20,050 --> 00:46:21,480
(Some people show up.)

1138
00:46:21,780 --> 00:46:23,150
(TAEYONG of NCT)

1139
00:46:24,990 --> 00:46:26,490
(BAILEY of ALLDAY PROJECT)

1140
00:46:27,090 --> 00:46:28,260
I'm really shocked.

1141
00:46:28,590 --> 00:46:29,930
I didn't expect them to show up.

1142
00:46:30,090 --> 00:46:32,160
I was so surprised to see them.

1143
00:46:32,390 --> 00:46:33,530
(Glad)

1144
00:46:33,730 --> 00:46:34,960
(Amazed)

1145
00:46:35,060 --> 00:46:36,369
(The artists for the mission: TAEYONG and BAILEY)

1146
00:46:36,370 --> 00:46:38,229
I felt the endorphins kick in.

1147
00:46:38,230 --> 00:46:39,230
Hello.

1148
00:46:39,231 --> 00:46:42,499
I'm TAEYONG, here to join you for the Solo Artist Direct Mission.

1149
00:46:42,500 --> 00:46:43,710
(TAEYONG: The solo artist whom the choreographers will direct)

1150
00:46:44,510 --> 00:46:47,980
He has dancing skills that professional dancers acknowledge.

1151
00:46:48,140 --> 00:46:49,850
He really pulls off the NEO vibe, too.

1152
00:46:50,150 --> 00:46:51,949
TAEYONG has a distinct color that's entirely his own.

1153
00:46:51,950 --> 00:46:53,120
Someone who knows how to carry style.

1154
00:46:53,280 --> 00:46:55,119
It was so surreal...

1155
00:46:55,120 --> 00:46:58,450
because it felt like watching TAEYONG of NCT right off the screen.

1156
00:46:58,790 --> 00:46:59,920
He was just so cool.

1157
00:47:00,720 --> 00:47:02,090
I only had eyes for BAILEY.

1158
00:47:02,290 --> 00:47:04,489
Her visual style in itself is something I love so much.

1159
00:47:04,490 --> 00:47:06,030
- I know.
- She looked so cool...

1160
00:47:06,130 --> 00:47:07,759
and striking.

1161
00:47:07,760 --> 00:47:09,870
You could definitely feel that true artist aura from her.

1162
00:47:10,170 --> 00:47:11,870
Hello. I'm BAILEY.

1163
00:47:13,140 --> 00:47:15,240
When people think of Kinjaz, who else comes to mind?

1164
00:47:15,300 --> 00:47:16,510
It's definitely BAILEY.

1165
00:47:16,570 --> 00:47:17,739
She competed...

1166
00:47:17,740 --> 00:47:20,080
on the WOD at age 14.

1167
00:47:20,340 --> 00:47:22,379
And at 16, she choreographed Red Velvet.

1168
00:47:22,380 --> 00:47:24,609
Her resume alone is already on a completely different level.

1169
00:47:24,610 --> 00:47:26,779
Her track record is truly unmatched in scale.

1170
00:47:26,780 --> 00:47:30,220
I think Bailey is an artist who can always take it further.

1171
00:47:30,420 --> 00:47:32,319
She's truly one of a kind,

1172
00:47:32,320 --> 00:47:34,720
a unique character in K-pop.

1173
00:47:34,860 --> 00:47:37,029
I am truly so honored to be here.

1174
00:47:37,030 --> 00:47:38,290
I'm so excited.

1175
00:47:38,490 --> 00:47:40,129
I'm a big fan of all of you guys.

1176
00:47:40,130 --> 00:47:42,329
So I'm more than grateful to be here.

1177
00:47:42,330 --> 00:47:43,799
I look forward to working with you.

1178
00:47:43,800 --> 00:47:45,429
(We are looking forward to it more.)

1179
00:47:45,430 --> 00:47:48,439
For this comeback, I want to show a new side of myself.

1180
00:47:48,440 --> 00:47:49,909
So beyond making choreography, I see this as a mission...

1181
00:47:49,910 --> 00:47:51,509
about how to direct...

1182
00:47:51,510 --> 00:47:53,309
and present the performance.

1183
00:47:53,310 --> 00:47:55,039
I'm really looking forward to it.

1184
00:47:55,040 --> 00:47:56,350
I look forward to working with you.

1185
00:47:57,210 --> 00:47:58,580
(Excited)

1186
00:47:58,780 --> 00:48:01,149
My first representation of myself...

1187
00:48:01,150 --> 00:48:02,279
as a solo artist.

1188
00:48:02,280 --> 00:48:03,290
So...

1189
00:48:03,650 --> 00:48:04,719
shall we hear it?

1190
00:48:04,720 --> 00:48:05,720
Yes!

1191
00:48:06,090 --> 00:48:07,559
This is "Can't Kill Me."

1192
00:48:07,560 --> 00:48:08,990
("Can't Kill Me" by Bailey)

1193
00:48:09,160 --> 00:48:10,690
"Can't Kill Me."

1194
00:48:12,290 --> 00:48:13,299
(Thrilled)

1195
00:48:13,300 --> 00:48:16,369
I liked it because the song itself fits my style.

1196
00:48:16,370 --> 00:48:18,200
It has a sexy feel too.

1197
00:48:18,270 --> 00:48:19,570
I love the intro.

1198
00:48:19,700 --> 00:48:21,639
First of all, the quality is great.

1199
00:48:21,640 --> 00:48:24,069
It's dark and slightly grotesque...

1200
00:48:24,070 --> 00:48:26,740
but it has this dangerously feminine edge.

1201
00:48:26,940 --> 00:48:29,580
I was glad Simeez could fill that feminine side for us.

1202
00:48:29,910 --> 00:48:31,749
But MIN JUN and Kasper don't have...

1203
00:48:31,750 --> 00:48:33,579
that feminine side covered.

1204
00:48:33,580 --> 00:48:36,220
But Bailey is a female artist,

1205
00:48:36,490 --> 00:48:39,389
and it doesn't have to be focused only on femininity.

1206
00:48:39,390 --> 00:48:41,759
There are endless possibilities.

1207
00:48:41,760 --> 00:48:44,230
I didn't think that would put me at much of a disadvantage.

1208
00:48:44,390 --> 00:48:46,089
That actually made me more nervous.

1209
00:48:46,090 --> 00:48:47,759
If Bailey really wants to show...

1210
00:48:47,760 --> 00:48:49,969
classic feminine choreography,

1211
00:48:49,970 --> 00:48:51,299
I'd be pretty worried.

1212
00:48:51,300 --> 00:48:53,400
I'm not familiar with it at all.

1213
00:48:53,700 --> 00:48:55,240
Yes! Oh, my gosh.

1214
00:48:57,210 --> 00:48:58,309
(The song is fire.)

1215
00:48:58,310 --> 00:48:59,339
Oh, my gosh!

1216
00:48:59,340 --> 00:49:00,480
Oh, yes!

1217
00:49:00,880 --> 00:49:02,679
So that was "Can't Kill Me."

1218
00:49:02,680 --> 00:49:03,779
From the lyrics...

1219
00:49:03,780 --> 00:49:05,149
to the final outro,

1220
00:49:05,150 --> 00:49:07,479
I made it while thinking about the performance the whole time.

1221
00:49:07,480 --> 00:49:08,480
Goodness.

1222
00:49:08,481 --> 00:49:10,849
For the performance. Crazy.

1223
00:49:10,850 --> 00:49:14,589
Working with Bailey taught me this more than anything.

1224
00:49:14,590 --> 00:49:16,959
You have to aim a hundred times...

1225
00:49:16,960 --> 00:49:20,729
above the usual standard.

1226
00:49:20,730 --> 00:49:22,759
Don't use the usual standard as your standard.

1227
00:49:22,760 --> 00:49:24,629
She already created next-level...

1228
00:49:24,630 --> 00:49:27,339
performances and choreography.

1229
00:49:27,340 --> 00:49:28,669
Try thinking a little differently...

1230
00:49:28,670 --> 00:49:31,069
and on a more global scale.

1231
00:49:31,070 --> 00:49:33,239
That might help.

1232
00:49:33,240 --> 00:49:34,579
Bailey is the kind of artist...

1233
00:49:34,580 --> 00:49:37,079
who directs her own performances and makes her own choreography...

1234
00:49:37,080 --> 00:49:39,279
and can carry it all herself as an entertainer.

1235
00:49:39,280 --> 00:49:41,749
Even if these two teams bring something to Bailey,

1236
00:49:41,750 --> 00:49:43,589
would she even like it?

1237
00:49:43,590 --> 00:49:46,359
I feel like Bailey already has it all in her head.

1238
00:49:46,360 --> 00:49:47,719
She's probably already imagining it all.

1239
00:49:47,720 --> 00:49:49,190
Oh, my gosh.

1240
00:49:50,030 --> 00:49:51,530
- Let's go!
- Let's go!

1241
00:49:52,590 --> 00:49:53,659
"Wacka Wak."

1242
00:49:53,660 --> 00:49:55,030
(Wakanda forever)

1243
00:49:57,500 --> 00:49:58,830
(Dancing automatically)

1244
00:49:59,130 --> 00:50:00,700
This one isn't easy either.

1245
00:50:00,840 --> 00:50:02,400
(Getting immersed)

1246
00:50:02,940 --> 00:50:04,539
It's extremely intense.

1247
00:50:04,540 --> 00:50:07,409
I really like TAEYONG's musical style.

1248
00:50:07,410 --> 00:50:10,010
Maybe we can create something that feels new.

1249
00:50:10,210 --> 00:50:12,609
It's a rhythm I'm confident with.

1250
00:50:12,610 --> 00:50:14,319
NaiN and I are both great at...

1251
00:50:14,320 --> 00:50:16,219
making that neo kind of style...

1252
00:50:16,220 --> 00:50:17,319
so we absolutely have to win.

1253
00:50:17,320 --> 00:50:18,989
We are never going to the Last Stage.

1254
00:50:18,990 --> 00:50:21,319
Compared to the other team,

1255
00:50:21,320 --> 00:50:23,259
they may be better at masculine moves,

1256
00:50:23,260 --> 00:50:24,859
but BADA does manly...

1257
00:50:24,860 --> 00:50:26,529
better than men.

1258
00:50:26,530 --> 00:50:27,959
BADA is excited.

1259
00:50:27,960 --> 00:50:29,599
Cool and stylish...

1260
00:50:29,600 --> 00:50:32,130
BADA and I can do that better.

1261
00:50:33,000 --> 00:50:34,840
(Very satisfied)

1262
00:50:35,040 --> 00:50:36,739
When I made it, I really wanted...

1263
00:50:36,740 --> 00:50:39,409
to just cut loose.

1264
00:50:39,410 --> 00:50:41,839
If you don't meet our standard,

1265
00:50:41,840 --> 00:50:43,209
you don't even deserve to jump.

1266
00:50:43,210 --> 00:50:44,710
There are...

1267
00:50:44,850 --> 00:50:46,849
lyrics like that.

1268
00:50:46,850 --> 00:50:49,789
So I want you to really go all out with it.

1269
00:50:49,790 --> 00:50:50,919
Yes!

1270
00:50:50,920 --> 00:50:52,689
TAEYONG likes...

1271
00:50:52,690 --> 00:50:54,459
moves with flavor.

1272
00:50:54,460 --> 00:50:55,490
(Strongly agrees)

1273
00:50:55,720 --> 00:50:57,429
(INGYOO choreographed NCT U's "Baggy Jeans.")

1274
00:50:57,430 --> 00:50:58,959
He won't do it if it isn't cool.

1275
00:50:58,960 --> 00:51:02,129
But if it's too hard, he won't want to do it either.

1276
00:51:02,130 --> 00:51:03,770
(Flustered)

1277
00:51:03,870 --> 00:51:05,269
(The current choreographer agrees.)

1278
00:51:05,270 --> 00:51:06,370
Right.

1279
00:51:06,400 --> 00:51:08,269
We need to balance the difficulty.

1280
00:51:08,270 --> 00:51:09,939
- Easy enough, - Easy enough.

1281
00:51:09,940 --> 00:51:12,239
but still cool.

1282
00:51:12,240 --> 00:51:14,179
You know, keep it smart and clean.

1283
00:51:14,180 --> 00:51:15,209
And he has such a strong...

1284
00:51:15,210 --> 00:51:17,579
character of his own.

1285
00:51:17,580 --> 00:51:20,649
So if there's room to bring his character into it,

1286
00:51:20,650 --> 00:51:22,079
I think he'd like that.

1287
00:51:22,080 --> 00:51:23,450
I'll work hard on it.

1288
00:51:23,990 --> 00:51:25,220
Let's do this.

1289
00:51:25,650 --> 00:51:26,819
- Hi.
- Hi.

1290
00:51:26,820 --> 00:51:29,390
- Hello.
- Hello.

1291
00:51:29,720 --> 00:51:31,089
Goodness.

1292
00:51:31,090 --> 00:51:32,689
I've always been such a huge fan of Bailey.

1293
00:51:32,690 --> 00:51:34,659
I was even more nervous.

1294
00:51:34,660 --> 00:51:35,829
I think it'll be fun.

1295
00:51:35,830 --> 00:51:38,869
She is energetic, smart, and a super dancer.

1296
00:51:38,870 --> 00:51:40,739
She was already a famous dancer.

1297
00:51:40,740 --> 00:51:41,769
She's basically a genius.

1298
00:51:41,770 --> 00:51:42,899
I know her really well.

1299
00:51:42,900 --> 00:51:44,869
We've worked on choreography together before too.

1300
00:51:44,870 --> 00:51:46,210
How are you guys feeling?

1301
00:51:46,680 --> 00:51:48,680
- So nervous.
- Crazy.

1302
00:51:48,880 --> 00:51:50,679
So crazy. I'm shaking.

1303
00:51:50,680 --> 00:51:53,849
- Why are you shaking?
- I practiced...

1304
00:51:53,850 --> 00:51:55,549
everything I was going to say earlier.

1305
00:51:55,550 --> 00:51:56,720
You were nervous.

1306
00:51:58,020 --> 00:51:59,319
Solo artist comeback.

1307
00:51:59,320 --> 00:52:00,959
Solo artist comeback.

1308
00:52:00,960 --> 00:52:01,960
(Bailey practicing her lines)

1309
00:52:01,961 --> 00:52:03,390
To be doing this together...

1310
00:52:03,790 --> 00:52:06,289
I was on the NBC show "World of Dance"...

1311
00:52:06,290 --> 00:52:09,129
maybe two or three times.

1312
00:52:09,130 --> 00:52:11,399
But this is a Korean competition show,

1313
00:52:11,400 --> 00:52:13,169
so I'm in shock.

1314
00:52:13,170 --> 00:52:14,439
I can't remember anything.

1315
00:52:14,440 --> 00:52:16,400
I'm basically frozen right now.

1316
00:52:17,440 --> 00:52:19,269
Is this your first show like this?

1317
00:52:19,270 --> 00:52:20,440
My very first one.

1318
00:52:20,840 --> 00:52:22,610
But I'm such a huge fan.

1319
00:52:23,010 --> 00:52:24,679
(Proud)

1320
00:52:24,680 --> 00:52:26,579
That's Bailey.

1321
00:52:26,580 --> 00:52:27,580
(Swagger mode: ON)

1322
00:52:27,581 --> 00:52:30,049
I think I was probably the first...

1323
00:52:30,050 --> 00:52:33,489
to put her in an SM dancer lineup.

1324
00:52:33,490 --> 00:52:35,660
I was maybe like 15 or 16.

1325
00:52:35,820 --> 00:52:39,129
TAEMIN's "IDEA"...

1326
00:52:39,130 --> 00:52:42,799
and SHINee's "Don't Call Me."

1327
00:52:42,800 --> 00:52:44,999
"Don't Call Me" was choreographed by Bailey and me.

1328
00:52:45,000 --> 00:52:46,469
When I was dancing in the U.S,

1329
00:52:46,470 --> 00:52:48,340
I took classes with them.

1330
00:52:48,700 --> 00:52:50,109
When I was working with Kasper,

1331
00:52:50,110 --> 00:52:51,439
I was finding my own style.

1332
00:52:51,440 --> 00:52:54,609
When I really didn't know anything about the K-pop industry too.

1333
00:52:54,610 --> 00:52:56,549
Some of it was maybe good,

1334
00:52:56,550 --> 00:52:57,879
and some of it was maybe really bad.

1335
00:52:57,880 --> 00:52:59,879
But I think he kind of saw all of that...

1336
00:52:59,880 --> 00:53:01,619
and directed everything really well.

1337
00:53:01,620 --> 00:53:03,519
He is highly capable of seeing somebody and understanding...

1338
00:53:03,520 --> 00:53:04,520
them so fast

1339
00:53:04,521 --> 00:53:06,859
He definitely has a really great understanding of my style.

1340
00:53:06,860 --> 00:53:10,729
I think I'm the one who understands her strengths the best.

1341
00:53:10,730 --> 00:53:13,899
He has a very good understanding of Bailey,

1342
00:53:13,900 --> 00:53:15,229
so that made me nervous.

1343
00:53:15,230 --> 00:53:16,430
I need to stay sharp today.

1344
00:53:17,370 --> 00:53:21,770
I have an extensive experience of stage and solo artists.

1345
00:53:22,000 --> 00:53:24,009
- You know TAEMIN, right?
- Yes.

1346
00:53:24,010 --> 00:53:26,939
I worked with him for a long time and always cared about...

1347
00:53:26,940 --> 00:53:30,379
I was involved...

1348
00:53:30,380 --> 00:53:31,779
from the song camp stage.

1349
00:53:31,780 --> 00:53:33,009
Song camp.

1350
00:53:33,010 --> 00:53:35,820
I may have the most experience out of everyone here.

1351
00:53:36,150 --> 00:53:37,150
What?

1352
00:53:37,151 --> 00:53:39,189
And for a really long time,

1353
00:53:39,190 --> 00:53:41,519
I've hoped Bailey would debut in K-pop someday.

1354
00:53:41,520 --> 00:53:42,789
Really?

1355
00:53:42,790 --> 00:53:44,759
For a really long time. Even when we used to take...

1356
00:53:44,760 --> 00:53:46,529
- classes together.
- Yes.

1357
00:53:46,530 --> 00:53:48,029
He was already so seasoned.

1358
00:53:48,030 --> 00:53:49,759
I thought he was incredible.

1359
00:53:49,760 --> 00:53:51,469
It's my turn to make my pitch.

1360
00:53:51,470 --> 00:53:53,199
This is...

1361
00:53:53,200 --> 00:53:55,740
I started...

1362
00:53:56,500 --> 00:53:58,309
writing songs...

1363
00:53:58,310 --> 00:53:59,469
and recording them. I'm preparing my EP.

1364
00:53:59,470 --> 00:54:00,979
Really?

1365
00:54:00,980 --> 00:54:03,710
Everything I'd been thinking...

1366
00:54:04,010 --> 00:54:07,419
could maybe be distilled and tried here first.

1367
00:54:07,420 --> 00:54:09,179
I have what he's missing.

1368
00:54:09,180 --> 00:54:11,390
And he has what I'm missing.

1369
00:54:12,050 --> 00:54:13,050
We'd make the perfect team.

1370
00:54:13,051 --> 00:54:15,219
And we've both directed projects...

1371
00:54:15,220 --> 00:54:17,329
from pre-production onward.

1372
00:54:17,330 --> 00:54:19,559
So we know how it should be presented to the world.

1373
00:54:19,560 --> 00:54:21,959
It is entering the K-pop market,

1374
00:54:21,960 --> 00:54:24,200
but Bailey doesn't have to fit into that mold.

1375
00:54:24,470 --> 00:54:25,929
I want Bailey to do what Bailey wants to do...

1376
00:54:25,930 --> 00:54:28,670
- What I do want to know is...
- Yes.

1377
00:54:29,040 --> 00:54:30,770
while you were making the song,

1378
00:54:31,240 --> 00:54:34,510
there must be a key image that's clearly stuck in your head.

1379
00:54:35,340 --> 00:54:36,610
There is.

1380
00:54:37,350 --> 00:54:38,779
(Concentrating)

1381
00:54:38,780 --> 00:54:39,850
There is something.

1382
00:54:40,180 --> 00:54:41,180
What is it?

1383
00:54:41,780 --> 00:54:43,849
Can you tell us what it is?

1384
00:54:43,850 --> 00:54:45,119
What kind of tone does she want?

1385
00:54:45,120 --> 00:54:46,489
What does the artist want?

1386
00:54:46,490 --> 00:54:47,890
I think that's most important.

1387
00:54:48,660 --> 00:54:52,159
I grew up dancing hip hop with a bunch of guys.

1388
00:54:52,160 --> 00:54:54,659
I grew up around S-Rank and Kinjaz.

1389
00:54:54,660 --> 00:54:55,759
So that's what I'm comfortable in.

1390
00:54:55,760 --> 00:54:56,929
But at the same time,

1391
00:54:56,930 --> 00:54:59,529
you know, sometimes, I want to put on the heels...

1392
00:54:59,530 --> 00:55:00,700
That's been key for me.

1393
00:55:01,070 --> 00:55:03,170
I think with this song, it needs a little femininity.

1394
00:55:03,770 --> 00:55:06,709
I think vocally, vocal tone-wise, it kind of has...

1395
00:55:06,710 --> 00:55:08,510
a deep femininity to it.

1396
00:55:08,680 --> 00:55:09,680
With Kasper,

1397
00:55:09,681 --> 00:55:11,509
the feminine side is still lacking.

1398
00:55:11,510 --> 00:55:13,549
No one here can really do heels.

1399
00:55:13,550 --> 00:55:16,350
MIN JUN too doesn't have much experience yet.

1400
00:55:16,450 --> 00:55:18,219
I'm quite thrown off right now.

1401
00:55:18,220 --> 00:55:19,789
When it comes to a feminine mood,

1402
00:55:19,790 --> 00:55:21,689
Simeez does it better than me.

1403
00:55:21,690 --> 00:55:23,159
I'm actually good at that stuff.

1404
00:55:23,160 --> 00:55:25,559
With female solo artists,

1405
00:55:25,560 --> 00:55:27,699
you can't go wrong with feminine.

1406
00:55:27,700 --> 00:55:29,860
I'm the one who can crack that.

1407
00:55:31,300 --> 00:55:32,629
But...

1408
00:55:32,630 --> 00:55:36,139
in terms of the instruments,

1409
00:55:36,140 --> 00:55:38,510
it might go on a different direction.

1410
00:55:38,710 --> 00:55:40,279
Right.

1411
00:55:40,280 --> 00:55:41,539
I'll be honest.

1412
00:55:41,540 --> 00:55:42,610
(Listening)

1413
00:55:42,810 --> 00:55:45,010
As a fellow performance director,

1414
00:55:45,310 --> 00:55:47,279
I don't want to direct you.

1415
00:55:47,280 --> 00:55:48,280
Gosh.

1416
00:55:48,281 --> 00:55:50,319
You want to be the creative force.

1417
00:55:50,320 --> 00:55:52,119
When I have to choreograph a different artist,

1418
00:55:52,120 --> 00:55:55,559
I feel like very rarely a choreographer and director...

1419
00:55:55,560 --> 00:55:56,859
- in that table...
- Yes?

1420
00:55:56,860 --> 00:55:58,759
Like "This doesn't work."

1421
00:55:58,760 --> 00:56:00,799
"Do like this." You know.

1422
00:56:00,800 --> 00:56:02,199
That really resonated with me.

1423
00:56:02,200 --> 00:56:03,730
Do whatever you want.

1424
00:56:04,070 --> 00:56:06,430
(Do whatever you want.)

1425
00:56:06,630 --> 00:56:08,139
Take it as far as you want.

1426
00:56:08,140 --> 00:56:10,339
Whether it's like something more isolated,

1427
00:56:10,340 --> 00:56:11,869
or if it's something bigger,

1428
00:56:11,870 --> 00:56:14,340
or if it's feminine or masculine.

1429
00:56:14,440 --> 00:56:16,240
You're 100 percent free.

1430
00:56:17,080 --> 00:56:19,679
I can take my imagination all the way, with no limits.

1431
00:56:19,680 --> 00:56:21,749
I can do anything. "Do whatever you want."

1432
00:56:21,750 --> 00:56:23,179
It almost sounds unreal.

1433
00:56:23,180 --> 00:56:25,749
I thought the possibilities were endless.

1434
00:56:25,750 --> 00:56:26,760
But...

1435
00:56:27,290 --> 00:56:28,290
Generally,

1436
00:56:28,291 --> 00:56:32,160
my taste doesn't really align with the set formula.

1437
00:56:32,290 --> 00:56:33,859
Say yes!

1438
00:56:33,860 --> 00:56:36,299
I wanted to clearly avoid anything stereotypical.

1439
00:56:36,300 --> 00:56:37,400
Now it feels like mine.

1440
00:56:37,570 --> 00:56:38,770
I am confident.

1441
00:56:39,600 --> 00:56:41,900
Wouldn't it be fun if we won?

1442
00:56:42,040 --> 00:56:43,399
I have no intention of going.

1443
00:56:43,400 --> 00:56:44,610
I'm not going.

1444
00:56:44,770 --> 00:56:46,109
In a way, they're the current...

1445
00:56:46,110 --> 00:56:48,379
working choreographers, NaiN and BABYZOO.

1446
00:56:48,380 --> 00:56:51,349
So I wanted to show a little more of what I can do.

1447
00:56:51,350 --> 00:56:53,450
The matchup sounds so fun.

1448
00:56:54,050 --> 00:56:55,149
- Hello.
- Hello.

1449
00:56:55,150 --> 00:56:56,989
- Long time no see.
- Long time no see.

1450
00:56:56,990 --> 00:56:58,089
(They greet the artist, TAEYONG.)

1451
00:56:58,090 --> 00:56:59,249
Nice to see you again.

1452
00:56:59,250 --> 00:57:00,889
- Congrats on first place.
- Thank you.

1453
00:57:00,890 --> 00:57:03,759
The TAEYONG track we worked on together...

1454
00:57:03,760 --> 00:57:06,029
got a pretty good result.

1455
00:57:06,030 --> 00:57:07,830
I think that gave me confidence.

1456
00:57:08,160 --> 00:57:10,670
- The Young versus The Old?
- What?

1457
00:57:11,100 --> 00:57:12,270
Sorry.

1458
00:57:12,670 --> 00:57:13,700
You're right.

1459
00:57:14,200 --> 00:57:16,000
No, I'm sorry.

1460
00:57:17,610 --> 00:57:19,239
I used to get lessons...

1461
00:57:19,240 --> 00:57:21,739
from Koo Young.

1462
00:57:21,740 --> 00:57:23,210
"Mr. Back?"

1463
00:57:23,650 --> 00:57:25,550
Koo Young seems to have really...

1464
00:57:25,650 --> 00:57:28,450
mellowed out these days.

1465
00:57:30,220 --> 00:57:31,950
Why would you say that?

1466
00:57:32,850 --> 00:57:35,690
When Koo Young teaches, he only demonstrates it once.

1467
00:57:35,790 --> 00:57:37,129
He shows it once and says,

1468
00:57:37,130 --> 00:57:38,130
"Practice."

1469
00:57:39,290 --> 00:57:40,299
(Quick demonstration)

1470
00:57:40,300 --> 00:57:41,359
(Do it.)

1471
00:57:41,360 --> 00:57:43,769
Then I just end up standing by the mirror.

1472
00:57:43,770 --> 00:57:45,000
(Oh, dear.)

1473
00:57:45,130 --> 00:57:47,800
And that's how I produced so many great students.

1474
00:57:48,800 --> 00:57:49,899
Of course.

1475
00:57:49,900 --> 00:57:51,309
This is your first time hearing the song today, right?

1476
00:57:51,310 --> 00:57:52,739
- Yes.
- Did you make it?

1477
00:57:52,740 --> 00:57:54,809
I wrote the whole thing myself.

1478
00:57:54,810 --> 00:57:56,139
This place has come alive thanks to the song.

1479
00:57:56,140 --> 00:57:58,109
- Really? That's a relief.
- My dopamine's kicking in.

1480
00:57:58,110 --> 00:57:59,349
He's so fit now.

1481
00:57:59,350 --> 00:58:01,649
Your physique fits this vibe perfectly.

1482
00:58:01,650 --> 00:58:03,080
They were really selling themselves.

1483
00:58:03,180 --> 00:58:04,819
I'll make sure you don't regret it.

1484
00:58:04,820 --> 00:58:06,390
I feel a little threatened.

1485
00:58:07,090 --> 00:58:08,090
NaiN...

1486
00:58:08,290 --> 00:58:09,419
(Me?)

1487
00:58:09,420 --> 00:58:11,759
was never around when I was active.

1488
00:58:11,760 --> 00:58:13,489
She just never showed up. She's the director after all.

1489
00:58:13,490 --> 00:58:14,759
- I...
- She was here the whole time.

1490
00:58:14,760 --> 00:58:16,969
- I was here.
- I see.

1491
00:58:16,970 --> 00:58:18,969
She hasn't paid you much attention.

1492
00:58:18,970 --> 00:58:20,940
I was a little thrown off.

1493
00:58:21,140 --> 00:58:23,399
This time, I'm going all out.

1494
00:58:23,400 --> 00:58:26,269
Honestly, his style might be...

1495
00:58:26,270 --> 00:58:28,109
- the one style I've never tried.
- Yes.

1496
00:58:28,110 --> 00:58:32,679
My lines aren't naturally pretty.

1497
00:58:32,680 --> 00:58:34,080
So I'm a little worried.

1498
00:58:34,380 --> 00:58:38,390
BABYZOO already has that slight Waacking image.

1499
00:58:38,620 --> 00:58:41,759
That is true. My strength is my lines, after all.

1500
00:58:41,760 --> 00:58:43,659
But I'm just as confident...

1501
00:58:43,660 --> 00:58:45,859
with something more hip.

1502
00:58:45,860 --> 00:58:48,299
So maybe I can use that and make it work visually.

1503
00:58:48,300 --> 00:58:50,100
"Wacha Wak" is actually...

1504
00:58:50,200 --> 00:58:51,829
just a sound effect I made up.

1505
00:58:51,830 --> 00:58:54,339
The phrase itself doesn't really mean anything.

1506
00:58:54,340 --> 00:58:55,970
But if you listen to the lyrics,

1507
00:58:56,070 --> 00:58:59,470
the theme is bound to feel intense and flashy.

1508
00:58:59,740 --> 00:59:01,109
It was easier to interpret...

1509
00:59:01,110 --> 00:59:04,009
because the track itself...

1510
00:59:04,010 --> 00:59:06,610
had the same concept as "WYLD," which I made with NaiN.

1511
00:59:06,780 --> 00:59:09,679
For anything with that neon vibe, call NaiN and me.

1512
00:59:09,680 --> 00:59:11,619
So I felt more confident.

1513
00:59:11,620 --> 00:59:14,289
For the chorus, I wanted it to work well...

1514
00:59:14,290 --> 00:59:16,759
as a dance challenge.

1515
00:59:16,760 --> 00:59:17,890
It was game over.

1516
00:59:18,390 --> 00:59:21,030
I'm really good at making challenge choreography.

1517
00:59:21,300 --> 00:59:23,559
TAEYONG was actually the first artist...

1518
00:59:23,560 --> 00:59:25,570
to do my "Smoke" challenge.

1519
00:59:25,730 --> 00:59:28,169
Like with the "Smoke" challenge,

1520
00:59:28,170 --> 00:59:30,739
I think I know what TAEYONG wants...

1521
00:59:30,740 --> 00:59:33,109
and can make choreography that he'll think is cool.

1522
00:59:33,110 --> 00:59:36,679
We worked with TAEYONG recently,

1523
00:59:36,680 --> 00:59:39,009
so I think it's time for us to pull off an upset.

1524
00:59:39,010 --> 00:59:41,379
I thought we had to show it more clearly this time.

1525
00:59:41,380 --> 00:59:43,449
As TAEYONG's choreographer,

1526
00:59:43,450 --> 00:59:44,549
I want him to see why I was there,

1527
00:59:44,550 --> 00:59:46,920
and why Koo Young was there before.

1528
00:59:47,090 --> 00:59:49,820
So I'm putting even more into this mission.

1529
00:59:49,920 --> 00:59:53,959
Now, you'll officially begin creating your choreography.

1530
00:59:53,960 --> 00:59:55,499
Even though this is a team mission.

1531
00:59:55,500 --> 00:59:57,329
In the first creation stage,

1532
00:59:57,330 --> 00:59:59,470
choose a choreographer for each section.

1533
00:59:59,830 --> 01:00:01,499
So it's a section-by-section competition.

1534
01:00:01,500 --> 01:00:03,499
(Oh?)

1535
01:00:03,500 --> 01:00:06,039
With your concept boards and choreography draft videos...

1536
01:00:06,040 --> 01:00:08,709
See you on June 19 at my company's HQ.

1537
01:00:08,710 --> 01:00:11,050
We'll meet at SM Entertainment.

1538
01:00:11,150 --> 01:00:12,949
- Yes!
- Yes!

1539
01:00:12,950 --> 01:00:14,119
(Finally, the day of concept briefing...)

1540
01:00:14,120 --> 01:00:15,719
(and choreography draft video reveal is here.)

1541
01:00:15,720 --> 01:00:17,490
(I'm really looking forward to it, like genuinely.)

1542
01:00:17,590 --> 01:00:18,720
(Loving it)

1543
01:00:18,820 --> 01:00:19,849
(The structure is insane.)

1544
01:00:19,850 --> 01:00:21,489
(We should've made this the title track.)

1545
01:00:21,490 --> 01:00:22,490
(We're screwed, aren't we?)

1546
01:00:22,491 --> 01:00:24,229
(Signature, forehead-flick dance)

1547
01:00:24,230 --> 01:00:25,759
(Is it a move...)

1548
01:00:25,760 --> 01:00:26,789
(people would want to copy?)

1549
01:00:26,790 --> 01:00:28,029
(Actually,)

1550
01:00:28,030 --> 01:00:29,229
(a forehead-flick is a little...)

1551
01:00:29,230 --> 01:00:30,729
(Something new, something cool)

1552
01:00:30,730 --> 01:00:31,799
(That's what's important.)

1553
01:00:31,800 --> 01:00:33,499
(I don't want to force something...)

1554
01:00:33,500 --> 01:00:34,500
(just for a dance challenge.)

1555
01:00:34,570 --> 01:00:36,570
(The chances of having the same...)

1556
01:00:36,670 --> 01:00:38,310
(intro choreography are one in a million.)

1557
01:00:40,110 --> 01:00:42,139
(The quality is really high.)

1558
01:00:42,140 --> 01:00:43,580
(but from a public standpoint,)

1559
01:00:43,680 --> 01:00:44,879
(it doesn't have a strong hook.)

1560
01:00:44,880 --> 01:00:46,979
(The use of the heels is very memorable.)

1561
01:00:46,980 --> 01:00:47,980
(But...)

1562
01:00:48,150 --> 01:00:49,150
(she took the heels off...)

1563
01:00:49,150 --> 01:00:50,150
(and krump?)

1564
01:00:50,151 --> 01:00:51,290
(I don't know if it's working.)

1565
01:00:51,390 --> 01:00:53,490
(Which team will be chosen by TAEYONG and Bailey?)

1566
01:00:54,090 --> 01:00:57,430
I should go back and watch TAEYONG's performances.

1567
01:00:58,260 --> 01:01:00,859
("Baggy Jeans" by NCT U)

1568
01:01:00,860 --> 01:01:03,399
He likes hip hop.

1569
01:01:03,400 --> 01:01:04,400
Yes.

1570
01:01:04,401 --> 01:01:06,270
("SHALALA" by TAEYONG)

1571
01:01:06,730 --> 01:01:08,100
He really dances a lot.

1572
01:01:08,500 --> 01:01:10,100
He likes standout moves,

1573
01:01:10,200 --> 01:01:11,869
but they're unusual.

1574
01:01:11,870 --> 01:01:13,340
("WYLO" by TAEYONG)

1575
01:01:13,510 --> 01:01:14,840
NaiN's recent work.

1576
01:01:15,080 --> 01:01:17,749
NaiN and BABYZOO are basically...

1577
01:01:17,750 --> 01:01:18,950
currently active choreographers.

1578
01:01:19,050 --> 01:01:20,519
So I do feel a little wary.

1579
01:01:20,520 --> 01:01:24,190
But I've actually worked with TAEYONG a lot too.

1580
01:01:24,290 --> 01:01:26,849
We choreographed "ZOO" together,

1581
01:01:26,850 --> 01:01:28,959
worked on his solo tracks,

1582
01:01:28,960 --> 01:01:30,659
and even made challenges together.

1583
01:01:30,660 --> 01:01:33,559
I know a lot of the things...

1584
01:01:33,560 --> 01:01:34,599
TAEYONG tends to like.

1585
01:01:34,600 --> 01:01:37,600
As for TAEYONG, back when he was still a trainee...

1586
01:01:37,700 --> 01:01:39,269
(I used to...)

1587
01:01:39,270 --> 01:01:40,469
(get lessons...)

1588
01:01:40,470 --> 01:01:41,800
(from Mr. Back.)

1589
01:01:41,900 --> 01:01:43,740
("Mr. Back?")

1590
01:01:43,970 --> 01:01:46,109
Koo Young was cool even then. He already had his own style.

1591
01:01:46,110 --> 01:01:48,509
TAEYONG won't do it if it isn't cool.

1592
01:01:48,510 --> 01:01:52,150
But NaiN and BABYZOO have such beautiful lines.

1593
01:01:52,380 --> 01:01:55,979
So I do wonder if that kind of pretty movement fits this song.

1594
01:01:55,980 --> 01:01:59,490
We're still better at more masculine movement.

1595
01:01:59,620 --> 01:02:02,660
We're going to compete with solidity and strength.

1596
01:02:02,760 --> 01:02:05,259
NaiN and BABYZOO are basically currently active choreographers now.

1597
01:02:05,260 --> 01:02:07,629
So I want him to understand why I was there before,

1598
01:02:07,630 --> 01:02:10,529
and why Koo Young was there.

1599
01:02:10,530 --> 01:02:12,999
I think that's different from NaiN and BABYZOO...

1600
01:02:13,000 --> 01:02:14,000
who only met him recently.

1601
01:02:14,200 --> 01:02:17,470
It's time to bring back TAEYONG's dance nostalgia.

1602
01:02:17,740 --> 01:02:20,010
But we still have to live in the present.

1603
01:02:20,310 --> 01:02:22,639
Wouldn't it be better...

1604
01:02:22,640 --> 01:02:23,980
if it had something new to it?

1605
01:02:24,150 --> 01:02:26,679
But they'll probably go hard...

1606
01:02:26,680 --> 01:02:29,750
with big, aggressive moves and things like that.

1607
01:02:29,850 --> 01:02:31,519
I feel like they'll make whole choreography like a picture.

1608
01:02:31,520 --> 01:02:33,489
Koo Young is strong at building those compositions.

1609
01:02:33,490 --> 01:02:36,360
But that might actually work against them.

1610
01:02:36,560 --> 01:02:39,360
Really hard choreography...

1611
01:02:39,960 --> 01:02:43,299
in my opinion, BADA's choreography...

1612
01:02:43,300 --> 01:02:45,100
will probably be very intense.

1613
01:02:45,200 --> 01:02:48,099
But it's also the kind that shines most on BADA.

1614
01:02:48,100 --> 01:02:51,739
So TAEYONG might look at it and think...

1615
01:02:51,740 --> 01:02:55,340
"That only shines when BADA does it."

1616
01:02:55,440 --> 01:02:57,180
I think there's a chance that could happen.

1617
01:02:57,280 --> 01:03:00,080
I don't think he'll want moves...

1618
01:03:00,180 --> 01:03:01,520
that need too much force.

1619
01:03:01,620 --> 01:03:04,949
Rather than moves that feel too fixed...

1620
01:03:04,950 --> 01:03:07,259
I think he'll want something that follows the groove...

1621
01:03:07,260 --> 01:03:09,559
with a few key accents.

1622
01:03:09,560 --> 01:03:10,959
When I was making the draft video for "WYLD,"

1623
01:03:10,960 --> 01:03:12,330
half of it was freestyle.

1624
01:03:12,430 --> 01:03:13,929
Only NaiN can say that because...

1625
01:03:13,930 --> 01:03:16,999
I brought in NaiN, who worked with him recently.

1626
01:03:17,000 --> 01:03:18,570
It's something only NaiN can say.

1627
01:03:18,870 --> 01:03:20,740
We really have to win.

1628
01:03:20,840 --> 01:03:23,699
You know better than anyone how badly I want this.

1629
01:03:23,700 --> 01:03:27,109
BADA and Koo Young have had such great results so far...

1630
01:03:27,110 --> 01:03:29,510
so maybe it's time for them to stumble once.

1631
01:03:30,110 --> 01:03:31,150
Absolutely.

1632
01:03:31,410 --> 01:03:35,320
We'll reveal which director has each section on the other team.

1633
01:03:35,450 --> 01:03:37,450
So it's divided by parts.

1634
01:03:37,950 --> 01:03:39,619
I had a feeling BABYZOO would take the intro.

1635
01:03:39,620 --> 01:03:42,189
Jun Hee got the pre-chorus. Front and back.

1636
01:03:42,190 --> 01:03:45,289
So NaiN leads, and BABYZOO...

1637
01:03:45,290 --> 01:03:46,890
Supports her?

1638
01:03:46,990 --> 01:03:48,999
It would be nice to have the whole framework first.

1639
01:03:49,000 --> 01:03:50,000
Yes.

1640
01:03:50,360 --> 01:03:54,300
The chorus is the most important part to make first.

1641
01:03:54,500 --> 01:03:56,469
So NaiN will take the chorus.

1642
01:03:56,470 --> 01:03:57,470
Leave it to me.

1643
01:03:58,010 --> 01:04:01,909
My choreography is trendy and loose but it still has that cool factor.

1644
01:04:01,910 --> 01:04:04,749
I can make it fit TAEYONG really well.

1645
01:04:04,750 --> 01:04:05,950
I'm confident.

1646
01:04:06,050 --> 01:04:07,849
What does TAEYONG like?

1647
01:04:07,850 --> 01:04:09,019
(This?)

1648
01:04:09,020 --> 01:04:11,349
But I'm hesitant to use big arm swings...

1649
01:04:11,350 --> 01:04:13,090
because it feels too similar to the choreography of "WYLD."

1650
01:04:13,320 --> 01:04:15,320
I want to give him something new.

1651
01:04:15,590 --> 01:04:17,159
What should I bring to him?

1652
01:04:17,160 --> 01:04:18,929
(Agonizing)

1653
01:04:18,930 --> 01:04:19,990
What could it be?

1654
01:04:20,490 --> 01:04:23,160
How well we match his taste is really important.

1655
01:04:23,260 --> 01:04:25,599
Something that can move TAEYONG.

1656
01:04:25,600 --> 01:04:26,899
We need that strategy.

1657
01:04:26,900 --> 01:04:28,539
NaiN, you'll find something that just clicks.

1658
01:04:28,540 --> 01:04:29,740
- Right, right.
- This!

1659
01:04:30,200 --> 01:04:31,740
I'll just throw out a bunch of ideas.

1660
01:04:31,940 --> 01:04:34,510
- "Wak."
- Since it's "Wak, Wak, Wak"...

1661
01:04:34,710 --> 01:04:35,710
If it's "Wak," then...

1662
01:04:35,711 --> 01:04:37,079
It means, "It's not great."

1663
01:04:37,080 --> 01:04:38,810
Right. Gross.

1664
01:04:40,650 --> 01:04:41,720
Or something like this?

1665
01:04:41,820 --> 01:04:43,649
(In perfect sync)

1666
01:04:43,650 --> 01:04:45,519
- This is pretty good.
- You are good.

1667
01:04:45,520 --> 01:04:46,549
That's nice.

1668
01:04:46,550 --> 01:04:48,059
And the head move is good too.

1669
01:04:48,060 --> 01:04:49,860
(Turning the head)

1670
01:04:51,660 --> 01:04:52,789
(Loving it)

1671
01:04:52,790 --> 01:04:53,859
We got it!

1672
01:04:53,860 --> 01:04:57,029
I thought the key was...

1673
01:04:57,030 --> 01:04:58,830
how to make the chorus fun and interesting.

1674
01:04:58,930 --> 01:05:01,500
Swinging the hands from side to side...

1675
01:05:02,800 --> 01:05:04,170
If we find one thing...

1676
01:05:04,270 --> 01:05:06,969
that instantly clicks, I think that's a success.

1677
01:05:06,970 --> 01:05:08,539
I'm absolutely sure about this.

1678
01:05:08,540 --> 01:05:09,910
I think TAEYONG would do this really well.

1679
01:05:10,440 --> 01:05:12,309
And I feel like BADA would do something like...

1680
01:05:12,310 --> 01:05:13,349
(What would BADA do for the chorus?)

1681
01:05:13,350 --> 01:05:14,749
I feel like she'd go for something like this.

1682
01:05:14,750 --> 01:05:16,050
(Laughing)

1683
01:05:16,150 --> 01:05:17,179
Or this.

1684
01:05:17,180 --> 01:05:18,819
(Possessed by BADA)

1685
01:05:18,820 --> 01:05:20,549
I feel like she'd do something like this.

1686
01:05:20,550 --> 01:05:22,220
I think she will hit it like this.

1687
01:05:22,320 --> 01:05:24,660
- Right? Stop, stop.
- Yes.

1688
01:05:24,760 --> 01:05:26,760
(What's BADA's intro chorus move?)

1689
01:05:27,060 --> 01:05:28,860
(Stop)

1690
01:05:28,960 --> 01:05:32,170
(Just as NaiN and BABY ZOO predicted)

1691
01:05:32,370 --> 01:05:33,700
Where were you working on?

1692
01:05:33,900 --> 01:05:35,540
Right here in front.

1693
01:05:35,640 --> 01:05:37,409
A-A-waka-wak

1694
01:05:37,410 --> 01:05:40,940
The song itself is full of swag and really fast...

1695
01:05:41,040 --> 01:05:43,539
but what's a point move...

1696
01:05:43,540 --> 01:05:45,910
that the public would like?

1697
01:05:46,410 --> 01:05:48,479
(For the chorus,)

1698
01:05:48,480 --> 01:05:50,450
(you can't ignore challenges.)

1699
01:05:50,750 --> 01:05:53,449
He brought up challenges himself...

1700
01:05:53,450 --> 01:05:57,559
and I also wanted to make...

1701
01:05:57,560 --> 01:06:00,030
something more approachable.

1702
01:06:00,760 --> 01:06:04,130
The image I have for Chorus One is...

1703
01:06:04,230 --> 01:06:06,900
"Wak" is kind of like... "You're all wack."

1704
01:06:07,000 --> 01:06:09,370
"I'm this. You're all wack."

1705
01:06:09,470 --> 01:06:11,769
(In that sense)

1706
01:06:11,770 --> 01:06:13,610
(Wack)

1707
01:06:14,740 --> 01:06:15,740
A forehead flick?

1708
01:06:16,340 --> 01:06:18,649
Is there anyone in Korea who can't flick a forehead?

1709
01:06:18,650 --> 01:06:21,079
I think anyone could do it easily.

1710
01:06:21,080 --> 01:06:25,120
I want to make this forehead-flick dance work.

1711
01:06:27,190 --> 01:06:29,260
To be completely honest...

1712
01:06:29,660 --> 01:06:31,960
(A forehead flick dance?)

1713
01:06:32,060 --> 01:06:34,830
I kept wondering how to make it work.

1714
01:06:36,060 --> 01:06:38,000
(The next day, they practice with the dancers.)

1715
01:06:39,930 --> 01:06:41,370
(The forehead flick attack makes the dancers fall.)

1716
01:06:41,570 --> 01:06:43,270
(Satisfied)

1717
01:06:43,370 --> 01:06:46,109
He said the dancers at the back...

1718
01:06:46,110 --> 01:06:47,809
would all fall back like this.

1719
01:06:47,810 --> 01:06:50,340
So I thought, "That could be fun."

1720
01:06:50,480 --> 01:06:52,279
Because what I wanted was...

1721
01:06:52,280 --> 01:06:54,549
a strong contrast between...

1722
01:06:54,550 --> 01:06:55,550
TAEYONG and everyone around him.

1723
01:06:56,180 --> 01:06:57,589
(Top tier TAEYONG's forehead flick)

1724
01:06:57,590 --> 01:06:58,819
He only needs to do this.

1725
01:06:58,820 --> 01:07:00,790
The dancers can provide all the energy.

1726
01:07:01,320 --> 01:07:03,620
Once we practiced with dancers, I became sure of it.

1727
01:07:03,720 --> 01:07:06,159
I think Koo Young's killing part...

1728
01:07:06,160 --> 01:07:08,060
is probably the forehead-flick dance.

1729
01:07:09,460 --> 01:07:12,029
Wak, wak, wak, wak, wak.

1730
01:07:12,030 --> 01:07:13,570
I wonder who made that part. Maybe Jun Hee?

1731
01:07:14,840 --> 01:07:16,000
(Wack-a-wak?)

1732
01:07:16,040 --> 01:07:17,040
He's a Waacker.

1733
01:07:17,041 --> 01:07:19,470
(Wack-a-wak?)

1734
01:07:20,640 --> 01:07:22,380
(Did Koo Young guess correctly?)

1735
01:07:22,440 --> 01:07:23,809
If I do this, people will criticize me...

1736
01:07:23,810 --> 01:07:25,450
for adding waacking moves again.

1737
01:07:26,350 --> 01:07:27,550
You know?

1738
01:07:28,050 --> 01:07:31,649
NaiN had such precise data about TAEYONG,

1739
01:07:31,650 --> 01:07:33,649
so I decided to refrain from adding my identity,

1740
01:07:33,650 --> 01:07:35,959
while reflecting her opinions more.

1741
01:07:35,960 --> 01:07:37,289
That way, I could pick...

1742
01:07:37,290 --> 01:07:40,190
the wow points that I liked.

1743
01:07:40,360 --> 01:07:41,629
I haven't...

1744
01:07:41,630 --> 01:07:44,529
(TAEYONG mentioned a flamboyant choreography.)

1745
01:07:44,530 --> 01:07:46,100
(He understands.)

1746
01:07:46,230 --> 01:07:47,399
BABYZOO does...

1747
01:07:47,400 --> 01:07:49,599
such a good job of painting with his body.

1748
01:07:49,600 --> 01:07:51,570
(TAEYONG approved of his arranging ability.)

1749
01:07:52,010 --> 01:07:53,240
In the intro...

1750
01:07:53,340 --> 01:07:56,509
(He had come up with the intro routine.)

1751
01:07:56,510 --> 01:07:58,010
(While practicing with the actual dancers,)

1752
01:07:59,110 --> 01:08:02,179
(he tried the intro routine that he came up with.)

1753
01:08:02,180 --> 01:08:04,120
BABYZOO is...

1754
01:08:04,190 --> 01:08:06,149
known in the industry...

1755
01:08:06,150 --> 01:08:08,559
to do a great job of arranging the wow points...

1756
01:08:08,560 --> 01:08:09,719
in K-pop songs.

1757
01:08:09,720 --> 01:08:11,190
No one can stop us.

1758
01:08:11,260 --> 01:08:12,659
But...

1759
01:08:12,660 --> 01:08:13,660
K-pop in this song?

1760
01:08:13,661 --> 01:08:16,799
(Sharp movements)

1761
01:08:16,800 --> 01:08:17,800
It doesn't suit this song.

1762
01:08:17,801 --> 01:08:19,670
This song is supposed to be performed on stages.

1763
01:08:19,700 --> 01:08:20,770
You have to be able to play.

1764
01:08:20,840 --> 01:08:22,300
There should be energy and krumping.

1765
01:08:22,370 --> 01:08:24,209
But I believed that strong movements...

1766
01:08:24,210 --> 01:08:26,669
might harm the song.

1767
01:08:26,670 --> 01:08:27,679
I expect the other team...

1768
01:08:27,680 --> 01:08:29,340
to focus on theatrical staging.

1769
01:08:30,240 --> 01:08:31,810
(Directing the intro)

1770
01:08:31,880 --> 01:08:34,550
Did you really call everyone else wack?

1771
01:08:34,680 --> 01:08:36,149
That's right.

1772
01:08:36,150 --> 01:08:37,279
BABYZOO...

1773
01:08:37,280 --> 01:08:38,450
and Jo Na In!

1774
01:08:39,590 --> 01:08:40,750
The intro will be...

1775
01:08:40,820 --> 01:08:42,019
like a press conference.

1776
01:08:42,020 --> 01:08:43,020
Everyone else...

1777
01:08:43,020 --> 01:08:44,020
is wack.

1778
01:08:44,021 --> 01:08:47,129
(TAEYONG stirred up trouble by calling people wack.)

1779
01:08:47,130 --> 01:08:48,630
(A press conference is held, and reporters come rushing in.)

1780
01:08:48,700 --> 01:08:49,929
A word, please.

1781
01:08:49,930 --> 01:08:51,169
Then, TAEYONG will...

1782
01:08:51,170 --> 01:08:53,129
(But TAEYONG doesn't care how others react.)

1783
01:08:53,130 --> 01:08:54,699
(A word? You're all wack!)

1784
01:08:54,700 --> 01:08:56,500
(He throws the microphone away and starts dancing.)

1785
01:08:56,600 --> 01:08:59,239
I believe our dance was more intense.

1786
01:08:59,240 --> 01:09:00,569
That could harm the song.

1787
01:09:00,570 --> 01:09:03,509
TAEYONG doesn't prefer meaningless highlights.

1788
01:09:03,510 --> 01:09:05,779
The artist picks it...

1789
01:09:05,780 --> 01:09:06,809
in the end.

1790
01:09:06,810 --> 01:09:09,349
The artist has to look cool...

1791
01:09:09,350 --> 01:09:10,749
when he does the dance.

1792
01:09:10,750 --> 01:09:13,020
We approached it with sensitivity and detail.

1793
01:09:13,550 --> 01:09:15,359
We came here for a reason.

1794
01:09:15,360 --> 01:09:16,860
We're both good at creating choreography.

1795
01:09:16,920 --> 01:09:19,790
We have the great choreographer from SM Entertainment.

1796
01:09:19,860 --> 01:09:21,759
And another choreographer from SM...

1797
01:09:21,760 --> 01:09:23,000
who's trying to follow in his footsteps.

1798
01:09:23,230 --> 01:09:24,529
Our chance of winning?

1799
01:09:24,530 --> 01:09:26,330
Probably 99 percent.

1800
01:09:26,400 --> 01:09:28,540
It's so obvious that we'll win this time,

1801
01:09:28,600 --> 01:09:29,969
but we want to win by a landslide.

1802
01:09:29,970 --> 01:09:32,710
(Which will TAEYONG pick?)

1803
01:09:32,740 --> 01:09:33,909
Their pride is on the line.

1804
01:09:33,910 --> 01:09:34,910
Except for MIN JUN,

1805
01:09:34,911 --> 01:09:37,310
they're the people who do this professionally.

1806
01:09:37,340 --> 01:09:38,510
I hope we do well.

1807
01:09:38,580 --> 01:09:39,580
If we lose,

1808
01:09:39,581 --> 01:09:41,349
we're done in this industry.

1809
01:09:41,350 --> 01:09:43,319
It's my profession, after all.

1810
01:09:43,320 --> 01:09:44,449
There's no way...

1811
01:09:44,450 --> 01:09:45,790
we're losing this.

1812
01:09:45,820 --> 01:09:47,520
(BAILEY's matchup: INGYOO and Simeez versus Kasper and MIN JUN)

1813
01:09:47,660 --> 01:09:48,760
(MIN JUN and Kasper's first meeting)

1814
01:09:49,060 --> 01:09:51,190
(The two listen to music without speaking.)

1815
01:09:51,930 --> 01:09:54,229
I never thought of working with Kasper,

1816
01:09:54,230 --> 01:09:56,360
and I didn't know him that well.

1817
01:09:56,430 --> 01:09:57,969
They've proven themselves,

1818
01:09:57,970 --> 01:09:59,230
and they're famous.

1819
01:09:59,300 --> 01:10:00,300
I guess they didn't pick me...

1820
01:10:00,301 --> 01:10:01,599
because they thought...

1821
01:10:01,600 --> 01:10:04,040
I was incompetent in the K-pop industry.

1822
01:10:04,070 --> 01:10:05,109
I thought...

1823
01:10:05,110 --> 01:10:07,140
I might be a burden to Kasper.

1824
01:10:07,740 --> 01:10:10,210
It was unsettling and difficult.

1825
01:10:10,580 --> 01:10:12,010
I'll do my best.

1826
01:10:12,510 --> 01:10:14,110
I'm just too worried.

1827
01:10:14,180 --> 01:10:15,749
No, I'm not worried about you.

1828
01:10:15,750 --> 01:10:16,779
Not at all.

1829
01:10:16,780 --> 01:10:17,789
I'm...

1830
01:10:17,790 --> 01:10:19,049
- No.
- worried, though.

1831
01:10:19,050 --> 01:10:20,349
Don't even think that.

1832
01:10:20,350 --> 01:10:21,990
As the missions went on,

1833
01:10:22,320 --> 01:10:25,230
he was the only one who constantly picked Hash.

1834
01:10:25,590 --> 01:10:28,130
It wasn't enough to convince me.

1835
01:10:28,200 --> 01:10:30,399
I don't think he utilized...

1836
01:10:30,400 --> 01:10:31,930
every dancer's character.

1837
01:10:32,000 --> 01:10:34,069
It's the Title Sequence Film Mission,

1838
01:10:34,070 --> 01:10:35,940
and the quality is ambiguous.

1839
01:10:36,000 --> 01:10:37,640
What about you, then?

1840
01:10:37,770 --> 01:10:39,239
He used to criticize me too.

1841
01:10:39,240 --> 01:10:40,909
So, I thought our preferences might be different.

1842
01:10:40,910 --> 01:10:41,980
I was worried...

1843
01:10:42,080 --> 01:10:43,780
that he wouldn't like me.

1844
01:10:44,080 --> 01:10:45,610
I believe...

1845
01:10:45,980 --> 01:10:47,679
you have a unique color...

1846
01:10:47,680 --> 01:10:50,020
that only you can show and no one else can.

1847
01:10:50,050 --> 01:10:53,519
For instance, I've been working with solo artists for too long.

1848
01:10:53,520 --> 01:10:55,519
TAEMIN, BAEKHYUN,

1849
01:10:55,520 --> 01:10:57,059
LAY, KEY,

1850
01:10:57,060 --> 01:10:58,060
and everyone.

1851
01:10:58,061 --> 01:10:59,789
I've only been working with them...

1852
01:10:59,790 --> 01:11:00,830
(Acting cocky again)

1853
01:11:00,930 --> 01:11:02,959
I directed their themes...

1854
01:11:02,960 --> 01:11:04,370
and even their outfits.

1855
01:11:04,900 --> 01:11:06,929
The cover of the album, how many we're going to release...

1856
01:11:06,930 --> 01:11:08,369
and which contractor we'll pick...

1857
01:11:08,370 --> 01:11:10,339
I couldn't fully trust him,

1858
01:11:10,340 --> 01:11:11,469
but if he was telling the truth,

1859
01:11:11,470 --> 01:11:13,109
he must have lots of data about this.

1860
01:11:13,110 --> 01:11:15,710
I thought I should believe him.

1861
01:11:15,810 --> 01:11:17,539
My trust in Kasper...

1862
01:11:17,540 --> 01:11:18,849
went from 0 to 40 percent...

1863
01:11:18,850 --> 01:11:20,349
after listening to him.

1864
01:11:20,350 --> 01:11:22,619
We need something that BAILEY wants.

1865
01:11:22,620 --> 01:11:23,919
In the end,

1866
01:11:23,920 --> 01:11:25,919
if the artist wants it,

1867
01:11:25,920 --> 01:11:27,219
that's it.

1868
01:11:27,220 --> 01:11:29,359
It's our job to make it that way.

1869
01:11:29,360 --> 01:11:31,690
I think it's impossible to lose to them.

1870
01:11:31,890 --> 01:11:32,930
Arrangements?

1871
01:11:32,990 --> 01:11:35,099
INGYOO and Hee Jung are...

1872
01:11:35,100 --> 01:11:37,099
so sure they're good at dance arrangement,

1873
01:11:37,100 --> 01:11:38,730
but that's my best quality.

1874
01:11:38,830 --> 01:11:40,369
And we have to win...

1875
01:11:40,370 --> 01:11:42,240
to make this more interesting.

1876
01:11:42,270 --> 01:11:44,739
That's true. It'll be interesting if those two go to the Last Stage.

1877
01:11:44,740 --> 01:11:46,469
Simeez, INGYOO, BADA, and Koo Young.

1878
01:11:46,470 --> 01:11:48,409
These four have to go to the Last Stage to make it fun.

1879
01:11:48,410 --> 01:11:50,509
If you go to the Last Stage twice, it's boring.

1880
01:11:50,510 --> 01:11:52,510
- I'm serious.
- It'll be boring for me too.

1881
01:11:52,610 --> 01:11:54,750
I don't think I can lose to them.

1882
01:11:55,150 --> 01:11:58,289
I'm the one who's been making the artists shine from behind.

1883
01:11:58,290 --> 01:12:00,050
I'm definitely going to win.

1884
01:12:00,090 --> 01:12:01,119
(Laughing)

1885
01:12:01,120 --> 01:12:03,619
I'm teaming up with Simeez.

1886
01:12:03,620 --> 01:12:04,690
I'm certain we'll win.

1887
01:12:04,760 --> 01:12:06,659
I've created choreography with him a few times.

1888
01:12:06,660 --> 01:12:10,430
I worked on "The Rizzness" by TAEMIN with him.

1889
01:12:10,500 --> 01:12:11,700
He's the best choreographer.

1890
01:12:11,800 --> 01:12:13,569
I think he makes them the most eye-catching...

1891
01:12:13,570 --> 01:12:15,370
among male choreographers.

1892
01:12:15,770 --> 01:12:17,769
I'm in charge of IVE from Starship Entertainment...

1893
01:12:17,770 --> 01:12:19,909
from the pre-production stage.

1894
01:12:19,910 --> 01:12:21,079
I have that experience.

1895
01:12:21,080 --> 01:12:22,310
We're going to win this.

1896
01:12:25,750 --> 01:12:26,779
(This is Simeez.)

1897
01:12:26,780 --> 01:12:27,949
Hang on.

1898
01:12:27,950 --> 01:12:28,950
(Falling)

1899
01:12:28,951 --> 01:12:30,749
(Laughing)

1900
01:12:30,750 --> 01:12:32,849
(What happened to INGYOO and Simeez?)

1901
01:12:32,850 --> 01:12:34,520
- Come outside.
- I wish I could.

1902
01:12:34,920 --> 01:12:36,890
Our main theme is...

1903
01:12:36,920 --> 01:12:38,790
- Do you know what Hydra is?
- I do.

1904
01:12:38,860 --> 01:12:40,260
It's a monster in Greek mythology.

1905
01:12:40,330 --> 01:12:41,429
She gives off that aura.

1906
01:12:41,430 --> 01:12:43,529
Hydra is the symbol of immortality and evolution.

1907
01:12:43,530 --> 01:12:45,900
They say Hydra is close to a systematic catastrophe.

1908
01:12:46,270 --> 01:12:47,939
But I feel like a systematic catastrophe...

1909
01:12:47,940 --> 01:12:49,699
is what BAILEY wants.

1910
01:12:49,700 --> 01:12:52,239
The appearance of a character that's never been here before.

1911
01:12:52,240 --> 01:12:53,469
You know, people call it...

1912
01:12:53,470 --> 01:12:55,439
a monster rookie.

1913
01:12:55,440 --> 01:12:56,609
Someone that never dies.

1914
01:12:56,610 --> 01:12:59,009
After all, the title is "Can't Kill Me."

1915
01:12:59,010 --> 01:13:01,009
The theme is a monster that only grows stronger...

1916
01:13:01,010 --> 01:13:02,450
every time you try to kill it.

1917
01:13:02,650 --> 01:13:03,980
In the intro,

1918
01:13:04,080 --> 01:13:05,389
Hydra Queen goes...

1919
01:13:05,390 --> 01:13:06,849
(Simeez will direct the intro.)

1920
01:13:06,850 --> 01:13:07,959
Before its birth,

1921
01:13:07,960 --> 01:13:09,220
and it's born.

1922
01:13:09,290 --> 01:13:11,020
(Was it successful?)

1923
01:13:11,090 --> 01:13:13,259
I wanted to express its transformation.

1924
01:13:13,260 --> 01:13:14,460
And we push.

1925
01:13:15,830 --> 01:13:17,259
I bet BAILEY wants...

1926
01:13:17,260 --> 01:13:18,869
to do something she's never done before.

1927
01:13:18,870 --> 01:13:20,069
If I were the artist,

1928
01:13:20,070 --> 01:13:23,400
I would want something that no K-pop choreographer has done.

1929
01:13:23,470 --> 01:13:25,439
But it has to be recognized by people,

1930
01:13:25,440 --> 01:13:26,440
while having a kick,

1931
01:13:26,441 --> 01:13:27,980
while being able to show off my abilities,

1932
01:13:28,010 --> 01:13:29,309
while being conceptual art,

1933
01:13:29,310 --> 01:13:30,510
while being the one and only.

1934
01:13:30,780 --> 01:13:31,879
I thought about it,

1935
01:13:31,880 --> 01:13:34,009
and I decided to use objets...

1936
01:13:34,010 --> 01:13:36,420
since I had experience.

1937
01:13:36,580 --> 01:13:38,019
(Ta-da)

1938
01:13:38,020 --> 01:13:40,390
We're in Dongdaemun...

1939
01:13:40,450 --> 01:13:42,220
to check out some fabric.

1940
01:13:42,820 --> 01:13:44,989
I wouldn't call it fabric.

1941
01:13:44,990 --> 01:13:47,390
I was thinking of a sort of film...

1942
01:13:47,430 --> 01:13:49,100
that sticks to your body.

1943
01:13:49,530 --> 01:13:51,930
Finding the right material isn't as it looks.

1944
01:13:52,330 --> 01:13:55,200
If we go with white, we can paint veins on it.

1945
01:13:55,300 --> 01:13:57,670
If we go with black, it'll set the mood.

1946
01:13:57,910 --> 01:14:00,639
(Simeez gives it a go.)

1947
01:14:00,640 --> 01:14:01,839
You're pretty.

1948
01:14:01,840 --> 01:14:02,910
(Laughing)

1949
01:14:04,440 --> 01:14:06,209
I like the red one.

1950
01:14:06,210 --> 01:14:07,280
Put it on.

1951
01:14:08,420 --> 01:14:12,750
I thought it would look more bizarre than black.

1952
01:14:12,820 --> 01:14:15,090
We'll use red fabric to express its birth.

1953
01:14:15,890 --> 01:14:17,219
I'm feeling it.

1954
01:14:17,220 --> 01:14:18,530
Look at me.

1955
01:14:18,630 --> 01:14:20,459
That's not bad. But if we're not careful,

1956
01:14:20,460 --> 01:14:22,530
it might look a bit funny.

1957
01:14:22,600 --> 01:14:25,769
(She tries dancing in the material.)

1958
01:14:25,770 --> 01:14:29,270
(Something like this?)

1959
01:14:29,800 --> 01:14:31,540
Not bad.

1960
01:14:32,070 --> 01:14:33,640
It's pretty. It's not that bad.

1961
01:14:33,970 --> 01:14:35,979
The performance that we have in mind is...

1962
01:14:35,980 --> 01:14:37,849
pretty conceptual.

1963
01:14:37,850 --> 01:14:40,849
I wanted to create a different image,

1964
01:14:40,850 --> 01:14:42,580
and I'm glad it came out well.

1965
01:14:43,120 --> 01:14:44,819
(They finally check the other team's section.)

1966
01:14:44,820 --> 01:14:46,220
That's how they did it?

1967
01:14:46,820 --> 01:14:48,960
We got something called Section Directors.

1968
01:14:49,020 --> 01:14:51,459
The first verse... At least it won't interrupt the flow.

1969
01:14:51,460 --> 01:14:53,090
The sections are largely divided.

1970
01:14:53,160 --> 01:14:54,460
It's a dance buildup.

1971
01:14:54,630 --> 01:14:57,300
I didn't expect MIN JUN to get the outro.

1972
01:14:57,400 --> 01:15:00,199
I thought Kasper would want the outro.

1973
01:15:00,200 --> 01:15:01,469
MIN JUN might do a good job.

1974
01:15:01,470 --> 01:15:02,540
I'm sure he will.

1975
01:15:02,570 --> 01:15:03,599
I wonder what he'll do.

1976
01:15:03,600 --> 01:15:06,210
I'm looking forward to seeing his outro.

1977
01:15:06,370 --> 01:15:08,079
When the sections were assigned,

1978
01:15:08,080 --> 01:15:09,109
there was a part...

1979
01:15:09,110 --> 01:15:10,640
that I was confident in.

1980
01:15:10,780 --> 01:15:13,150
Is there a section you really want?

1981
01:15:13,450 --> 01:15:15,920
The parts that I can clearly picture are...

1982
01:15:16,020 --> 01:15:17,779
the second verse...

1983
01:15:17,780 --> 01:15:19,590
- and the outro.
- Okay.

1984
01:15:19,720 --> 01:15:22,219
I have a clear picture in mind...

1985
01:15:22,220 --> 01:15:23,690
in terms of choreography.

1986
01:15:24,160 --> 01:15:26,359
The beat gets louder in the outro...

1987
01:15:26,360 --> 01:15:27,589
as they dance,

1988
01:15:27,590 --> 01:15:30,160
so I believe that's where his strength will shine.

1989
01:15:30,360 --> 01:15:32,330
- Before we meet tomorrow, - Yes.

1990
01:15:32,400 --> 01:15:33,830
let's complete most of it.

1991
01:15:33,970 --> 01:15:35,839
I don't know what your style is,

1992
01:15:35,840 --> 01:15:38,240
but I hate one-dimensional choreography.

1993
01:15:38,310 --> 01:15:39,909
I dislike nodding...

1994
01:15:39,910 --> 01:15:41,140
when you're supposed to nod in a part.

1995
01:15:41,210 --> 01:15:43,240
I'd like it to be a bit abstract.

1996
01:15:43,340 --> 01:15:46,610
(MIN JUN studies ALLDAY PROJECT's videos.)

1997
01:15:46,950 --> 01:15:48,680
K-pop isn't my strength,

1998
01:15:48,750 --> 01:15:50,019
so I can't decide.

1999
01:15:50,020 --> 01:15:53,750
I have to keep popularity in mind when I'm creating it.

2000
01:15:53,850 --> 01:15:55,759
I can't seem to come up with one.

2001
01:15:55,760 --> 01:15:57,320
My mind keeps going blank.

2002
01:15:57,590 --> 01:15:59,060
How far along are you?

2003
01:15:59,230 --> 01:16:01,189
(He can't seem to answer.)

2004
01:16:01,190 --> 01:16:03,160
I keep hitting a wall.

2005
01:16:04,230 --> 01:16:06,069
Show me the overall choreo,

2006
01:16:06,070 --> 01:16:07,970
thinking you're reminding yourself.

2007
01:16:08,500 --> 01:16:11,339
(MIN JUN shows him the pre-chorus that he came up with.)

2008
01:16:11,340 --> 01:16:14,470
It showed his inexperience.

2009
01:16:14,540 --> 01:16:16,140
I thought his feet were on fire.

2010
01:16:16,180 --> 01:16:18,080
He couldn't keep them still.

2011
01:16:18,180 --> 01:16:19,180
He was like...

2012
01:16:19,181 --> 01:16:22,880
(Fluttering and stomping)

2013
01:16:23,050 --> 01:16:25,119
He did the dance he did on his knees in the 1-on-1 Signature Mission...

2014
01:16:25,120 --> 01:16:26,220
only on his feet this time.

2015
01:16:26,390 --> 01:16:28,459
Here's what I think.

2016
01:16:28,460 --> 01:16:30,159
In the first "started" part,

2017
01:16:30,160 --> 01:16:32,129
it's quite similar to the one...

2018
01:16:32,130 --> 01:16:34,460
- you did in the first mission.
- Yes.

2019
01:16:34,490 --> 01:16:35,760
- You noticed it too, right?
- Yes.

2020
01:16:35,960 --> 01:16:37,500
That part could be...

2021
01:16:37,630 --> 01:16:38,729
I'll show you an example.

2022
01:16:38,730 --> 01:16:39,870
What was the exact dance?

2023
01:16:40,230 --> 01:16:42,240
Rather than going hard like this...

2024
01:16:42,500 --> 01:16:44,609
The outro, pre-chorus, and the chorus...

2025
01:16:44,610 --> 01:16:46,070
all looked the same.

2026
01:16:46,110 --> 01:16:47,509
I taught him...

2027
01:16:47,510 --> 01:16:49,079
which parts to leave out and how to change them...

2028
01:16:49,080 --> 01:16:50,880
on the spot.

2029
01:16:50,980 --> 01:16:52,109
Do you want to try the left hand?

2030
01:16:52,110 --> 01:16:53,180
Keep your right hand still.

2031
01:16:53,310 --> 01:16:57,520
(They keep revising the pre-chorus choreography.)

2032
01:16:57,550 --> 01:17:00,049
You can fully enjoy fried chicken if it's the only thing on the table.

2033
01:17:00,050 --> 01:17:01,249
But if there's fried chicken, tteokbokki,

2034
01:17:01,250 --> 01:17:02,720
jjajangmyeon, tangsuyuk,

2035
01:17:02,790 --> 01:17:03,889
and fried rice,

2036
01:17:03,890 --> 01:17:05,329
you can't decide what to eat.

2037
01:17:05,330 --> 01:17:06,330
So, I went,

2038
01:17:06,331 --> 01:17:08,960
"MIN JUN, I think we should eat jjajangmyeon today."

2039
01:17:09,260 --> 01:17:11,500
"Eat this." That was what I did.

2040
01:17:11,630 --> 01:17:12,800
You're good.

2041
01:17:12,900 --> 01:17:14,529
- Thank you.
- It's good.

2042
01:17:14,530 --> 01:17:15,940
I was so worried.

2043
01:17:16,100 --> 01:17:17,300
I'm here for you.

2044
01:17:18,040 --> 01:17:20,140
The buildup looks way better, thanks to you.

2045
01:17:21,610 --> 01:17:23,039
I wasn't sure if my choreography was good or not...

2046
01:17:23,040 --> 01:17:24,680
because I didn't have much experience.

2047
01:17:25,250 --> 01:17:27,710
But he complimented me a lot.

2048
01:17:28,080 --> 01:17:29,149
(A thumbs-up)

2049
01:17:29,150 --> 01:17:31,120
It looks better with a different texture.

2050
01:17:31,620 --> 01:17:33,819
This is how we normally do it. We change it bit by bit.

2051
01:17:33,820 --> 01:17:34,820
He said I did a good job.

2052
01:17:34,821 --> 01:17:37,719
Not only did he trust me, he also supported me.

2053
01:17:37,720 --> 01:17:40,690
My trust in him is up to 70 percent now.

2054
01:17:41,400 --> 01:17:44,199
This mission is practically what I do for a living,

2055
01:17:44,200 --> 01:17:46,070
so I can never lose.

2056
01:17:46,830 --> 01:17:47,930
It's what he does for a living?

2057
01:17:48,340 --> 01:17:51,000
What I'm doing is what I do for a living.

2058
01:17:51,170 --> 01:17:52,269
It was all thanks to the artist?

2059
01:17:52,270 --> 01:17:53,569
("like JENNIE" would have been a success,)

2060
01:17:53,570 --> 01:17:54,910
(no matter who directed it.)

2061
01:17:55,510 --> 01:17:56,580
He thought wrong.

2062
01:17:56,680 --> 01:17:58,910
I'm going to prove him wrong this time.

2063
01:17:59,150 --> 01:18:01,880
(Who will win in the end?)

2064
01:18:02,520 --> 01:18:04,080
There are so many new clothes, Na In.

2065
01:18:04,650 --> 01:18:06,420
They renew them every time.

2066
01:18:06,590 --> 01:18:07,719
It's what we wore yesterday.

2067
01:18:07,720 --> 01:18:09,259
For the draft proposal?

2068
01:18:09,260 --> 01:18:11,659
I could move really well in it when I danced.

2069
01:18:11,660 --> 01:18:12,790
It's cool.

2070
01:18:12,930 --> 01:18:15,060
Did they have these short jeans?

2071
01:18:15,460 --> 01:18:17,600
This screams, "BABYZOO."

2072
01:18:17,730 --> 01:18:19,770
- I can wear it on top of pants.
- Totally.

2073
01:18:20,630 --> 01:18:22,640
Is this what the other team wore?

2074
01:18:23,070 --> 01:18:24,099
Yes.

2075
01:18:24,100 --> 01:18:25,869
(The windbreaker that BADA and Koo Young wore)

2076
01:18:25,870 --> 01:18:27,369
(I'll try it on too.)

2077
01:18:27,370 --> 01:18:28,510
It's cute.

2078
01:18:29,310 --> 01:18:30,379
Isn't it?

2079
01:18:30,380 --> 01:18:31,380
(Does it suit me?)

2080
01:18:33,650 --> 01:18:34,779
You started dancing out of nowhere.

2081
01:18:34,780 --> 01:18:36,579
(He's excited because it looks good on him.)

2082
01:18:36,580 --> 01:18:37,649
(In love with himself)

2083
01:18:37,650 --> 01:18:39,020
There's one that I've been dying to wear.

2084
01:18:39,350 --> 01:18:40,449
- This one.
- I like it.

2085
01:18:40,450 --> 01:18:41,460
(The windbreaker that Na In picked)

2086
01:18:41,590 --> 01:18:42,820
This is yours.

2087
01:18:43,060 --> 01:18:44,759
(How do I look?)

2088
01:18:44,760 --> 01:18:45,760
Cute.

2089
01:18:45,761 --> 01:18:46,789
(I love it.)

2090
01:18:46,790 --> 01:18:48,629
It's pretty loose.

2091
01:18:48,630 --> 01:18:49,759
Like that?

2092
01:18:49,760 --> 01:18:50,859
(She tightens the hem drawstring.)

2093
01:18:50,860 --> 01:18:51,900
I like it.

2094
01:18:52,230 --> 01:18:53,429
That's a good point.

2095
01:18:53,430 --> 01:18:55,100
(It even goes well with the choreography.)

2096
01:18:55,340 --> 01:18:56,440
Nice.

2097
01:18:57,100 --> 01:18:58,569
Now that we have done some shopping,

2098
01:18:58,570 --> 01:19:00,039
why don't we move on to the next mission?

2099
01:19:00,040 --> 01:19:01,409
- All right.
- Let's go.

2100
01:19:01,410 --> 01:19:04,540
(Good luck, stylish NaiN and BABYZOO.)

2101
01:19:05,480 --> 01:19:07,150
Let's get some practice.

2102
01:19:07,510 --> 01:19:10,450
I just need to complete the outro and come up with a bridge.

2103
01:19:10,720 --> 01:19:12,390
We'll film the draft based on those.

2104
01:19:12,920 --> 01:19:15,759
Here's my idea for the second verse.

2105
01:19:15,760 --> 01:19:17,490
I wanted to play with the lyrics.

2106
01:19:17,820 --> 01:19:19,829
I had already come up with the second verse,

2107
01:19:19,830 --> 01:19:22,160
but I didn't want to stop his passion.

2108
01:19:22,260 --> 01:19:23,799
So, I decided...

2109
01:19:23,800 --> 01:19:25,030
to let him do what he wanted.

2110
01:19:25,130 --> 01:19:27,129
My sections are the second verse,

2111
01:19:27,130 --> 01:19:29,870
the 2nd pre-chorus, the 2nd chorus, and the outro.

2112
01:19:30,070 --> 01:19:33,140
That's how I made the dance for the second verse.

2113
01:19:33,310 --> 01:19:34,409
Stay here,

2114
01:19:34,410 --> 01:19:36,579
and you come down as you shake.

2115
01:19:36,580 --> 01:19:37,980
(Dancing hard)

2116
01:19:38,080 --> 01:19:39,180
Is this a prank?

2117
01:19:39,880 --> 01:19:41,650
(Laughing)

2118
01:19:41,750 --> 01:19:44,119
Kind of like Lady Gaga.

2119
01:19:44,120 --> 01:19:45,120
(Okay.)

2120
01:19:45,121 --> 01:19:48,560
If all our angles line up,

2121
01:19:48,720 --> 01:19:51,630
it will look pretty cool. That was my imagination.

2122
01:19:51,730 --> 01:19:52,989
Do we move our elbows or not?

2123
01:19:52,990 --> 01:19:54,629
Keep your elbows still, and only use your wrists.

2124
01:19:54,630 --> 01:19:55,730
- Just our wrists?
- Yes.

2125
01:19:57,000 --> 01:19:59,300
It was a new type of choreography.

2126
01:19:59,530 --> 01:20:00,600
But...

2127
01:20:00,870 --> 01:20:02,540
Seven, eight, and...

2128
01:20:03,400 --> 01:20:04,669
(Confused with the timing)

2129
01:20:04,670 --> 01:20:08,069
Six, seven, eight, and one. I guess it's this.

2130
01:20:08,070 --> 01:20:09,740
- Yes.
- Eight, and one.

2131
01:20:10,080 --> 01:20:11,479
That's how you do it.

2132
01:20:11,480 --> 01:20:13,610
It'd be great if you came all the way here.

2133
01:20:13,710 --> 01:20:15,949
- If not, we can form...
- We can.

2134
01:20:15,950 --> 01:20:17,520
two lines.

2135
01:20:17,720 --> 01:20:19,990
Sorry, this wasn't the formation that I had in mind.

2136
01:20:20,650 --> 01:20:22,920
(Hesitant)

2137
01:20:22,990 --> 01:20:24,019
Three...

2138
01:20:24,020 --> 01:20:25,629
(He can't give them clear directions.)

2139
01:20:25,630 --> 01:20:27,889
He seemed to lack confidence.

2140
01:20:27,890 --> 01:20:30,360
He also seemed unsure.

2141
01:20:30,560 --> 01:20:32,999
- Inside...
- If you want to stick to it...

2142
01:20:33,000 --> 01:20:34,030
Yes?

2143
01:20:34,270 --> 01:20:35,799
I don't think Ye Hwan and I should be the ones...

2144
01:20:35,800 --> 01:20:37,699
coming forward while grabbing their shoulders.

2145
01:20:37,700 --> 01:20:39,510
- It should be these two.
- Okay.

2146
01:20:40,570 --> 01:20:43,840
Kasper mostly led practice.

2147
01:20:44,210 --> 01:20:47,180
I know that I should show them a cool choreography...

2148
01:20:47,250 --> 01:20:49,049
and be able to lead them...

2149
01:20:49,050 --> 01:20:50,949
as a director,

2150
01:20:50,950 --> 01:20:52,390
but it didn't go my way.

2151
01:20:52,490 --> 01:20:55,820
I'm upset that I failed to give them detailed directions.

2152
01:20:57,220 --> 01:20:58,329
(Simeez and INGYOO's draft shoot)

2153
01:20:58,330 --> 01:20:59,660
(Simeez and INGYOO rehearse before the shoot.)

2154
01:21:00,160 --> 01:21:02,199
(Simeez plays BAILEY, the artist,)

2155
01:21:02,200 --> 01:21:04,200
(and WE DEM BOYZ is the dance team for the draft?)

2156
01:21:04,300 --> 01:21:06,599
If I were BAILEY's director,

2157
01:21:06,600 --> 01:21:08,640
I would never put a female dancer next to her.

2158
01:21:08,870 --> 01:21:11,270
I agree. I'd rather put her there by herself.

2159
01:21:11,440 --> 01:21:12,870
But I'm concerned...

2160
01:21:13,270 --> 01:21:16,580
that no male dancer can do this type of dance.

2161
01:21:16,780 --> 01:21:18,350
You're looking for a wild man.

2162
01:21:18,510 --> 01:21:20,209
I need Vata to do it.

2163
01:21:20,210 --> 01:21:22,720
AHOB is pretty good at that too. You know, wild movements.

2164
01:21:22,920 --> 01:21:24,279
Kamel's good too.

2165
01:21:24,280 --> 01:21:25,490
He crawls around like a dog.

2166
01:21:26,320 --> 01:21:27,449
(They practice the 2nd pre-chorus...)

2167
01:21:27,450 --> 01:21:28,790
(after the 1st verse.)

2168
01:21:29,160 --> 01:21:30,620
(The heels won't come off easily.)

2169
01:21:31,020 --> 01:21:33,129
It's the part where the artist takes her heels off.

2170
01:21:33,130 --> 01:21:35,360
She couldn't take them off.

2171
01:21:35,860 --> 01:21:37,729
She has to hand over the microphone,

2172
01:21:37,730 --> 01:21:38,769
take her heels off,

2173
01:21:38,770 --> 01:21:41,599
and the microphone has to go around and return to her.

2174
01:21:41,600 --> 01:21:43,840
The timing was off.

2175
01:21:44,040 --> 01:21:45,109
Get the microphone!

2176
01:21:45,110 --> 01:21:47,110
I wasn't so sure it would work.

2177
01:21:47,510 --> 01:21:48,979
You have to move your heels with your right hand...

2178
01:21:48,980 --> 01:21:50,409
as fast as possible...

2179
01:21:50,410 --> 01:21:51,710
so that you can get the microphone with your left hand.

2180
01:21:51,980 --> 01:21:53,279
Show the first heel...

2181
01:21:53,280 --> 01:21:54,749
and take off the second heel fast.

2182
01:21:54,750 --> 01:21:56,119
(You think I don't know that?)

2183
01:21:56,120 --> 01:21:57,819
And don't stand in the front for too long.

2184
01:21:57,820 --> 01:21:59,519
Take one heel off, and move to the back.

2185
01:21:59,520 --> 01:22:02,390
I can't because they're still passing.

2186
01:22:03,720 --> 01:22:05,730
Oh, no. Hang on.

2187
01:22:05,830 --> 01:22:08,560
My feet are too sweaty to take them off.

2188
01:22:08,660 --> 01:22:09,660
I see.

2189
01:22:09,661 --> 01:22:11,899
There were some tiring parts.

2190
01:22:11,900 --> 01:22:13,200
I had to wear heels,

2191
01:22:13,400 --> 01:22:16,340
and we wasted a lot of time doing the lift.

2192
01:22:17,800 --> 01:22:19,809
(The outro lift is another tricky part.)

2193
01:22:19,810 --> 01:22:21,070
It looks funny because...

2194
01:22:21,540 --> 01:22:22,909
(It looks limp after pointing her toes.)

2195
01:22:22,910 --> 01:22:23,910
This is funny.

2196
01:22:23,911 --> 01:22:26,249
I want it to look stronger when you touch it.

2197
01:22:26,250 --> 01:22:27,579
I don't think...

2198
01:22:27,580 --> 01:22:29,219
the touching part should be intense.

2199
01:22:29,220 --> 01:22:30,749
This is the highlight.

2200
01:22:30,750 --> 01:22:32,650
- I can't see that.
- Why not?

2201
01:22:32,850 --> 01:22:34,449
Because we didn't do it properly...

2202
01:22:34,450 --> 01:22:35,859
or you just couldn't see it?

2203
01:22:35,860 --> 01:22:38,359
I played the artist,

2204
01:22:38,360 --> 01:22:39,889
so I couldn't...

2205
01:22:39,890 --> 01:22:42,560
look at the whole choreography from outside.

2206
01:22:42,730 --> 01:22:45,269
I had to be her eyes...

2207
01:22:45,270 --> 01:22:46,669
because she was playing the artist.

2208
01:22:46,670 --> 01:22:48,799
I tried to keep a cool head and didn't give up.

2209
01:22:48,800 --> 01:22:49,839
I told her,

2210
01:22:49,840 --> 01:22:51,740
"That doesn't look right. We have to go farther."

2211
01:22:52,270 --> 01:22:53,409
(Trying the intro...)

2212
01:22:53,410 --> 01:22:54,669
(where she hangs inside the fabric.)

2213
01:22:54,670 --> 01:22:56,740
I felt the limit in the intro.

2214
01:22:56,810 --> 01:22:59,649
I was upside down, and...

2215
01:22:59,650 --> 01:23:00,979
Good. Come down.

2216
01:23:00,980 --> 01:23:02,619
Their feet kept slipping because of the cloth,

2217
01:23:02,620 --> 01:23:05,150
so the three of them held me only with their arm strength.

2218
01:23:05,750 --> 01:23:07,549
This is full of risks.

2219
01:23:07,550 --> 01:23:08,889
Our performance is very risky.

2220
01:23:08,890 --> 01:23:11,189
It would have been fine if we were only using our bodies.

2221
01:23:11,190 --> 01:23:12,989
I'm concerned that we may not...

2222
01:23:12,990 --> 01:23:14,490
complete the perfect draft.

2223
01:23:15,560 --> 01:23:16,629
Get ready.

2224
01:23:16,630 --> 01:23:18,000
Set it up.

2225
01:23:18,370 --> 01:23:20,229
- Fog!
- Let's start.

2226
01:23:20,230 --> 01:23:21,299
All right, MIN JUN.

2227
01:23:21,300 --> 01:23:22,300
- Let's go!
- Let's go!

2228
01:23:22,300 --> 01:23:23,300
- Get set.
- All right.

2229
01:23:23,301 --> 01:23:24,439
In the intro,

2230
01:23:24,440 --> 01:23:26,140
we expressed a snake hanging on a tree.

2231
01:23:26,510 --> 01:23:29,010
There's moonlight and thick fog.

2232
01:23:29,210 --> 01:23:31,809
The first part is what sets the mood for the whole song,

2233
01:23:31,810 --> 01:23:33,450
so it's very important.

2234
01:23:33,680 --> 01:23:36,380
Kasper looked certain about the performance.

2235
01:23:36,480 --> 01:23:39,120
I decided to trust him since he was so sure.

2236
01:23:39,450 --> 01:23:41,419
MIN JUN tries hard to follow my lead,

2237
01:23:41,420 --> 01:23:43,420
and I also try hard to reflect his opinions.

2238
01:23:43,620 --> 01:23:45,129
- It looks good.
- I tried to be quick...

2239
01:23:45,130 --> 01:23:46,190
with the decisions.

2240
01:23:46,230 --> 01:23:47,289
Great work, guys.

2241
01:23:47,290 --> 01:23:48,359
- Good job.
- Great job.

2242
01:23:48,360 --> 01:23:50,060
I'm positive we'll win.

2243
01:23:50,930 --> 01:23:52,530
(Simeez and INGYOO take a long time to film.)

2244
01:23:52,730 --> 01:23:54,399
One, two...

2245
01:23:54,400 --> 01:23:56,069
(The microphone keeps getting in the way,)

2246
01:23:56,070 --> 01:23:58,540
(and there are mistakes with the props.)

2247
01:23:58,670 --> 01:23:59,869
I started getting worried...

2248
01:23:59,870 --> 01:24:01,780
that our goal was too ideal...

2249
01:24:01,840 --> 01:24:03,940
and that we might not be able to reach it.

2250
01:24:04,210 --> 01:24:06,380
It doesn't looks so pretty when it's sticking out.

2251
01:24:06,510 --> 01:24:08,420
I think you should be sitting on the fabric.

2252
01:24:08,680 --> 01:24:10,679
- Do you get what I mean?
- I knew that.

2253
01:24:10,680 --> 01:24:12,650
But I just went with it because it was dangerous.

2254
01:24:13,020 --> 01:24:14,590
Let's go with this one. Let's move on.

2255
01:24:14,750 --> 01:24:16,220
I don't think we have it yet.

2256
01:24:16,460 --> 01:24:18,730
To be honest, I didn't like any of it.

2257
01:24:19,860 --> 01:24:20,959
What is it that you want?

2258
01:24:20,960 --> 01:24:22,899
I'm still scared when I'm hanging upside down.

2259
01:24:22,900 --> 01:24:24,659
- That's true.
- From here...

2260
01:24:24,660 --> 01:24:26,969
I was exhausted and pressured,

2261
01:24:26,970 --> 01:24:29,200
so I started getting sensitive.

2262
01:24:29,900 --> 01:24:32,209
I didn't want to make it obvious,

2263
01:24:32,210 --> 01:24:35,179
but we both have our unique styles,

2264
01:24:35,180 --> 01:24:37,140
and they were too different.

2265
01:24:37,180 --> 01:24:38,379
I guess I kind of snapped...

2266
01:24:38,380 --> 01:24:40,550
because it felt too different all of a sudden.

2267
01:24:41,180 --> 01:24:42,379
I regretted it a bit.

2268
01:24:42,380 --> 01:24:44,519
Maybe I should have been more considerate.

2269
01:24:44,520 --> 01:24:46,189
She was dancing on heels...

2270
01:24:46,190 --> 01:24:48,320
for hours and showing her tenacity.

2271
01:24:48,460 --> 01:24:49,620
It was impressive.

2272
01:24:49,860 --> 01:24:50,959
Should we go again?

2273
01:24:50,960 --> 01:24:52,290
- Okay.
- Let's do it.

2274
01:24:52,360 --> 01:24:53,389
- We're almost there.
- Let's go!

2275
01:24:53,390 --> 01:24:54,960
- You've got this!
- Let's go!

2276
01:24:55,630 --> 01:24:57,430
Even though it was risky,

2277
01:24:57,600 --> 01:24:59,469
I wanted to show her...

2278
01:24:59,470 --> 01:25:02,270
how much we could help her achieve her dream.

2279
01:25:02,900 --> 01:25:05,169
It's totally perfect.

2280
01:25:05,170 --> 01:25:07,839
I was watching, and she eventually surprised me.

2281
01:25:07,840 --> 01:25:09,440
So, I thought, "This is it!"

2282
01:25:09,910 --> 01:25:10,910
That was the one.

2283
01:25:11,340 --> 01:25:12,509
Great work!

2284
01:25:12,510 --> 01:25:14,149
(Their shoot took 12 hours.)

2285
01:25:14,150 --> 01:25:16,180
I couldn't wait to see her perform...

2286
01:25:16,280 --> 01:25:18,890
the choreography that INGYOO and I created.

2287
01:25:18,990 --> 01:25:20,790
We have to win.

2288
01:25:21,350 --> 01:25:22,359
All right.

2289
01:25:22,360 --> 01:25:24,920
I don't think I've ever worked on a draft...

2290
01:25:25,960 --> 01:25:27,689
wishing so hard...

2291
01:25:27,690 --> 01:25:29,699
that they would pick ours.

2292
01:25:29,700 --> 01:25:34,130
(Desperate)

2293
01:25:35,270 --> 01:25:36,440
Hello.

2294
01:25:36,900 --> 01:25:38,769
(They have another meeting with TAEYONG.)

2295
01:25:38,770 --> 01:25:39,810
Hi.

2296
01:25:40,570 --> 01:25:42,280
(Giggling)

2297
01:25:42,440 --> 01:25:43,540
It's so awkward.

2298
01:25:44,240 --> 01:25:46,410
(Who's sitting next to him?)

2299
01:25:46,950 --> 01:25:50,920
(He's been in charge of NCT's numerous performances.)

2300
01:25:51,080 --> 01:25:52,389
(Choreographer Lee Il Hyeong has worked...)

2301
01:25:52,390 --> 01:25:53,750
(on numerous performances by TAEYONG.)

2302
01:25:54,020 --> 01:25:56,259
- Right?
- I expect it to be intense.

2303
01:25:56,260 --> 01:25:57,390
I know.

2304
01:25:58,420 --> 01:26:00,059
(The two teams will compete section by section.)

2305
01:26:00,060 --> 01:26:04,429
Winning in the chorus section is better for the choreographers...

2306
01:26:04,430 --> 01:26:07,070
because having to choreograph the chorus...

2307
01:26:07,300 --> 01:26:10,200
is easier to make their names known.

2308
01:26:10,370 --> 01:26:12,609
But I believe that a choreographer and a director are...

2309
01:26:12,610 --> 01:26:14,840
two different roles.

2310
01:26:15,010 --> 01:26:17,209
From a director's perspective,

2311
01:26:17,210 --> 01:26:19,049
it doesn't matter which section you get.

2312
01:26:19,050 --> 01:26:22,350
You should be able to make the artist shine whichever it is.

2313
01:26:22,580 --> 01:26:27,020
Also, the chorus isn't the only part that goes viral.

2314
01:26:27,150 --> 01:26:30,189
Whether it's the verse or the intro,

2315
01:26:30,190 --> 01:26:32,360
there's a possibility that it goes viral.

2316
01:26:32,430 --> 01:26:35,729
I honestly think that every section matters now.

2317
01:26:35,730 --> 01:26:37,559
But if I were the choreographer,

2318
01:26:37,560 --> 01:26:40,569
I would be prouder to know...

2319
01:26:40,570 --> 01:26:43,170
that I choreographed the chorus.

2320
01:26:43,400 --> 01:26:45,239
It would make me feel good.

2321
01:26:45,240 --> 01:26:47,110
(That's true.)

2322
01:26:47,170 --> 01:26:48,170
We're coming in.

2323
01:26:48,171 --> 01:26:50,310
- Hello.
- Hello.

2324
01:26:51,640 --> 01:26:52,879
- Hello.
- Hi.

2325
01:26:52,880 --> 01:26:54,850
- Hello.
- Hello.

2326
01:26:55,680 --> 01:26:58,119
As soon as I saw him, I wasn't even nervous.

2327
01:26:58,120 --> 01:27:00,520
I just thought it'd be fun. I was confident.

2328
01:27:01,120 --> 01:27:03,820
I reckoned that TAEYONG would prefer ours.

2329
01:27:04,560 --> 01:27:06,289
Today, we'll watch...

2330
01:27:06,290 --> 01:27:08,090
the draft videos of each team.

2331
01:27:08,190 --> 01:27:10,629
First, NaiN and BABYZOO.

2332
01:27:10,630 --> 01:27:11,630
Okay.

2333
01:27:11,631 --> 01:27:13,300
NaiN, I'll give them the proposal.

2334
01:27:13,970 --> 01:27:15,230
- It's...
- Here you go.

2335
01:27:15,400 --> 01:27:16,700
- Yes. This is ours.
- Thank you.

2336
01:27:17,100 --> 01:27:18,240
Look at all those words.

2337
01:27:18,540 --> 01:27:19,740
(Packed)

2338
01:27:19,840 --> 01:27:22,539
I thought that...

2339
01:27:22,540 --> 01:27:25,910
there was a bit too much written on the sheet.

2340
01:27:26,650 --> 01:27:27,909
- Hello!
- Hello!

2341
01:27:27,910 --> 01:27:28,979
I'm Choreographer NaiN.

2342
01:27:28,980 --> 01:27:30,619
I'm Choreographer BABYZOO.

2343
01:27:30,620 --> 01:27:32,250
(Full of expectation)

2344
01:27:32,790 --> 01:27:34,649
She was the choreographer...

2345
01:27:34,650 --> 01:27:36,289
in charge of TAEYONG.

2346
01:27:36,290 --> 01:27:39,159
She was on my mind...

2347
01:27:39,160 --> 01:27:40,689
as she knew what TAEYONG wanted.

2348
01:27:40,690 --> 01:27:43,159
I predicted the choreography...

2349
01:27:43,160 --> 01:27:44,599
to come out neat.

2350
01:27:44,600 --> 01:27:45,999
But this time,

2351
01:27:46,000 --> 01:27:48,970
being neat doesn't seem to suit the energy of the song.

2352
01:27:49,440 --> 01:27:52,409
We thought about the keyword of the song.

2353
01:27:52,410 --> 01:27:56,609
We wanted to focus on "top tier."

2354
01:27:56,610 --> 01:27:58,609
It isn't a competition with the others.

2355
01:27:58,610 --> 01:28:00,049
It's the feeling that others are trying to catch up.

2356
01:28:00,050 --> 01:28:01,649
We wanted to express...

2357
01:28:01,650 --> 01:28:04,379
being on another level.

2358
01:28:04,380 --> 01:28:05,419
We were on the same line.

2359
01:28:05,420 --> 01:28:06,919
NaiN's team emphasized superiority.

2360
01:28:06,920 --> 01:28:08,790
That was also our focus.

2361
01:28:09,320 --> 01:28:11,219
Instead of doing a long explanation,

2362
01:28:11,220 --> 01:28:13,130
we wanted to reveal the video right away.

2363
01:28:13,430 --> 01:28:15,559
We'll play the video first...

2364
01:28:15,560 --> 01:28:17,330
and explain afterward!

2365
01:28:18,230 --> 01:28:19,400
That's confidence!

2366
01:28:20,330 --> 01:28:22,170
(Team NaiN and BABYZOO's draft video gets revealed.)

2367
01:28:28,440 --> 01:28:29,839
The intro was disappointing.

2368
01:28:29,840 --> 01:28:32,049
I thought it would be a lot more eye-catching.

2369
01:28:32,050 --> 01:28:33,249
When the intro started,

2370
01:28:33,250 --> 01:28:35,680
I didn't feel a great impact.

2371
01:28:41,020 --> 01:28:44,259
For the intro chorus, we didn't follow the lyrics.

2372
01:28:44,260 --> 01:28:47,260
We made a new rhythm to make an impact.

2373
01:28:49,030 --> 01:28:51,099
I thought that the overall balance...

2374
01:28:51,100 --> 01:28:53,100
felt slightly feminine.

2375
01:28:58,040 --> 01:28:59,239
That's impressive.

2376
01:28:59,240 --> 01:29:01,639
We worked with the rap rhymes in Verse One...

2377
01:29:01,640 --> 01:29:04,409
and created key moves.

2378
01:29:04,410 --> 01:29:06,649
(Impressed)

2379
01:29:06,650 --> 01:29:08,749
It was a simple structure,

2380
01:29:08,750 --> 01:29:10,719
but they added wow points.

2381
01:29:10,720 --> 01:29:12,020
I was impressed by them.

2382
01:29:13,250 --> 01:29:14,250
We thought...

2383
01:29:14,251 --> 01:29:16,119
It was cool.

2384
01:29:16,120 --> 01:29:19,230
I like how the moves were expressed using the whole body.

2385
01:29:22,330 --> 01:29:23,799
The pre-chorus was disappointing.

2386
01:29:23,800 --> 01:29:25,359
The part felt...

2387
01:29:25,360 --> 01:29:27,900
less energetic than the other parts.

2388
01:29:34,610 --> 01:29:38,309
To express the song's strong vibes,

2389
01:29:38,310 --> 01:29:40,450
we put in the signature choreography.

2390
