2652
01:41:08,200 --> 01:41:10,870
(I wish for it to become a challenge.)

2653
01:41:11,140 --> 01:41:14,910
We had to fulfill the needs of the artist.

2654
01:41:20,350 --> 01:41:23,380
TAEYONG seemed to like the finger flick move.

2655
01:41:23,480 --> 01:41:24,680
It felt great.

2656
01:41:25,620 --> 01:41:29,620
"Would people really want to copy the finger flick move?"

2657
01:41:29,720 --> 01:41:31,260
This was what I thought.

2658
01:41:31,890 --> 01:41:34,459
As for the chorus,

2659
01:41:34,460 --> 01:41:37,429
we came up with the W hand gesture...

2660
01:41:37,430 --> 01:41:42,429
that represents "Wack."

2661
01:41:42,430 --> 01:41:44,739
It was obvious that this was a W...

2662
01:41:44,740 --> 01:41:46,640
even without an explanation.

2663
01:41:46,740 --> 01:41:48,739
There had to be an interesting part to it,

2664
01:41:48,740 --> 01:41:53,250
but I felt that it wasn't that charming.

2665
01:41:53,850 --> 01:41:56,720
The sense of something coming up with "Wack."

2666
01:41:57,050 --> 01:41:58,619
- "Wack."
- We used that feel...

2667
01:41:58,620 --> 01:42:00,549
to create the performance.

2668
01:42:00,550 --> 01:42:02,319
The last chorus...

2669
01:42:02,320 --> 01:42:05,460
is a big explosion. The whole stage is taken over.

2670
01:42:05,560 --> 01:42:08,189
The audience will be on the side instead of being underneath.

2671
01:42:08,190 --> 01:42:10,559
- The audience will join in...
- I see.

2672
01:42:10,560 --> 01:42:13,630
and the dancers will go up on the poles and do a headbang.

2673
01:42:13,730 --> 01:42:16,300
The energy on the stage.

2674
01:42:16,540 --> 01:42:17,799
(Laughing)

2675
01:42:17,800 --> 01:42:20,209
We focused a lot...

2676
01:42:20,210 --> 01:42:22,309
on how the artist would connect with the audience.

2677
01:42:22,310 --> 01:42:25,840
That part definitely stands out from the choreography.

2678
01:42:25,940 --> 01:42:28,549
TAEYONG wanted to make a good performance...

2679
01:42:28,550 --> 01:42:30,279
with the audience.

2680
01:42:30,280 --> 01:42:31,919
He wanted to show his excitement on stage.

2681
01:42:31,920 --> 01:42:33,590
It felt like he was going to prefer our performance.

2682
01:42:33,890 --> 01:42:36,359
The sound gets turned off toward the end.

2683
01:42:36,360 --> 01:42:38,119
- Right.
- The sounds are removed.

2684
01:42:38,120 --> 01:42:40,759
"Okay. I don't want to hear any sound."

2685
01:42:40,760 --> 01:42:43,360
"I want silence." We wanted to express this vibe.

2686
01:42:43,930 --> 01:42:45,700
As for the outfit,

2687
01:42:46,030 --> 01:42:49,270
there's a point move that uses quick steps.

2688
01:42:49,940 --> 01:42:52,969
To emphasize those steps,

2689
01:42:52,970 --> 01:42:55,069
we thought it was a great idea to use "Wacka Wak."

2690
01:42:55,070 --> 01:42:57,339
- Right.
- These are rhinestones.

2691
01:42:57,340 --> 01:43:01,150
We thought it would be great to go with this design.

2692
01:43:01,250 --> 01:43:04,080
These outfits were seen often.

2693
01:43:04,280 --> 01:43:07,349
The stage will look like this...

2694
01:43:07,350 --> 01:43:08,919
with the dancers.

2695
01:43:08,920 --> 01:43:10,819
"Wacka Wak..."

2696
01:43:10,820 --> 01:43:12,929
will constantly be shown through the LED display.

2697
01:43:12,930 --> 01:43:15,589
"Wacka Wak" will be the only thing they think about after it ends.

2698
01:43:15,590 --> 01:43:17,660
We tried to make everyone focus on TAEYONG only.

2699
01:43:18,130 --> 01:43:19,830
- Right.
- That's all from us!

2700
01:43:20,070 --> 01:43:21,770
- Thank you!
- Thank you!

2701
01:43:22,200 --> 01:43:24,139
- "Wacka Wak!"
- "Wacka Wak!"

2702
01:43:24,140 --> 01:43:25,599
("Wacka Wak!")

2703
01:43:25,600 --> 01:43:27,939
When we ended our presentation,

2704
01:43:27,940 --> 01:43:29,739
TAEYONG did this.

2705
01:43:29,740 --> 01:43:31,980
"Our W gesture..."

2706
01:43:32,080 --> 01:43:33,810
"must be stuck inside his head."

2707
01:43:34,510 --> 01:43:35,709
After seeing that,

2708
01:43:35,710 --> 01:43:37,479
I felt a rush of adrenaline.

2709
01:43:37,480 --> 01:43:40,390
I believe we have a great chance of winning.

2710
01:43:40,590 --> 01:43:44,419
TAEYONG really liked our V sign.

2711
01:43:44,420 --> 01:43:46,120
Doesn't that mean the game is over?

2712
01:43:46,220 --> 01:43:49,130
I strongly believe that he will choose our draft.

2713
01:43:49,960 --> 01:43:50,999
Hello.

2714
01:43:51,000 --> 01:43:53,299
We came today...

2715
01:43:53,300 --> 01:43:56,130
with a great sense of determination.

2716
01:43:56,470 --> 01:43:59,140
To be honest, I didn't have anything to worry about.

2717
01:43:59,370 --> 01:44:00,710
We're quite far away from each other.

2718
01:44:01,140 --> 01:44:02,739
I wanted to present it quickly.

2719
01:44:02,740 --> 01:44:04,939
We're talented in creating universes.

2720
01:44:04,940 --> 01:44:07,850
I felt confident about our performance.

2721
01:44:08,110 --> 01:44:09,379
"What did they come up with?"

2722
01:44:09,380 --> 01:44:10,479
I was certain that...

2723
01:44:10,480 --> 01:44:12,619
our performance would suit BAILEY more than theirs.

2724
01:44:12,620 --> 01:44:13,649
I was curious about theirs.

2725
01:44:13,650 --> 01:44:15,149
(Relaxed)

2726
01:44:15,150 --> 01:44:17,419
We didn't feel that much threat from them.

2727
01:44:17,420 --> 01:44:19,259
I wondered...

2728
01:44:19,260 --> 01:44:21,260
what they would say after seeing ours.

2729
01:44:22,360 --> 01:44:25,660
- Let's go!
- Hello!

2730
01:44:26,060 --> 01:44:28,270
- Hi! Hello!
- Hey!

2731
01:44:28,370 --> 01:44:31,199
Yo! Oh, my gosh!

2732
01:44:31,200 --> 01:44:32,839
Look at you guys! How are you doing?

2733
01:44:32,840 --> 01:44:34,439
It was tough for us.

2734
01:44:34,440 --> 01:44:36,239
You're the star.

2735
01:44:36,240 --> 01:44:37,680
I can't kill you guys.

2736
01:44:38,410 --> 01:44:40,209
- Okay.
- Okay.

2737
01:44:40,210 --> 01:44:41,779
Okay. As you guys know,

2738
01:44:41,780 --> 01:44:45,150
the draft videos will get revealed today.

2739
01:44:45,620 --> 01:44:48,019
And I'm really looking forward to them. Genuinely.

2740
01:44:48,020 --> 01:44:49,549
- Oh, my gosh!
- Gosh!

2741
01:44:49,550 --> 01:44:52,259
I did feel worried as we had to meet her expectations.

2742
01:44:52,260 --> 01:44:53,429
I was confident...

2743
01:44:53,430 --> 01:44:55,489
because I knew what her strengths were.

2744
01:44:55,490 --> 01:44:56,960
I came up with a tailor-made suit.

2745
01:44:57,600 --> 01:44:59,430
Team MIN JUN and Kasper...

2746
01:44:59,670 --> 01:45:01,269
- Good luck!
- will go first.

2747
01:45:01,270 --> 01:45:04,599
The video will be shown first instead of a long explanation.

2748
01:45:04,600 --> 01:45:08,139
We tried our best while thinking about...

2749
01:45:08,140 --> 01:45:10,740
your greatest strengths.

2750
01:45:11,610 --> 01:45:12,610
Thank you.

2751
01:45:12,611 --> 01:45:15,149
Won't Kasper and MIN JUN focus on the dancing?

2752
01:45:15,150 --> 01:45:18,079
Kasper isn't someone with great concepts.

2753
01:45:18,080 --> 01:45:19,819
I didn't know what to expect from MIN JUN,

2754
01:45:19,820 --> 01:45:21,589
but I knew Kasper's style of work.

2755
01:45:21,590 --> 01:45:23,260
I didn't expect something feminine from them.

2756
01:45:23,890 --> 01:45:26,160
(Team JEONG MIN JUN and Kasper's draft video gets revealed.)

2757
01:45:31,330 --> 01:45:32,430
What?

2758
01:45:32,560 --> 01:45:35,429
Kasper and I must've had similar ideas.

2759
01:45:35,430 --> 01:45:36,870
It's better for us as ours will stand out more.

2760
01:45:39,940 --> 01:45:40,970
The intro.

2761
01:45:42,410 --> 01:45:45,339
It was the first scene that started the mood of the song.

2762
01:45:45,340 --> 01:45:47,680
We focused on dreamlike vibes.

2763
01:45:50,820 --> 01:45:52,680
It's really similar to our part.

2764
01:45:54,520 --> 01:45:57,289
I came up with BAILEY's...

2765
01:45:57,290 --> 01:45:58,820
first signature move.

2766
01:45:59,360 --> 01:46:01,890
I think he knows my style.

2767
01:46:03,660 --> 01:46:05,859
There were many body control parts.

2768
01:46:05,860 --> 01:46:09,570
The repetitive parts felt nice.

2769
01:46:12,170 --> 01:46:13,509
For Chorus One,

2770
01:46:13,510 --> 01:46:16,140
we designed a solo part.

2771
01:46:16,240 --> 01:46:17,909
We came up with this part...

2772
01:46:17,910 --> 01:46:20,580
thinking that she was the only one who could pull this off.

2773
01:46:22,750 --> 01:46:24,379
It lacked impact.

2774
01:46:24,380 --> 01:46:26,350
Why a solo part out of nowhere?

2775
01:46:26,590 --> 01:46:29,149
The part felt too long...

2776
01:46:29,150 --> 01:46:31,160
and it made it feel empty.

2777
01:46:34,530 --> 01:46:37,700
Verse Two focuses on the lyrics.

2778
01:46:46,140 --> 01:46:48,409
I think the symmetry is really pretty.

2779
01:46:48,410 --> 01:46:51,080
And it kind of makes me feel the fullness of the song.

2780
01:46:52,980 --> 01:46:55,179
And for Pre-Chorus 2 and Chorus 2,

2781
01:46:55,180 --> 01:46:57,319
there's a rhythm-making part.

2782
01:46:57,320 --> 01:47:00,320
We wanted to make a catchy part that people would remember.

2783
01:47:04,620 --> 01:47:07,390
MIN JUN's parts looked similar.

2784
01:47:10,400 --> 01:47:13,170
I could see BAILEY...

2785
01:47:13,370 --> 01:47:14,530
with the choreography.

2786
01:47:16,170 --> 01:47:18,240
But with the overall flow...

2787
01:47:18,340 --> 01:47:20,009
It was a nonstop sequence of movements.

2788
01:47:20,010 --> 01:47:21,569
It was difficult to pinpoint...

2789
01:47:21,570 --> 01:47:23,380
a clear theme of the choreography.

2790
01:47:25,140 --> 01:47:27,609
I composed the bridge with a bit more feminine movements.

2791
01:47:27,610 --> 01:47:30,220
But I couldn't miss out on the musicality.

2792
01:47:32,920 --> 01:47:34,119
It's unfortunate.

2793
01:47:34,120 --> 01:47:35,649
As for both MIN JUN and Kasper,

2794
01:47:35,650 --> 01:47:37,789
they're not used to dancing with a feminine touch.

2795
01:47:37,790 --> 01:47:38,959
It seemed that...

2796
01:47:38,960 --> 01:47:40,489
they didn't have a good understanding of her style.

2797
01:47:40,490 --> 01:47:42,590
So their choreography left a lot to be desired.

2798
01:47:43,600 --> 01:47:46,159
The outro has a lot of bold beats.

2799
01:47:46,160 --> 01:47:47,430
I wanted them to be more explosive.

2800
01:47:50,500 --> 01:47:53,209
The choreography for the outro is broken down into small, quick moves.

2801
01:47:53,210 --> 01:47:55,770
There are many moments where things could just blow up.

2802
01:47:55,840 --> 01:47:56,910
That's crazy.

2803
01:48:03,380 --> 01:48:06,019
(You can watch their full video on "The CHOOM" and "Mnet Plus.")

2804
01:48:06,020 --> 01:48:07,320
(Giving them a round of applause)

2805
01:48:07,690 --> 01:48:08,990
(Glancing over)

2806
01:48:09,350 --> 01:48:10,719
I was like, "What's going on?"

2807
01:48:10,720 --> 01:48:11,989
It was hard to tell whether or not she liked it.

2808
01:48:11,990 --> 01:48:13,390
She's so good at keeping a poker face.

2809
01:48:13,460 --> 01:48:15,329
It was impossible to read her at all.

2810
01:48:15,330 --> 01:48:16,760
I thought it was an either-or situation.

2811
01:48:16,830 --> 01:48:18,460
She either loves it or hates it.

2812
01:48:18,500 --> 01:48:19,829
We had some similar moves.

2813
01:48:19,830 --> 01:48:21,430
It was bound to happen because of the lyrics.

2814
01:48:21,530 --> 01:48:24,039
They had a similar mood and flow.

2815
01:48:24,040 --> 01:48:26,069
But they didn't have a clear concept that left an impression.

2816
01:48:26,070 --> 01:48:27,909
Their performance was predictable.

2817
01:48:27,910 --> 01:48:29,610
Their performance primarily focused on dancing.

2818
01:48:29,670 --> 01:48:32,610
They didn't have any wow factor or impress us with the routine.

2819
01:48:32,640 --> 01:48:34,210
So I knew we had this in the bag.

2820
01:48:34,310 --> 01:48:35,410
Oh, my.

2821
01:48:35,650 --> 01:48:36,780
What did you think?

2822
01:48:36,820 --> 01:48:38,080
So much information.

2823
01:48:38,280 --> 01:48:39,319
(Nervous)

2824
01:48:39,320 --> 01:48:41,150
I'm definitely going to have to keep watching that.

2825
01:48:41,320 --> 01:48:43,990
Dissecting it and digging it a little bit.

2826
01:48:44,890 --> 01:48:45,959
Is this a good thing?

2827
01:48:45,960 --> 01:48:47,089
Or a bad thing?

2828
01:48:47,090 --> 01:48:48,329
I was worried.

2829
01:48:48,330 --> 01:48:50,129
She might be in a different mood.

2830
01:48:50,130 --> 01:48:51,700
And her style might be different too.

2831
01:48:51,730 --> 01:48:53,470
If she's going to keep watching that...

2832
01:48:54,000 --> 01:48:55,469
When she said she had to analyze it,

2833
01:48:55,470 --> 01:48:57,299
that feedback didn't sound positive.

2834
01:48:57,300 --> 01:48:59,439
It sounded more like she didn't know...

2835
01:48:59,440 --> 01:49:01,640
what kind of feedback she should give them.

2836
01:49:01,710 --> 01:49:02,839
First of all,

2837
01:49:02,840 --> 01:49:06,009
we only focused on your strength...

2838
01:49:06,010 --> 01:49:08,609
and came up with this choreography.

2839
01:49:08,610 --> 01:49:12,579
So we didn't want to bring in any of that diva energy because...

2840
01:49:12,580 --> 01:49:15,189
you can only pull off certain performances at a specific age.

2841
01:49:15,190 --> 01:49:16,820
I thought he had it completely wrong.

2842
01:49:16,890 --> 01:49:18,859
Every female artist has a fantasy...

2843
01:49:18,860 --> 01:49:20,189
of becoming a diva on stage.

2844
01:49:20,190 --> 01:49:21,289
He was completely off here.

2845
01:49:21,290 --> 01:49:23,459
I thought this was the moment that decided the outcome.

2846
01:49:23,460 --> 01:49:24,760
I didn't think that...

2847
01:49:24,830 --> 01:49:27,029
she could embody the queen vibe.

2848
01:49:27,030 --> 01:49:28,469
She's too young to pull that off.

2849
01:49:28,470 --> 01:49:30,699
I wanted to show the world...

2850
01:49:30,700 --> 01:49:32,970
who she was with this choreography.

2851
01:49:33,070 --> 01:49:35,739
The performance keyword we conveyed...

2852
01:49:35,740 --> 01:49:37,309
with our routine was...

2853
01:49:37,310 --> 01:49:39,409
the albino snake.

2854
01:49:39,410 --> 01:49:40,609
Albino snakes are...

2855
01:49:40,610 --> 01:49:42,079
different from other snakes.

2856
01:49:42,080 --> 01:49:43,549
But being different doesn't mean...

2857
01:49:43,550 --> 01:49:44,579
there's something wrong with them.

2858
01:49:44,580 --> 01:49:47,949
We wanted to convey that this difference was special

2859
01:49:47,950 --> 01:49:50,219
In the intro, you're hanging upside down from a tree.

2860
01:49:50,220 --> 01:49:52,059
I tried to picture you as an albino snake...

2861
01:49:52,060 --> 01:49:53,890
when I composed the intro.

2862
01:49:53,930 --> 01:49:54,959
In Verse One,

2863
01:49:54,960 --> 01:49:57,259
the dark energy is pulling you in.

2864
01:49:57,260 --> 01:49:58,459
"I don't care."

2865
01:49:58,460 --> 01:50:00,869
You're facing a lot of hardships, but they don't get to you.

2866
01:50:00,870 --> 01:50:02,930
That's what I had in mind for this part.

2867
01:50:03,000 --> 01:50:04,569
For Pre-Chorus One,

2868
01:50:04,570 --> 01:50:07,070
you're known for your hand gestures.

2869
01:50:07,910 --> 01:50:09,979
I really loved this part.

2870
01:50:09,980 --> 01:50:11,710
Really? Thank you.

2871
01:50:11,810 --> 01:50:13,449
Hearing such comments makes me so happy.

2872
01:50:13,450 --> 01:50:16,309
I came up with a move that could represent her style.

2873
01:50:16,310 --> 01:50:18,119
And she said she really liked that.

2874
01:50:18,120 --> 01:50:20,289
I could tell that he spent a lot of time analyzing her style.

2875
01:50:20,290 --> 01:50:22,820
He practically tailored this choreography for her.

2876
01:50:22,920 --> 01:50:24,419
There were a few parts...

2877
01:50:24,420 --> 01:50:26,119
where he added hand gestures...

2878
01:50:26,120 --> 01:50:27,629
BAILEY would be satisfied with.

2879
01:50:27,630 --> 01:50:30,029
But I need to take a closer look to see if they made sense...

2880
01:50:30,030 --> 01:50:31,499
with the story and the overall choreography.

2881
01:50:31,500 --> 01:50:33,669
And it was just a nonstop sequence of movements for the rest.

2882
01:50:33,670 --> 01:50:35,269
"I'm so good."

2883
01:50:35,270 --> 01:50:36,699
When you're showing off with 40 consecutive moves,

2884
01:50:36,700 --> 01:50:37,700
people get sick of it.

2885
01:50:37,740 --> 01:50:39,569
When the song flows into the outro,

2886
01:50:39,570 --> 01:50:41,809
this is where you're going to blow it up.

2887
01:50:41,810 --> 01:50:44,739
We came up with the sequence that was perfect for the ending.

2888
01:50:44,740 --> 01:50:46,009
You're declaring victory...

2889
01:50:46,010 --> 01:50:47,079
or telling people you'll win.

2890
01:50:47,080 --> 01:50:48,609
We focused on "You can't kill me."

2891
01:50:48,610 --> 01:50:50,249
This concept aligns with the move of shooting a gun with eyes covered.

2892
01:50:50,250 --> 01:50:52,419
We wanted to convey that vibe.

2893
01:50:52,420 --> 01:50:53,490
That's quite deep.

2894
01:50:54,390 --> 01:50:55,520
The whole story is deep.

2895
01:50:55,550 --> 01:50:57,490
I think it is important.

2896
01:50:57,520 --> 01:51:01,389
I think killing parts having moments that are memorable are important...

2897
01:51:01,390 --> 01:51:02,660
with the right intention.

2898
01:51:02,760 --> 01:51:05,159
I think a lot of times now it's very...

2899
01:51:05,160 --> 01:51:08,130
We think we have to do something to get people going.

2900
01:51:08,170 --> 01:51:09,699
You know? But if it's unnatural,

2901
01:51:09,700 --> 01:51:12,939
I feel like I can feel that just as a creative person.

2902
01:51:12,940 --> 01:51:14,469
None of it feels forced, though.

2903
01:51:14,470 --> 01:51:15,910
Which I really appreciate here.

2904
01:51:16,110 --> 01:51:17,340
I was relieved.

2905
01:51:17,440 --> 01:51:18,840
I was anxious.

2906
01:51:18,940 --> 01:51:21,380
I think in the very beginning...

2907
01:51:21,410 --> 01:51:22,950
with this tree situation...

2908
01:51:22,980 --> 01:51:25,019
It just automatically wowed me.

2909
01:51:25,020 --> 01:51:27,650
Right from the beginning... "Oh, my gosh. What am I looking at?"

2910
01:51:28,120 --> 01:51:30,360
I think that's definitely a big memorable part.

2911
01:51:30,420 --> 01:51:32,090
It was just as I thought.

2912
01:51:32,120 --> 01:51:34,629
We did give her something she really loved.

2913
01:51:34,630 --> 01:51:36,589
It's like we crafted a tailored suit for BAILEY.

2914
01:51:36,590 --> 01:51:38,560
We whipped up something she'd love and served it to her.

2915
01:51:38,760 --> 01:51:42,129
Satisfying BAILEY's needs as an artist?

2916
01:51:42,130 --> 01:51:43,439
That's a given.

2917
01:51:43,440 --> 01:51:44,569
We need to go a step beyond that...

2918
01:51:44,570 --> 01:51:46,040
and level it up.

2919
01:51:46,440 --> 01:51:48,809
Let's go, Team B.

2920
01:51:48,810 --> 01:51:50,280
- Team B.
- What's up, B?

2921
01:51:50,380 --> 01:51:51,439
How are you doing?

2922
01:51:51,440 --> 01:51:54,409
I'm curious to see what the performance director...

2923
01:51:54,410 --> 01:51:55,679
of Jennie and IVE can do.

2924
01:51:55,680 --> 01:51:57,479
I think they might have come up...

2925
01:51:57,480 --> 01:51:59,050
with a similar concept.

2926
01:51:59,080 --> 01:52:00,249
Okay. Hold on.

2927
01:52:00,250 --> 01:52:01,590
The concept is about...

2928
01:52:02,150 --> 01:52:05,460
Hydra Queen.

2929
01:52:08,260 --> 01:52:09,460
(Silent)

2930
01:52:09,690 --> 01:52:11,760
What's this? Is he feeling okay?

2931
01:52:11,860 --> 01:52:13,200
Hold on. Did I mess this up?

2932
01:52:13,530 --> 01:52:15,430
Gosh. This isn't what we expected. Something was off.

2933
01:52:15,570 --> 01:52:16,969
- Do you know Hydra?
- Hydra?

2934
01:52:16,970 --> 01:52:19,199
Yes. Hydra is...

2935
01:52:19,200 --> 01:52:21,409
like a monster.

2936
01:52:21,410 --> 01:52:22,439
(A monster?)

2937
01:52:22,440 --> 01:52:23,739
A monster?

2938
01:52:23,740 --> 01:52:25,040
Did I hear that right?

2939
01:52:25,140 --> 01:52:26,309
Do you have pictures?

2940
01:52:26,310 --> 01:52:27,649
There. Boom.

2941
01:52:27,650 --> 01:52:28,680
Here you go.

2942
01:52:29,950 --> 01:52:31,249
Those were some grotesque-looking pictures.

2943
01:52:31,250 --> 01:52:32,820
He wants BAILEY to execute this concept?

2944
01:52:32,880 --> 01:52:34,919
There's a thin line between looking creepy...

2945
01:52:34,920 --> 01:52:36,049
and looking cool.

2946
01:52:36,050 --> 01:52:37,320
And it looked creepy.

2947
01:52:37,690 --> 01:52:38,919
Let me explain what she can do.

2948
01:52:38,920 --> 01:52:40,229
Even when her neck gets sliced,

2949
01:52:40,230 --> 01:52:41,259
it regenerates.

2950
01:52:41,260 --> 01:52:42,389
- I see. Okay.
- Yes.

2951
01:52:42,390 --> 01:52:43,729
The more she gets killed,

2952
01:52:43,730 --> 01:52:45,400
the stronger she becomes.

2953
01:52:46,100 --> 01:52:48,169
Let me explain how we came up with this concept.

2954
01:52:48,170 --> 01:52:50,869
If we were to measure...

2955
01:52:50,870 --> 01:52:53,139
the combat power of your dance,

2956
01:52:53,140 --> 01:52:54,940
this would happen.

2957
01:52:55,340 --> 01:52:56,470
So...

2958
01:52:57,210 --> 01:52:58,779
- What was that?
- She's already...

2959
01:52:58,780 --> 01:52:59,979
Did you prepare that?

2960
01:52:59,980 --> 01:53:01,480
(She fails to hold back her laughter.)

2961
01:53:01,610 --> 01:53:03,209
- What was that?
- She's already...

2962
01:53:03,210 --> 01:53:04,249
Did you prepare that?

2963
01:53:04,250 --> 01:53:05,380
No.

2964
01:53:05,680 --> 01:53:07,490
(Laughing)

2965
01:53:07,520 --> 01:53:09,390
It was embarrassing to watch him present.

2966
01:53:09,420 --> 01:53:10,890
I wanted to hide.

2967
01:53:11,390 --> 01:53:12,620
She's already a queen.

2968
01:53:13,190 --> 01:53:14,290
She's...

2969
01:53:14,360 --> 01:53:16,730
She's already Hydra Queen.

2970
01:53:17,430 --> 01:53:18,729
You know what it is, right?

2971
01:53:18,730 --> 01:53:20,769
- It's Son Goku's glasses.
- Gosh, he's just crazy.

2972
01:53:20,770 --> 01:53:21,799
Why is he so funny?

2973
01:53:21,800 --> 01:53:23,330
Yes. I know what you're saying.

2974
01:53:23,470 --> 01:53:24,539
I guess I won her over...

2975
01:53:24,540 --> 01:53:26,170
when I ambushed her with my little joke.

2976
01:53:26,440 --> 01:53:27,969
Actually, I wasn't trying to be funny.

2977
01:53:27,970 --> 01:53:29,969
I wanted to convey my concept.

2978
01:53:29,970 --> 01:53:31,279
But she liked it.

2979
01:53:31,280 --> 01:53:32,379
It didn't matter whether she laughed...

2980
01:53:32,380 --> 01:53:33,479
because she liked it or she found it ridiculous.

2981
01:53:33,480 --> 01:53:34,809
Laughing is good.

2982
01:53:34,810 --> 01:53:36,680
When we laugh, it puts us in a good mood.

2983
01:53:36,810 --> 01:53:37,950
Okay. Next.

2984
01:53:38,420 --> 01:53:39,649
We went with high heels.

2985
01:53:39,650 --> 01:53:40,819
With these heels...

2986
01:53:40,820 --> 01:53:42,189
and these styling elements,

2987
01:53:42,190 --> 01:53:43,559
we wanted to depict non-human aspects.

2988
01:53:43,560 --> 01:53:45,019
Bones are protruding out here.

2989
01:53:45,020 --> 01:53:48,289
We wanted to give you an outfit where it made you look combat ready.

2990
01:53:48,290 --> 01:53:50,899
So you're a queen in combat mode.

2991
01:53:50,900 --> 01:53:51,900
You know what I'm saying?

2992
01:53:52,000 --> 01:53:53,000
Let's go to the next slide.

2993
01:53:53,001 --> 01:53:54,070
(That's it.)

2994
01:53:54,200 --> 01:53:55,329
(Clapping)

2995
01:53:55,330 --> 01:53:57,499
Our presentation is compact.

2996
01:53:57,500 --> 01:53:58,870
What's he saying?

2997
01:53:58,940 --> 01:54:00,540
He moved on super fast.

2998
01:54:00,610 --> 01:54:02,769
"We want you to be a queen for our concept."

2999
01:54:02,770 --> 01:54:04,579
But anyone could've come up with that.

3000
01:54:04,580 --> 01:54:07,349
Their approach to this project...

3001
01:54:07,350 --> 01:54:09,650
felt predictable to me.

3002
01:54:10,010 --> 01:54:12,179
- Must we explain more?
- No.

3003
01:54:12,180 --> 01:54:13,689
Let's begin. Boom.

3004
01:54:13,690 --> 01:54:15,549
(Simeez and INGYOO reveal their performance video.)

3005
01:54:15,550 --> 01:54:17,190
(Curious)

3006
01:54:22,760 --> 01:54:25,499
The chance of having an identical sequence for the intro...

3007
01:54:25,500 --> 01:54:27,129
would be one in a million.

3008
01:54:27,130 --> 01:54:28,769
It was identical. I thought that was crazy.

3009
01:54:28,770 --> 01:54:30,569
What was crazier was that they were holding her up in the same pose.

3010
01:54:30,570 --> 01:54:32,440
I could tell that they were determined to win too.

3011
01:54:32,700 --> 01:54:35,239
It crossed my mind that we might end up with some same moves.

3012
01:54:35,240 --> 01:54:37,579
They must've thought that it was a groundbreaking move.

3013
01:54:37,580 --> 01:54:38,880
But it wasn't.

3014
01:54:44,220 --> 01:54:46,119
We were going for the imagery...

3015
01:54:46,120 --> 01:54:48,019
of a cocoon, wrapped in silk, for the intro.

3016
01:54:48,020 --> 01:54:51,120
We wanted to build suspense before the birth of a monster.

3017
01:54:51,920 --> 01:54:53,729
I wish the red wrap was prettier...

3018
01:54:53,730 --> 01:54:55,189
and stood out a little more.

3019
01:54:55,190 --> 01:54:56,430
It didn't look good at all.

3020
01:54:56,690 --> 01:54:58,200
So many thoughts.

3021
01:54:59,760 --> 01:55:01,199
He's going to hold the microphone like that?

3022
01:55:01,200 --> 01:55:03,770
That's something an amateur would come up with.

3023
01:55:04,840 --> 01:55:07,669
In Pre-Chorus One, we wanted to show the awakening...

3024
01:55:07,670 --> 01:55:09,869
of Hydra Queen, born as a completely different creature.

3025
01:55:09,870 --> 01:55:12,640
In the lyrics, the word, "gun," really stood out.

3026
01:55:16,450 --> 01:55:18,319
"You can't kill me."

3027
01:55:18,320 --> 01:55:21,190
To express that, she has to show her combativeness.

3028
01:55:21,290 --> 01:55:23,449
It's dark and a bit grotesque.

3029
01:55:23,450 --> 01:55:27,030
But it also has a feminine aspect with an alluring edge.

3030
01:55:28,660 --> 01:55:31,200
Just the color... It sticks so well.

3031
01:55:33,400 --> 01:55:35,599
For Verse Two, we wanted to stay on the beat...

3032
01:55:35,600 --> 01:55:38,200
and incorporate high heels into our routine.

3033
01:55:40,670 --> 01:55:42,369
The heels didn't look like an integral element.

3034
01:55:42,370 --> 01:55:44,840
It just looked like she was dancing in heels.

3035
01:55:45,210 --> 01:55:47,379
She wore heels. Then we should've been impressed...

3036
01:55:47,380 --> 01:55:48,409
by her routine.

3037
01:55:48,410 --> 01:55:50,110
But she was just a dancer in heels.

3038
01:55:55,450 --> 01:55:58,159
When she takes off the high heels in Pre-Chorus Two,

3039
01:55:58,160 --> 01:55:59,589
she breaks away from everything...

3040
01:55:59,590 --> 01:56:00,730
and turns into a monster.

3041
01:56:06,060 --> 01:56:07,999
We wanted to show that...

3042
01:56:08,000 --> 01:56:10,369
everyone has surrendered to her as she's the queen.

3043
01:56:10,370 --> 01:56:12,200
That was the storyline of our routine.

3044
01:56:12,500 --> 01:56:13,570
It's really cool.

3045
01:56:16,310 --> 01:56:18,379
Once the choreography comes together,

3046
01:56:18,380 --> 01:56:19,880
the synergy would blow up.

3047
01:56:22,750 --> 01:56:24,949
The real battle starts now. She's in combat mode.

3048
01:56:24,950 --> 01:56:26,050
- Combat mode.
- Okay.

3049
01:56:29,590 --> 01:56:30,659
Krump?

3050
01:56:30,660 --> 01:56:33,320
Krump isn't her thing.

3051
01:56:34,760 --> 01:56:37,099
He wants a female artist to krump barefoot?

3052
01:56:37,100 --> 01:56:38,130
On stage?

3053
01:56:38,900 --> 01:56:41,629
I thought she would be the only artist...

3054
01:56:41,630 --> 01:56:43,740
who could pull off krumping in a solo dance break.

3055
01:56:44,800 --> 01:56:46,699
The next part was really important..

3056
01:56:46,700 --> 01:56:48,869
So many things are happening in the outro. We went with a lift.

3057
01:56:48,870 --> 01:56:51,310
Everything would just blow up at the end.

3058
01:56:51,980 --> 01:56:53,280
(Impressed)

3059
01:56:55,150 --> 01:56:56,849
We tried to convey the combativeness...

3060
01:56:56,850 --> 01:56:59,420
and energy of the queen the best we could.

3061
01:57:00,650 --> 01:57:02,389
I thought all those micro-movements...

3062
01:57:02,390 --> 01:57:04,389
breaking down the beats...

3063
01:57:04,390 --> 01:57:05,520
were messy.

3064
01:57:10,460 --> 01:57:12,229
(You can watch their full video on "The CHOOM" and "Mnet Plus.")

3065
01:57:12,230 --> 01:57:13,770
Oh, my gosh.

3066
01:57:14,170 --> 01:57:15,229
Check out the look on her face.

3067
01:57:15,230 --> 01:57:16,600
It was no joke.

3068
01:57:18,700 --> 01:57:19,769
I did see them as a threat.

3069
01:57:19,770 --> 01:57:21,739
They used the red wrap, gloves,

3070
01:57:21,740 --> 01:57:23,310
and heels in their routine.

3071
01:57:23,370 --> 01:57:24,609
Their visual taste is spot on.

3072
01:57:24,610 --> 01:57:27,209
But they lacked any real choreography.

3073
01:57:27,210 --> 01:57:29,350
I thought it was just lame.

3074
01:57:29,580 --> 01:57:31,250
Simeez's use of the red wrap...

3075
01:57:31,520 --> 01:57:33,320
She's already done something similar at a showcase.

3076
01:57:34,790 --> 01:57:37,189
I thought everything was excessive.

3077
01:57:37,190 --> 01:57:39,019
The styling was too much. Hair and makeup were too much.

3078
01:57:39,020 --> 01:57:40,589
The concept was too much. And the choreography too.

3079
01:57:40,590 --> 01:57:43,390
The way she took off her heels looked silly.

3080
01:57:43,560 --> 01:57:47,269
There are so many techniques BAILEY can do with heels.

3081
01:57:47,270 --> 01:57:49,670
But she mostly gave BAILEY basic moves.

3082
01:57:49,830 --> 01:57:51,839
I was worried that it might offend BAILEY.

3083
01:57:51,840 --> 01:57:54,170
"This is all you can do with my skillset?"

3084
01:57:54,340 --> 01:57:57,309
We set Hydra Queen as our motif.

3085
01:57:57,310 --> 01:57:59,010
"Can't kill me." She can't be killed.

3086
01:57:59,240 --> 01:58:01,709
As for the intro, we had the same sequence.

3087
01:58:01,710 --> 01:58:05,050
It was identical. I was pretty shocked too.

3088
01:58:05,580 --> 01:58:08,219
In the intro, four dancers hold the red wrap...

3089
01:58:08,220 --> 01:58:09,890
and pull it down.

3090
01:58:10,620 --> 01:58:12,360
And it creates a visually striking scene...

3091
01:58:12,590 --> 01:58:15,030
and brings focus to Hydra Queen.

3092
01:58:16,030 --> 01:58:19,130
You'll rip it and come out at "started."

3093
01:58:19,260 --> 01:58:22,200
Before that part, I won't have a microphone with me?

3094
01:58:22,300 --> 01:58:23,870
The dancers are going to carry it.

3095
01:58:24,900 --> 01:58:27,139
We can definitely develop more regarding the microphone.

3096
01:58:27,140 --> 01:58:28,770
- There's a lot to develop.
- Yes.

3097
01:58:28,840 --> 01:58:30,840
I was quite shocked because it was really bad.

3098
01:58:31,080 --> 01:58:33,380
It looked silly to have a microphone here.

3099
01:58:33,610 --> 01:58:37,250
I get that the dancer is going to move the microphone.

3100
01:58:37,420 --> 01:58:38,550
But it doesn't look cool.

3101
01:58:38,780 --> 01:58:40,379
We were able to deliver the microphone to her.

3102
01:58:40,380 --> 01:58:41,790
It was done with precision and complete accuracy.

3103
01:58:41,920 --> 01:58:43,150
I thought it was irresponsible.

3104
01:58:43,650 --> 01:58:45,590
There's something I'm a little concerned about.

3105
01:58:45,820 --> 01:58:48,459
I'm afraid I might look like a fish.

3106
01:58:48,460 --> 01:58:50,060
Too much like a fish.

3107
01:58:50,460 --> 01:58:52,529
- Oh, that.
- Like a fish.

3108
01:58:52,530 --> 01:58:53,530
Don't worry about that.

3109
01:58:53,531 --> 01:58:55,529
We can only pick out cool-looking ones.

3110
01:58:55,530 --> 01:58:56,969
We can pick out only the good ones...

3111
01:58:56,970 --> 01:58:58,440
- and narrow them down.
- Okay.

3112
01:58:59,170 --> 01:59:00,240
Don't worry.

3113
01:59:00,470 --> 01:59:03,010
Even she thought it was pretty lame.

3114
01:59:03,110 --> 01:59:05,180
"Do I really have to do that? Do I have to become a fish?"

3115
01:59:05,340 --> 01:59:07,909
She'll have to compromise her looks for this choreography.

3116
01:59:07,910 --> 01:59:09,510
Is this worth her trouble?

3117
01:59:09,580 --> 01:59:10,780
I don't think it is.

3118
01:59:10,850 --> 01:59:12,779
This wasn't a one-time thing, was it?

3119
01:59:12,780 --> 01:59:14,150
I thought she was going to use this for every performance.

3120
01:59:14,190 --> 01:59:16,320
I just didn't understand where their confidence came from.

3121
01:59:16,620 --> 01:59:18,189
You'll ditch the heels. Actually,

3122
01:59:18,190 --> 01:59:20,490
- you can freestyle here.
- Yes.

3123
01:59:21,430 --> 01:59:22,829
Unlike any other artists,

3124
01:59:22,830 --> 01:59:24,900
you can fully freestyle on stage.

3125
01:59:25,100 --> 01:59:26,129
My gosh.

3126
01:59:26,130 --> 01:59:28,199
When I heard that they wanted her to freestyle for the second chorus,

3127
01:59:28,200 --> 01:59:29,970
I gave up trying to understand their concept.

3128
01:59:30,100 --> 01:59:32,039
They're just leaving everything up to her.

3129
01:59:32,040 --> 01:59:34,439
She's going to take that risk and perform this song on stage?

3130
01:59:34,440 --> 01:59:36,370
I don't think that's possible.

3131
01:59:36,510 --> 01:59:39,179
After hearing everything, I can see it super clear...

3132
01:59:39,180 --> 01:59:40,809
even with stage things.

3133
01:59:40,810 --> 01:59:43,250
I think that the use of heels is very memorable...

3134
01:59:44,280 --> 01:59:47,849
because at least from a non-dancer's point of view...

3135
01:59:47,850 --> 01:59:49,289
"Oh, that's like that heel thing."

3136
01:59:49,290 --> 01:59:51,160
You can kind of click that with something.

3137
01:59:51,690 --> 01:59:54,390
I think those little moments are a really strong part of me.

3138
01:59:54,490 --> 01:59:56,459
It feels like maybe, there's a little bit...

3139
01:59:56,460 --> 01:59:58,659
more room that we can go with that.

3140
01:59:58,660 --> 02:00:00,799
Is it going to turn into a gun? Or it is going to...

3141
02:00:00,800 --> 02:00:03,030
I feel like we can use a little bit more.

3142
02:00:03,230 --> 02:00:05,940
I got the feeling that she focused a lot on the heels.

3143
02:00:06,040 --> 02:00:08,139
I thought we were going in the right direction.

3144
02:00:08,140 --> 02:00:10,509
Her feedback sounded like she was planning...

3145
02:00:10,510 --> 02:00:11,940
to perform this choreography.

3146
02:00:12,910 --> 02:00:15,180
Okay. Well, I have a lot of thinking to do.

3147
02:00:15,310 --> 02:00:17,419
But I think I genuinely want to thank you...

3148
02:00:17,420 --> 02:00:18,880
for making it this difficult for me.

3149
02:00:19,350 --> 02:00:20,789
So I will...

3150
02:00:20,790 --> 02:00:21,849
(She has a lot on her mind.)

3151
02:00:21,850 --> 02:00:23,390
work things through.

3152
02:00:24,860 --> 02:00:27,330
Really. Truly. Thank you so much. I'll see you guys at the rehearsal.

3153
02:00:27,490 --> 02:00:28,490
Thank you.

3154
02:00:29,690 --> 02:00:31,359
- I feel confident.
- It looked like..

3155
02:00:31,360 --> 02:00:33,700
she wanted to dance in heels.

3156
02:00:33,760 --> 02:00:35,329
For a female artist to krump, it's a new challenge.

3157
02:00:35,330 --> 02:00:37,129
So I was certain she would love...

3158
02:00:37,130 --> 02:00:38,900
these groundbreaking elements.

3159
02:00:39,100 --> 02:00:40,939
They completely lacked in character understanding.

3160
02:00:40,940 --> 02:00:44,079
Let's say I bought a product. And I fully read the manual.

3161
02:00:44,080 --> 02:00:45,739
But they didn't.

3162
02:00:45,740 --> 02:00:47,509
I know...

3163
02:00:47,510 --> 02:00:49,849
how to maximize the use of this iPhone.

3164
02:00:49,850 --> 02:00:50,850
But they're clueless.

3165
02:00:50,851 --> 02:00:52,580
They only use it to make calls and watch YouTube.

3166
02:00:52,850 --> 02:00:55,250
